INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112840','Multiphysics analysis of hydrogen kinetics and their effects in UZrHx-fueled reactors','UZrHx 핵연료 원자로에서 수소 거동 동역학 및 그 영향에 대한 다중물리 해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Shixin Lin; Youqi Zheng; Xianan Du; Hongchun Wu','2026-09-13','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Hydrogen kinetics within the Uranium–zirconium hydride (UZrH x ) fuel, including redistribution, dissociation, and permeation loss, can alter local moderating capability and material properties, thereby affecting core neutronics and safety characteristics. In this work, a hydrogen kinetics model was developed and integrated into the deterministic code system SARAX to establish a coupled neutronic-thermal-hydrogen kinetics analysis tool. Hydrogen redistribution, dissociation, and permeation loss were simulated at the whole-core scale over the full reactor lifetime and their effects on neutron science and thermal parameters were quantitatively evaluated. The results show that temperature gradients drive pronounced hydrogen migration from hotter regions to colder regions, leading to a nonuniform hydrogen distribution and a corresponding change in local moderating capability. Axial hydrogen redistribution shifts the axial power profile toward the lower core region with higher hydrogen concentration. Radial redistribution increases the H/Zr ratio at the outer solid–gas interface of the fuel pellet, thereby increasing the local equilibrium hydrogen pressure and promoting subsequent permeation loss. The core-averaged H/Zr ratio decreases nearly linearly from 1.6 to 1.5763 by the end of life, while the minimum local H/Zr ratio remains within the δ-ZrH x phase field under the corresponding temperature condition. Axial hydrogen redistribution alone increases k eff by approximately 49 pcm, whereas hydrogen permeation loss decreases k eff by approximately 489 pcm. Under their combined effects, k eff decreases by approximately 447 pcm over the reactor lifetime. The present results provide a computational basis for the design and safety evaluation of UZrH x -fueled microreactors.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926007280','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112840',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112818','On the asymmetric grid-to-rod fretting wear of PWR fuel rods induced by nonlinear vibration','비선형 진동에 의한 PWR 핵연료봉의 비대칭 지지격자-연료봉 프레팅 마모','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Shuo Ma; Peng Li; Heng Huang; Junzhe Cui; Jinming Li','2026-09-13','','2027-02','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926007061','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112818',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104671','Integration method for determining the potential alpha energy concentration of radon and thoron decay products in air','공기 중 라돈 및 토론 붕괴생성물의 잠재 알파에너지 농도 결정을 위한 적분법','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Agata Grygier; Krystian Skubacz; Stanisław Chałupnik','2026-09-13','','2027-02','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005590','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104671',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106608','Dynamic modeling and simulation of supercritical carbon dioxide recompression Brayton cycle energy converter coupled with a 400MWth natural circulation lead-cooled reactor','400 MWth 자연순환 납냉각 원자로와 연계된 초임계 이산화탄소 재압축 브레이튼 사이클 에너지 변환기의 동적 모델링 및 모의','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Zongyun Wu; Tiancai Liu','2026-09-13','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','The natural circulation lead-cooled fast reactor (NCLFR) possesses excellent neutron economy, thermal safety characteristics, and application potential. Meanwhile, the supercritical carbon dioxide recompression closed Brayton cycle (s-CO 2 -RCBC) has the merits of high thermal energy conversion efficiency, system compactness, environmental friendliness, safety, and notable economic benefits. Coupling the NCLFR with s-CO 2 -RCBC can integrate the advantages of both, representing a key development direction for future advanced clean-energy nuclear energy systems. However, the unique thermophysical properties of supercritical carbon dioxide, the complexity of the recompression Brayton cycle, and the intricate coupling with the NCLFR render the transient behavior and control strategies of the entire system highly complex. This paper establishes a dynamic model for a 400MW th small lead-cooled fast reactor coupled with a supercritical carbon dioxide conversion Brayton cycle system based on the reactor transient simulation code RESYS, and a control system for reactor power and s-CO 2 -RCBC system was established. The component model and closed-cycle dynamic model of the s-CO 2 -RCBC were validated using literature reference data. Subsequently, a detailed analysis is conducted on both the steady-state and transient operational characteristics of the integrated system. Firstly, the steady-state simulation is conducted to validate the precision of the integrated system model and serve as the initial condition for the transient simulation. Thereafter, three transient operational conditions are simulated, including reactor power perturbation, external load reduction, and fluctuations in cooling-water temperature and flow rate. The result shows that the automatic control system can effectively control the system and yield satisfactory system dynamic characteristics under the condition of these transients. The research findings presented in this paper can serve as an important reference for the design and evaluation of control methods for NCLFR systems coupled with s-CO 2 -RCBC.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003732','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106608',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112786','A simulation study of X-ray-induced acoustic dosimetry for a compact FLASH radiotherapy device using digital phantoms','디지털 팬텀을 이용한 소형 FLASH 방사선치료 장치의 X선 유도 음향 선량 측정 모의 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Xulin Hu; Junling Wang; Dai Wu; Liuyuan Zhou; Xiaoqin Nie; Jianwen Huo','2026-09-12','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','FLASH radiotherapy (FLASH-RT) is a novel technique characterized by its capacity to deliver ultra-high radiation doses to tumor sites within fractions of a second, thereby effectively sparing normal tissues while maintaining therapeutic efficacy against tumors. The X-ray-based FLASH-RT holds particular promise for clinical adoption due to its accessibility to ultra-high-dose-rate beams, compact accelerator design, and reduced treatment costs. Accurate dosimetric verification during FLASH-RT delivery necessitates online monitoring and visualization of spatial dose distribution within the irradiation target. However, the extreme radiotherapy conditions pose substantial challenges to conventional dosimetry methods, such as signal saturation and measurement inaccuracies caused by pair production effects. To address these challenges, in this study, we propose and evaluate an X-ray-induced acoustic imaging (XAI) approach for in-phantom dosimetry in FLASH-RT. Using the Monte Carlo (MC) simulation toolkit Geant4, we modeled the irradiation of three heterogeneous tissue-mimicking phantoms with a single-pulse X-ray beam delivered by a 10 MV medical linear accelerator (Linac) integrated into a compact FLASH radiotherapy device. The generation, propagation, and attenuation of the induced acoustic waves following irradiation from the Linac were approximated using the k-space pseudospectral method. The acoustic signals were collected by a 128-element annular array transducer and subsequently used to reconstruct the spatial dose distribution within the phantoms. The results demonstrate the feasibility of XAI-based dosimetry for ultra-high-dose-rate X-ray beams even under low signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) conditions, providing a preliminary basis for its further development toward clinical FLASH-RT applications.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006742','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112786',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;US;AU','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112846','Development of a 3D neutron-transport-based system analysis code for heat pipe reactor nuclear energy system','히트파이프 원자로 원자력 에너지 계통을 위한 3차원 중성자 수송 기반 계통해석 코드 개발','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Dong Huang; Youqi Zheng; Xianan Du','2026-09-12','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926007346','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112846',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115217','Modeling for operators collaboration in the Main control room of SMR based on time petri net','시간 페트리넷 기반 SMR 주제어실 운전원 협업 모델링','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Zhengyang Li; Jun Zhao; Meng Kong; Hongru Zhao; Jiejuan Tong','2026-09-12','','2026-12','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','The main control room (MCR) is essential for the safe and coordinated operation of nuclear power plant (NPP). With the development of multi-reactor control configurations in small modular reactors (SMRs), operator collaboration has become increasingly important and more complex. However, existing studies have mainly focused on human error modeling and failure rate estimation, systematic methods for analyzing collaborative behaviors and quantifying task execution time in team-based scenarios remain limited. To address this gap, we propose a hierarchical modeling and performance evaluation framework based on an extended Time Petri Net (TPN). The TPN is extended to represent interrupt behavior and progress retention, enabling realistic modeling of collaborative tasks in the MCR. This study provides a quantitative framework for evaluating and optimizing operator collaboration and offers practical implications for MCR design in SMR.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004693','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115217',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104710','Analysis of Helical Coil Steam Generator Tube Rupture with Multiple Failure Accident at the innovative SMR using SPACE','SPACE를 이용한 혁신형 SMR의 다중고장 동반 나선형 코일 증기발생기 전열관 파단사고 해석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Hyunjoon Jeong','2026-09-12','','2026-09','연구논문','열수력·유체','ABSTRACT Steam generator tube rupture (SGTR) accidents may occur due to degradation mechanisms in steam generator tubes, such as stress corrosion cracking and foreign object damage. A more severe accident scenario, referred to as multiple steam generator tube rupture (MSGTR), involves the simultaneous failure of multiple tubes within a steam generator. Compared with conventional single-tube rupture events, MSGTR can result in significantly increased coolant discharge rates and more rapid accident progression. In addition, the possibility of containment bypass through the secondary system raises important safety concerns. Although extensive studies on SGTR accidents have been performed for conventional pressurized water reactors (PWRs), investigations of MSGTR behavior in advanced small modular reactors (SMRs), particularly innovative SMRs (i-SMRs), remain limited. In this study, a thermal-hydraulic safety analysis of MSGTR accidents in an i-SMR was performed using the SPACE code. Conservative assumptions were applied to evaluate accident behavior under design extension conditions (DEC) without active safety system operation. Sensitivity analyses were conducted for several major parameters, including the number of ruptured steam generator tubes, the heat transfer area of the passive auxiliary feedwater system (PAFS), and the rupture locations. In consideration of the helical coil steam generator (HCSG) configuration of the i-SMR, additional analyses were performed for accident scenarios involving simultaneous tube ruptures in two steam generators (SGs). The analysis results indicate that the inherent safety characteristics of the i-SMR, including the integral reactor configuration and passive heat removal systems, can maintain core cooling capability and mitigate accident consequences even under limiting MSGTR conditions. The findings of this study provide useful technical insights for the safety evaluation and licensing of advanced i-SMR designs.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S173857332600598X?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104710',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104709','Asymmetric loop seal clearing and reformation during a shutdown-cooling LOCA with single-loop passive cooling: ATLAS integral effect test and MARS-KS assessment','단일루프 피동냉각 조건의 정지냉각 LOCA 시 비대칭 루프실 제거 및 재형성: ATLAS 종합효과시험 및 MARS-KS 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Jae Bong Lee; Byoung-Uhn Bae; Yu-Sun Park; Kyoung-Ho Kang','2026-09-12','','2026-09','연구논문','열수력·유체','A loss-of-coolant accident (LOCA) initiated from a shutdown-cooling condition (shutdown-cooling LOCA) was investigated in the ATLAS integral effect test facility as the C4.2 test of the OECD-ATLAS3 joint project. The test simulated a 50 % direct vessel injection (DVI) line break of APR1400, with two operator actions: PAFS (passive auxiliary feedwater system) actuation on one steam generator after a 30-minute grace delay, and manual safety injection on a surrogate heater-temperature trigger. Under these low-power, low-pressure conditions, loop seal clearing and reformation developed asymmetrically: after both intermediate legs cleared, only the PAFS-cooled loop reformed its loop seal; the other remained cleared, holding the hot leg and downcomer at nearly equal pressure. This asymmetric state governs the inter-loop pressure distribution, yet the core inventory continued to deplete - PAFS removes heat but cannot make up lost inventory - and active injection was required. A limited MARS-KS assessment reproduces the pre-injection transient (heat-up onset within 1.3 %), and a PAFS-configuration sensitivity study indicates that passive cooling delays but does not prevent the excursion. The C4.2 dataset provides a unique integral characterization of a shutdown-cooling LOCA with a passive secondary heat sink and a code-assessment benchmark in a largely unvalidated low-pressure regime.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005978?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104709',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104702','Atmospheric dispersion modeling and radiological environmental impact assessment for the potential recommissioning of the Bataan Nuclear Power Plant, Philippines','필리핀 바탄 원자력발전소 재가동 가능성에 대한 대기확산 모델링 및 방사선 환경영향평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Fern Rose A. Peregrino; Jessie O. Samaniego; Angel T. Bautista; Rico Neil M. Quierrez; Jihan H. Adil','2026-09-12','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','To meet rising energy demands and reduce fossil fuel dependence, the Philippines aims to integrate nuclear energy in the energy mix by 2032, including the possible revival of the inactive Bataan Nuclear Power Plant (BNPP), a 621-MWe Westinghouse Pressurized Water Reactor. This work presents an updated radiological and environmental impact assessment (REIA) of estimated atmospheric radionuclide releases during normal operation using recent local meteorological data. The Hybrid Single Particle Lagrangian Integrated Trajectory (HYSPLIT) model was used to simulate long-range transport and deposition for the 2023 wet and dry seasons. Meteorological data from Cubi Point Weather Station in Zambales confirmed dominant northeast winds from November to April and southwest winds from May to October, consistent with GDAS1 data. Annual effective dose from cloudshine, groundshine, and inhalation pathways was estimated at 1.93 x 10 -5 mSv/yr for a critical residence 1.5 km to the northeast direction from the plant. This value is far below the ICRP 103 recommended public dose limit of 1 mSv/yr and lower than the previous Gaussian plume estimates. Major contributors were 3 H (HTO) and 133 Xe, accounting for approximately 50% and 30% of the total dose, respectively. The study highlights the applicability of HYSPLIT for REIA studies at prospective nuclear power plant sites.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005905','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104702',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','PH','PH','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/s0149-1970(26)00367-7','Editorial Board','편집위원회','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-09-12','','2026-11','편집물','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003677','https://doi.org/10.1016/s0149-1970(26)00367-7',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106588','Experimental and numerical thermal-hydraulic performance analyses of a novel spiral printed circuit heat exchanger','신형 나선형 인쇄기판형 열교환기의 열수력 성능에 관한 실험 및 수치해석','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Habib Ur Rahman; Muhammad Ilyas; Khalid Waheed; Abid Hussain; Muhammad Ali Khan; Mirza Nadeem Baig; Manzoor Ahmed; Inam ul Haq','2026-09-12','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study presents a comprehensive experimental and numerical investigation of a novel design Spiral Printed Circuit Heat Exchanger (SPCHE), evaluating its thermal-hydraulic performance against a conventional straight-channel Printed Circuit Heat Exchanger (PCHE). Water is used as a working fluid in both hot and cold channels. The finite element based framework is used to accurately capture the thermal-hydraulic behavior inside the SPCHE. Due to the channel curvature, Dean flow develops over the range of Reynolds numbers studied, motivating the use of a turbulent RANS 𝑘 – 𝜔 model. The numerical model is validated against experimental measurements to analyze various thermal hydraulics characteristics across Reynolds numbers ranging from 1000 to 12000 and hot-inlet temperatures from 323.15 K to 343.15 K. Results demonstrate that the spiral geometry induces secondary flows which significantly enhance thermal performance, yielding convective heat transfer coefficients exceeding 1 . 6 × 1 ⁢ 0 4 W m −2 K −1 and 2 . 0 × 1 ⁢ 0 4 W m −2 K −1 for the hot and cold channels, respectively at the expense of increased pressure drop. A comparative Performance Evaluation Criterion (PEC) analysis confirms a net thermal-hydraulic improvement of 52.5%–54.9% for the hot side and 35.4%–39.6% for the cold side. The heat duty is improved by 65%–70% with variation of the hot-inlet temperature from 323.15 K to 343.15 K. The experimentally validated friction factor and Nusselt number correlations with prediction errors within ± 5 % is obtained with current study. It provides a foundation for the enhanced performance design of advanced compact heat exchanger like SPCHE where high thermal efficiency and space constraints are critical. Furthermore, the spiral channels achieve a fourfold reduction in maximum dimension of the device corresponding to a linear compactness ratio ( 𝐿 s t r a i g h t / 𝐷 s p i r a l ) of 4.1, highlighting their superior space efficiency compared to straight channels.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003537','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106588',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','PK;CH;GB','PK','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106606','Improved core design and integrated back-end fuel cycle scheme for 200 MWt marine molten chloride fast reactor','200 MWt 선박용 용융염화물 고속로의 개선된 노심 설계 및 통합 후행 핵연료주기 방안','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Andika Putra Dwijayanto; Kenji Nishihara; Tomohiro Okamura; Masahiko Nakase','2026-09-12','','2027-01','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','This study presents an improved core design and the introduction of integrated back-end fuel cycle scheme for a 200 MWt Molten Chloride Fast Reactor (MCFR) intended as nuclear marine propulsion. The objective is to increase fuel burnup and reducing uranium consumption whilst maintaining appropriate safety level. Dual Reflector concept was introduced to increase fuel burnup, by using outer secondary magnesium oxide reflector as an addition to primary beryllium oxide reflector. To increase nuclear fuel utilisation, Partial Fuel Change (PFC) mechanism was applied with several fuel replacement fractions, whilst uranium re-enrichment scenario was inserted within the refuelling scheme to minimise natural uranium consumption even further. All burnup calculations were conducted using Serpent-2 reactor physics code and ENDF/B-VII.0 neutron cross section library. From the findings, the use of Dual Reflector concept with 50% PFC fraction and uranium re-enrichment increased fuel burnup up to 150.89 GWd/tHM and operational time up to 29 years. The use of Dual Reflector yields slightly weaker temperature coefficient of reactivity (TCR), but still sufficiently negative nonetheless. Overall, Dual Reflector concept with PFC refuelling scheme and uranium re-enrichment is suitable to improve design and fuel cycle performance of the marine MCFR. Whilst PFC scheme offers only a modest improvement of fuel consumption, uranium re-enrichment allows a significant reduction of natural uranium and enrichment demands.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003719','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106606',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','JP','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106607','Investigation of core-power control based on fuzzy predictive control and Kalman filter for a fast-spectrum lithium-cooled space nuclear reactor','고속 스펙트럼 리튬냉각 우주용 원자로의 퍼지 예측제어 및 칼만 필터 기반 노심출력 제어 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Zhenheng Yuan; Binzhe Sun; Yi Ren; Bo Pang','2026-09-12','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','The intelligent control of reactor core power is critical for the safety and reliability of space nuclear reactors, which operate in highly uncertain cosmic environments. Focusing on a lithium-cooled space reactor, this study proposed a fuzzy-model-based model predictive controller (FM-MPC-KF) based on a Takagi-Sugeno (T-S) fuzzy model and Kalman filter for core power regulation. To address system nonlinearities, the T-S fuzzy approach was employed to approximate the core dynamics. A Kalman filter was incorporated to estimate the reactor core states under limited sensor availability and the presence of measurement noise. The FM-MPC-KF controller was evaluated through comprehensive simulations covering ramp and step transients, and compared with Fuzzy Model Predictive Control (FMPC). The results demonstrate that FM-MPC-KF offers superior dynamic performance and enhanced load-following capability compared to the standard FMPC. Furthermore, the unified fuzzy prediction framework conceptually simplifies the multi-controller architecture, establishing its proof-of-concept algorithmic feasibility as a potential candidate for space reactor control. Moreover, with the integrated Kalman filter, FM-MPC-KF exhibits notably better baseline noise immunity than FMPC against Gaussian, Poisson, and salt-and-pepper measurement noise. This study underscores the potential of combining T-S fuzzy modeling, MPC, and the Kalman filter for the advanced control of space nuclear reactors under complex and uncertain conditions.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003720','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106607',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112806','Anomaly-aware leveling algorithm for airborne gamma-ray spectroscopy data','항공 감마선 분광 데이터를 위한 이상치 인지 레벨링 알고리즘','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Chao Xiong; Xin Wang; Tao Wu; Xin Qiao; Yuan Yuan; Hexi Wu','2026-09-11','','2027-02','연구논문','방사선·계측','Airborne gamma-ray spectrometry (AGS) data often exhibit directional anomalies termed “stripe noise”, which obscure true subsurface distributions and hinder mineral exploration. To address this without tie-line assistance, this paper proposes an anomaly-aware AGS data leveling algorithm. Original data are clustered using an improved directional neighborhood search strategy with entropy and deviation factors. Based on noise characteristics, a dual-dimensional background estimation technique is designed, while an enhanced sample entropy method accurately delineates anomalous regions to avoid masking crucial mineralization features. Compared to traditional micro-leveling, the proposed approach yields a larger reduction in the Root Mean Square Error (RMSE) across survey lines, improving data consistency by approximately 25\% while successfully preserving roughly 92\% of genuine ore-caused anomalies. Power spectral density and profile analyses confirm that post-leveling data exhibit smoother trends, effectively filtering out high-frequency noise. Specifically, the coefficient of variation decreases by an average of 26\% across 13 out of 14 survey lines using an optimal 3 × 9 filter window. These quantitative results demonstrate that our algorithm achieves excellent stripe suppression with minimal data distortion, providing an efficient, robust solution for high-fidelity AGS data processing.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006948','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112806',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112836','Natural circulation characteristics of compact petal-shaped fuel rod bundle channel under rolling conditions','요동 조건에서 소형 꽃잎형 핵연료봉 다발 유로의 자연순환 특성','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jinyi Cao; Jianchuang Sun; Xuelong Li; Wenchao Zhang; Jinchen Wang; Weihua Cai','2026-09-11','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study develops a multiscale computational model to examine the thermal–hydraulic response of a natural circulation loop equipped with a compact arranged petal-shaped fuel rod bundle under rolling motion. Rolling motion changes the gravity projection of loop sections and introduces inertial forces, thereby modifying the driving pressure. The results indicate that oscillatory flow is governed by the dynamic balance between time-varying driving pressure and flow resistance. Under static conditions, the rod bundle exhibits geometric periodicity and centrosymmetric temperature characteristics. Local temperature distributions along helical auxiliary lines show distinct thermal responses in petal-root and petal-tip regions. Petal-root regions generally have higher wall temperatures and weaker axial fluctuations, whereas petal-tip regions show lower average temperatures but stronger periodic fluctuations. Under rolling motion, the transverse coolant redistribution breaks temperature centrosymmetry, especially in the upper rod-bundle region and outer subchannels. These findings support thermal safety assessment and reliability evaluation of marine natural circulation systems.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926007243','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112836',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;VN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112833','Study on density wave oscillations in multi-coil parallel helical-coiled tubes for small modular reactors','소형모듈원자로용 다중 코일 병렬 나선형 전열관의 밀도파 진동 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Sheng-hui Liu; Yi-hang Wu; Muhammad Jahanzaib; Hou-jun Gong; Jia-ning Dai; Yi-chen Dong','2026-09-11','','2027-02','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926007218','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112833',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115203','Assessment of DRACCAR predictive capabilities during bundle reflood under low-power conditions: A systematic uncertainty and sensitivity analysis','저출력 조건 핵연료다발 재관수 시 DRACCAR 예측 성능 평가: 체계적 불확실성 및 민감도 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','J.E. Luna Valencia; T. Glantz','2026-09-11','','2026-12','연구논문','기타 원자력','International audience','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004553','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115203',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115179','Experimental flow visualization and thermal-hydraulic characterization of local heating effects in a molten salt natural circulation loop','용융염 자연순환 루프에서 국부 가열 효과의 유동 가시화 실험 및 열수력 특성 규명','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Thomas Carson; Hansol Kim; Joseph Seo; Theodore Kupper; Cole Gentry; Kevin Clarno; Yassin Hassan','2026-09-11','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','As the primary mechanism of passive heat removal in nuclear reactors, understanding natural circulation is paramount to their safe operation and shutdown conditions. Natural circulation in molten salt reactors is of particular relevance due to the fluid’s high Prandtl number as well as the phase of the fissile material in liquid-fueled reactors. Natural circulation loops are employed to study the thermal-hydraulic behavior of fluids when subject to thermal gradients and small flow disturbances. The objective of this work is to introduce and analyze the experimental effects of local heating conditions on the velocity profile and near-wall behavior of molten salts in a heated transparent test section. The study combines experimental PIV measurements with thermal-hydraulic characterization of the same natural-circulation operating states. Particle image velocimetry (PIV) was performed, and the boundary layer was analyzed for three different heating conditions. Those conditions were applied to the transparent test section: a cooling test condition, a thermally isolated test condition, and a heated test condition. In addition, the other thermal conditions of the loop were held constant. As the test section is heated, the peak velocity and slope of the velocity profile increase with test section heater power.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004310','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115179',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115208','Investigation of high-flux two-phase flows and entrainment mechanisms','고유속 2상유동 및 비말동반 메커니즘 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Charie A. Tsoukalas; Akshay Khandelwal; Mamoru Ishii','2026-09-11','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','Interfacial area concentration and critical heat flux predictions in high-void-fraction two-phase flow depend on correctly identifying the annular sub-regime but static flow regime maps do not resolve these sub-regimes or their transient behavior. A Kohonen self-organizing map (SOM) trained on chord length statistics from a two-sensor droplet-capable conductivity probe (DCCP-2) was previously used to classify these sub-regimes up to j g ≈ 16 m / s . Here the classifier is applied, without retraining, to 51 new test conditions in a 25.4 mm ID vertical pipe extending the range to j g = 27 m / s and j f = 3 m / s . The SOM separates the extended dataset into the same three classes with minimal inter-class overlap above j g ≈ 16 m / s : annular flow at j f = 0.1 − 0.2 m / s , rolling annular at intermediate j f , and wispy-annular above j f = 1 m / s . High-speed imaging at 2000 fps for representative conditions at high j g for each class is consistent with the classification. Annular flow is marked by a thin, ripple-dominated wall film and an optically clear gas core, with disturbance waves absent below the critical film Reynolds number. Rolling annular flow shows large-amplitude disturbance waves that propagate and merge across the film, with entrainment governed by ligament break-up at wave crests and wave undercut. Wispy-annular flow is distinguished by liquid ligaments that shed from the disturbed interface and penetrate deep into the gas core, carrying entrained gas bubbles rather than breaking down into discrete. These regime-specific mechanisms are consistent across both short ( 0 − 44 ms ) and long ( 0 − 180 ms ) observation windows, distinguishing transient wave passage from sustained interfacial disturbance. The imaging is corroborated by a Kohonen self-organizing map applied to DCCP-2 chord length statistics, which reproduces the same three-class structure with well-defined boundaries above j g = 16 m / s , confirming that the visually identified flow structures correspond to statistically distinct probe signatures.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004607','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115208',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115211','Microstructure and hydrogen content of electrodeposited chromium coating on the inner surface of EP823-SH steel cladding','EP823-SH 강 피복관 내면 전착 크롬 코팅의 미세조직 및 수소 함량','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Isayev R.Sh; G.N. Elmanov; P.S. Dzhumaev; I.A. Naumenko; V.I. Polskij; A.V. Markin','2026-09-11','','2026-12','연구논문','핵연료·재료','To reduce corrosion damage to the inner surface of ferritic-martensitic steel fuel rod claddings, additional measures must be taken to increase the corrosion resistance of this steel. One potential approach is applying a chromium coating to the cladding''s inner surface. This study investigates the microstructure and hydrogen content of chromium coatings electrodeposited onto the inner surface of fuel rod cladding tubes (internal diameter: 8.7 mm). Under the tested conditions, an electrolyte temperature of 30–35 °C yielded crack-free, equiaxed coatings at a current density ≤ 0.2 A/cm 2 . Higher electrolyte temperatures produce coatings with a columnar structure. Hydrogen accumulation of ∼2 at.% was observed in coatings deposited under optimal conditions. Annealing chromium-coated claddings at 420 °C enables complete hydrogen degassing. Consequently, hydrogen uptake during the chromium plating process will not degrade the cladding''s original performance characteristics.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004632','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115211',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','AZ;RU','AZ','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104707','Clause-Level Structural Alignment between ASME Section III and Czech NTD A.S.I. Section III: Domain- and Component-Resolved Assessment','ASME Section III와 체코 NTD A.S.I. Section III 간 조항 수준 구조적 대응: 분야 및 기기별 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Seungwook Lee; Ki Sig Kang; Wooyong Jung','2026-09-11','','2026-09','연구논문','열수력·유체','Comparative studies of nuclear pressure-boundary component design codes have focused mainly on selected provisions and governing equations, but domain- and component-resolved clause-level quantification between ASME Section III and NTD A.S.I. Section III has not been systematically reported. This study applies a Clause Harmonization Index (CHI) to compare the two codes for piping, vessels, and pumps across nine technical domains. The overall clause-level structural alignment was CHI = 0.724, with piping showing the highest overall correspondence and pumps the lowest. A bounded numerical illustration for piping, vessel, and equivalent pump pressure-boundary cases showed only limited deviations in representative analytical quantities, with the largest difference not exceeding 5.5% in simplified fatigue usage, under the yield-governed pressure–temperature condition representative of primary system operation. These patterns are traced to two structural features of NTD A.S.I.: an explicit ASME-NC alternative for piping and qualification-related provisions distributed across multiple NTD Sections. The CHI-based comparison provides a reproducible basis for identifying where additional cross-code mapping is required in national adaptations of ASME Section III.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005954?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104707',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104699','Comparative Neutronic Performance Assessment of Prospective Accident-Tolerant Fuel Configurations for the VVER-1200','VVER-1200용 사고저항성핵연료(ATF) 후보 구성의 중성자 성능 비교 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','K.M..Rakib Al Hasan; Md. Shafiqul Islam; Altab Hossain','2026-09-11','','2026-09','연구논문','열수력·유체','An OpenMC-based study assesses the neutronic performance of four prospective ATF configurations—UN, UN+U 3 Si 2 , UO 2 +BeO, and UO 2 +SiC against conventional UO 2 for the VVER-1200, considering combinations of Zircaloy, SiC composite, and SiC-coated Zircaloy cladding. The objective is to assess prospective ATF configurations and identify candidates that balance enhanced safety, sustained reactivity, and acceptable thermal performance. Results reveal distinct trade-offs. UN exhibits a relatively high peak power density, consistent with its greater fissile atom density compared to UO 2 , while maintaining a low peak fuel temperature (∼410 °C), indicating improved thermal behavior; however, its higher radial power peaking factor (1.72) may increase localized heat generation. The oxide-based configurations show similar initial reactivity (k eff = 1.23–1.26), but UO 2 +SiC experiences a greater reduction, decreasing to 0.75 at 40 MWd/kgHM. In contrast, the nitride-based configurations converge to similar reactivity at high burnup, demonstrating consistent depletion behavior. Among the investigated fuel configurations, UN+U 3 Si 2 demonstrates balanced neutronic and approximate thermal performance under the adopted modeling assumptions, highlighting its potential as a promising candidate for further assessment in the VVER-1200. In addition, the analysis is based on neutronic modeling with a sequential thermal assessment and does not include fully coupled thermal-hydraulic feedback or experimental validation.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005875?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104699',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','BD','BD','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104703','Development of an inspection maturity level model for the Korean regulatory framework and its application to spent fuel dry storage facilities','국내 규제체계를 위한 검사 성숙도 수준 모델 개발 및 사용후핵연료 건식저장시설 적용','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Dae Sik Yook; Gyeong-uk Kang; SaeHanSol Kang; Minchul Song','2026-09-11','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Because siting a final disposal facility for high-level radioactive waste remains challenging in South Korea, on-site dry storage of spent fuel is becoming increasingly important. Regulatory inspection programs should ensure safety during dry storage operation and future transport after long-term storage. Therefore, inspection programs should support differentiated inspection based on safety performance and risk significance, beyond simple compliance with procedures and acceptance criteria. This study develops an Inspection Maturity Level (IML) model based on international recommendations and a case study of the U.S. Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) Independent Spent Fuel Storage Installation (ISFSI) inspection program. The IML model consists of five levels: regulatory requirements, prescriptive inspection, life-cycle-based inspection, performance-based inspection, and risk-informed regulation. Using this model, the U.S. and Korean inspection frameworks for spent fuel dry storage operations were compared. The results show that South Korea''s inspection framework for loading and unloading activities remains at IML-1 because dedicated inspection programs and detailed procedures have not yet been established. A screening-level relative risk assessment and an IML evaluation matrix were then applied to derive key elements of an inspection program. The results suggest that South Korea should develop structured inspection contents integrating detailed procedures, performance verification, and risk-informed prioritization.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005917','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104703',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104704','Engineering design and verification of toroidal field magnet power supply for EXL-50U spherical tokamak device','EXL-50U 구형 토카막 장치의 토로이달 자장 코일 전원장치 공학설계 및 검증','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Zemin Wang; Liangliang Hao; Zixuan Zhao; Peihai Zhou; Shaoxuan Liu; Wenwu Luo; Xianming Song; Dianjie Dang; Zequn Sun','2026-09-11','','2027-02','연구논문','방사선·계측','This paper presents the systematic engineering design and verification of a megawatt-level pulsed power supply system tailored for the toroidal field (TF) magnet of the ENN Xuanlong-50 Upgrade (EXL-50U) spherical tokamak. The system is engineered to meet stringent operational demands, including a high current of 150 kA, second-scale pulse durations, and high robustness. To overcome the engineering challenges of input frequency fluctuations and complex parameter coupling inherent to pulsed generator supplies, a system-level hardware selection and parameter-matching methodology was established. This framework comprehensively integrates five core components: the pulsed generator set (PGS), phase-shifting transformer (PST), thyristor converter (TC), interphase reactor (IPR), and overvoltage protection circuit (OVPC). Furthermore, to resolve the inherent trade-off between high-precision tracking and system robustness when driving large inductive loads, a compound control strategy based on a feedforward-feedback architecture was proposed and implemented. Commissioning and experimental data demonstrate that the dynamic response and flat-top current-regulation accuracy of the power supply fully satisfy the physical experimental requirements of the EXL-50U device, thereby verifying the effectiveness and engineering applicability of the proposed design.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005929','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104704',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2722502','Fabrication and Characterization of B
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2721224','Knowledge-Driven Explainable AI for Automated Defect Detection in Nuclear Reactor Components','원자로 구성품 자동 결함 탐지를 위한 지식 기반 설명가능 AI','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','A. Young; C. Manning; J. Zabalza; G. West; P. Murray; S. McArthur','2026-09-11','2026-09-11','2026-09-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','Critical assets in nuclear power plants, such as reactor vessels, coolant systems, and containment structures, must be inspected to ensure safe and reliable operations. However, these inspections are often complicated by the harsh environments in which they are conducted, with high radiation levels creating significant visual noise in inspection footage. Identifying defects, such as cracks or surface anomalies, is vital for preventing failures, but manual review by engineers can be time consuming due to challenging visual conditions.To address these challenges, a novel, automated defect detection algorithm has been developed, integrating image processing techniques with a knowledge-driven framework. The approach uses frame differencing to detect temporal changes in the video frames, thresholding to isolate potential defects, and morphological operations to eliminate noise.The main contribution of this work is a rule-based filtering process that incorporates domain-specific knowledge, including factors such as anomaly size, persistence across multiple frames, and proximity to critical surfaces. A key feature of this approach is the emphasis on explainability. Unlike black-box machine learning models, this method provides clear, rule-based justifications for each detected anomaly. Such transparency is crucial in the highly regulated nuclear industry, where every decision must be traceable and defensible.To validate the approach, it was applied to a case study involving calandria tubesheet bore inspection videos, a particularly challenging data set due to the visual noise caused by radiation. The knowledge-based rules tailored to this inspection process helped filter out irrelevant anomalies and generated detailed reports with visualizations to assist engineers in their final assessments.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2721224','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2721224',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','GB','GB','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106598','A Human-Equipment-Society (HES) framework for classifying and analyzing operational events in Chinese nuclear power plants','중국 원자력발전소 운전사건 분류 및 분석을 위한 인간-설비-사회(HES) 프레임워크','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Tao Zhang; Jianqiang Shan; Shengzhi Liu','2026-09-11','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','An effective analysis of operational events is crucial to preventing major accidents and improving safety levels in nuclear power. However, global event reporting currently suffers from inconsistent standards, vague information descriptions, and superficial root cause analysis. These shortcomings hinder the closure of the feedback loop of the experience and constrain systematic improvements in nuclear power safety management. Based on accident causation theory, the Human-Equipment Society (HES) cause classification and analysis framework was proposed for nuclear power operational events. The framework aims to achieve systematic and standardized attribution of event causes. A total of 532 operational events published by the Chinese National Nuclear Safety Administration between 2006 and 2024 were compiled and analyzed using the HES framework. At the triggering factor level, the results show that human factors account for 50.38% and equipment factors account for 46.62% of the triggering events, while society factors account for 3.01%. At the root cause level, the results show that equipment failure (35.71%), organizational failures (26.32%), and individual failure (19.17%) are the main root causes. It can be found that root causes related to human error account for 57.52% (including coupling failure) and those related to equipment failure account for 54.51% (including coupling failure). The average number of events per unit of operation has shown a downward trend since 2016. Differences in the distribution of event triggers in different nuclear power plants highlight the need for targeted safety management. The standardized analysis framework developed in this study can provide data-driven decision support for nuclear regulatory agencies and operators, and facilitate a change in experience feedback from case-specific handling to systematic prevention. In addition, it promotes the intelligent and refined development of nuclear power safety management.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S014919702600363X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106598',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106593','Estimate unfavorable meteorological conditions based on ERA5 data for the transport of radionuclides from the nuclear power plant site','ERA5 데이터 기반 원자력발전소 부지로부터 방사성핵종 이동에 불리한 기상조건 추정','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Andrzej, A. Wyszogrodzki; Sławomir Potempski; Piotr Kopka; Michał Jędrzejczyk; Andrzej Mazur','2026-09-11','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','The main goal of this study is to estimate the most unfavorable stability conditions for the purpose of transport and dispersion simulations of radioactive nuclides from hypothetical accidental releases at a planned nuclear power plant location. Based on these weather sequences, it is possible to determine, with a high degree of confidence, the maximum extent of Emergency Planning Zones (EPZs) around nuclear power plants, thereby enabling effective preparedness planning and optimized emergency response strategies. The analysis is based on the ERA5 reanalysis data set for the 24- year period between 2000 and 2023. The Pasquill-Gifford stability conditions were computed with the use of ERA5-derived near-surface winds and net surface radiative fluxes. The different methods for estimating net surface radiative flux allow the selection of the most unfavorable stability conditions from the point of the adverse effects on the environment and humans. A continuous multi-day sequence, based on different combinations of stability classes, depicts possible realistic scenarios. The statistical analysis led to the selection of the reference year for the purpose of accompanying site evaluation studies with a numerical dispersion modelling suite. The short-range simulations of instantaneous atmospheric dispersion with JRODOS/RIMPUFF models are performed to compare the expected doses for the selected meteorological conditions.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003586','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106593',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','PL','PL','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112826','A hybrid neural-voxel physics-constrained framework for 3D reconstruction of radiation fields from multiple unknown sources','미지의 다중 선원으로부터 방사선장 3차원 재구성을 위한 신경망-복셀 하이브리드 물리제약 프레임워크','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Zongheng Hong; Feiyun Cong; Bo Yang; Zhangyu Chen; Tianjie Xie','2026-09-10','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Accurate and rapid reconstruction of three-dimensional (3D) radiation fields is a critical task for nuclear emergency response and environmental monitoring. However, existing neural network reconstruction methods are heavily reliant on the quantity and quality of measurement data. Under sparse data conditions, this dependence often leads to physically implausible predictions, thereby compromising the reliability of safety assessments. To address this challenge, this paper introduces a Hybrid Neural-Voxel Physics-Constrained Framework (HNV-PCF). Unlike purely data-driven models, HNV-PCF embeds a discrete physical radiation transport model into a continuous neural network architecture, effectively coupling physical priors with data-driven rendering. Through comprehensive numerical simulations and high-fidelity scenarios, HNV-PCF was systematically compared with conventional data-driven methods under varying levels of data sparsity. Quantitative results demonstrate that, under typical sparse robotic sampling scenarios, HNV-PCF reduces the global Mean Absolute Percentage Error (MAPE) by 68.7% compared to the best-performing baseline. Furthermore, even in high-fidelity obstructed environments involving complex shielding, the proposed method robustly maintains physical consistency and accurately delineates the structural contours of hazardous regions. The method proposed in this paper offers an effective approach to solving the reconstruction problem of radiation fields under data-scarce conditions, demonstrating significant application potential in the field of nuclear safety.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926007140','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112826',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112783','Immersed boundary methods for the NekRS spectral element Navier–Stokes solver','NekRS 스펙트럴 요소 Navier–Stokes 해석기를 위한 가상경계법','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Aya Hegazy; Dillon Shaver; Rizwan-uddin; April Novak','2026-09-10','','2027-02','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006717','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112783',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115202','A reliability-based framework for emergency planning zone assessment under radioactive atmospheric release','방사성물질 대기 방출 시 비상계획구역 평가를 위한 신뢰도 기반 프레임워크','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Túlio Raunyr Cândido Felipe; Juliana de Sá Sanchez','2026-09-10','','2026-12','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004541','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115202',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115204','Application of deep learning techniques for nuclear safety calculations; analysis for LBLOCA scenarios','원자력 안전 계산을 위한 딥러닝 기법 적용: LBLOCA 시나리오 해석','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Roberto Miguelez-Silva; Kevin Fernandez-Cosials; César Queral','2026-09-10','','2026-12','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Deterministic safety analysis constitutes a foundational component within the framework of safety analysis in nuclear power plants. In this work, the potential of Deep Learning as high-efficiency tools for nuclear surrogate-modelling is explored. These models are used to calculate Figures of Merit, representing either discrete values or entire temporal sequences through Deep Neural Networks and Long Short-Term Memory architectures. Since this approach eliminates the need for direct code execution for input creation phase, this approach enables the performance of extensive Sensitivity Analysis and Uncertainty Quantification on sequences outside the training, validation, and test sets. The trained Large Break LOCA surrogate models achieved Mean Absolute Error lower than 27 K for cladding temperature and 0.03 for normalized core liquid level using a dynamic approach. Furthermore, a static approach developed for Peak Cladding Temperature yielded Mean Absolute Error of 10 K and 22 K for the blowdown and reflood phases, respectively. A comprehensive comparison between static surrogate models and TRACE code results was conducted by performing Once-at-a-Time sensitivity analysis. Non-linear cross-input interaction cases were analyzed by means of surrogate models. Shapley additive explanations analysis for interpretability and surrogate models MC dropout analysis was performed too. Wilks method for Uncertainty Quantification was performed to initially assess the reliability of the surrogate models against TRACE code previous results.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004565','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115204',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','ES','ES','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115212','Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy investigation on the oxidation behavior of Si-containing ferritic/martensitic steels in lead–bismuth eutectic','납–비스무트 공정 내 Si 함유 페라이트/마르텐사이트강 산화 거동의 전기화학 임피던스 분광 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Yang Li; Xian-ze Meng; Lin Luo; Fa-he Cao; Xing-ming Yang; Jing Liu; Heng-jiang Chai; Ping-han Chen; Yue Zhou','2026-09-10','','2026-12','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004644','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115212',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104685','An unsupervised anomaly detection method for controller area network in nuclear industrial control system','원자력 산업제어계통 CAN(Controller Area Network)을 위한 비지도 이상탐지 방법','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Yanqun Wu; Yongtao Zhang; Fan Wen; MingXing Liu; Quan Ma; Meiyuan Chen','2026-09-10','','2027-02','연구논문','AI·디지털','Despite its widespread adoption in industrial control systems (ICS), the Controller Area Network (CAN) lacks built-in security, rendering it vulnerable to cyber threats. Existing anomaly detection methods for CAN are hindered by the lack of labeled attack data, diverse attack patterns, and stringent resource constraints, particularly in nuclear applications, where KB-level memory, stringent real-time latency, and complex physical transients pose unique challenges. To address these challenges, we present CANCLLA, an unsupervised autoencoder framework with parallel CNN and BiLSTM encoders to jointly capture spatial payload patterns and temporal dependencies, enhanced by attention and feature-wise threshold selection. We also introduce VNCAN, a nuclear-specific benchmark constructed from a certified full-scope simulator to capture realistic operational transients. Extensive experiments on VNCAN and public CAN datasets demonstrate that CANCLLA achieves highly competitive detection performance against both standard and stealthy attacks, uses only 1/6 to 1/92 of the parameters of competing methods, and attains an end-to-end detection latency of 11.709 ms. These advantages demonstrate strong potential for future deployment on legacy and embedded devices in nuclear ICS without compromising real-time control performance.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005735','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104685',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112827','Effects of inlet boundary conditions and turbulence models on pressure pulsation prediction in a reactor coolant pump','원자로냉각재펌프 압력맥동 예측에 대한 입구 경계조건 및 난류모델의 영향','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Yongxin Jin; Zhiyuan Shang; Mingqian Zhang; Hongqian Wang; Junlian Yin','2026-09-09','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926007152','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112827',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115194','Comparison of MURR high-assay low-enriched uranium fuel element and design demonstration element irradiation thermo-mechanical analysis predictions','MURR HALEU 핵연료 요소와 설계실증 요소의 조사 열-기계 해석 예측 비교','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Guanyi Wang; Prasad Vegendla; Firat Cetinbas; Joseph Nielsen; Grant Hawkes; Cezary Bojanowski; Erik Wilson; Walid Mohamed; Travis Howell; Gregory Housley; Maria Pinilla','2026-09-09','','2026-12','연구논문','핵연료·재료','A high-assay low-enriched uranium (HALEU) fuel element design for the University of Missouri Research Reactor (MURR) has been completed to convert from highly enriched uranium (HEU) to a very high-density U-10Mo monolithic fuel. Irradiation performance of this fuel element as a design demonstration element (DDE) has been predicted. This DDE is designed to be irradiated under conditions close to prototypic of actual reactor irradiation conditions to confirm fuel plate performance and resistance to potential failure modes for reactor-specific plate and element designs including the first full-scale irradiation of the thinner MURR HALEU plates. Using the same method developed for MURR HALEU element, irradiation thermo-mechanical (T-M) analysis of MURR DDE is performed to be compared with the structural analyses of MURR HALEU element operating in the MURR reactor. This study indicates that the MURR DDE structural behavior is representative of that of the MURR HALEU fuel element. In addition, this analysis predicts the channel gap reductions expected in the MURR DDE, which can be compared to the channel gap measurement in-between and after the irradiation cycles.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004462','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115194',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104706','Neutron spectrum optimization for reactor-based production of Ac-225 and impurity control','원자로 기반 Ac-225 생산 및 불순물 제어를 위한 중성자 스펙트럼 최적화','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Guo Lv; Qingquan Pan; Xiaojing Liu','2026-09-09','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','ABSTRACT Actinium-225 ( 225 Ac) is a key medical radionuclide for targeted alpha therapy. Reactor irradiation of 226 Ra offers a promising route to expand 225 Ac supply, but the co-production of long-lived 227 Ac poses challenges for product quality control and clinical safety. In this study, a coupled neutronics-depletion model of a 226 Ra target irradiated in High Flux Isotope Reactor (HFIR) was developed using the LIGHTMC Monte Carlo code. Energy-bin flux perturbations were employed to establish the 225 Ac yield importance, 227 Ac impurity accumulation importance, and production-impurity optimization quality factor Fᵢ, enabling quantitative assessment of neutron-energy contributions and screening of candidate filtration materials. The results indicate that 157 Gd provides the best synergistic performance. At 0.004 g/cm 3 , it increases the 225 Ac yield by 3.45%, reduces 227 Ac by 23.05%, and improves the specific activity by 34.44% in HFIR. Japan Research Reactor No. 3 (JRR-3) validation confirms similar trends, demonstrating its potential cross-reactor applicability. The proposed method provides quantitative guidance for neutron spectrum tailoring, filtration-material selection, and 227 Ac impurity control.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005942','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104706',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
