INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106594','Institutional structures, ownership models, and the economic impacts of microreactors in remote Indigenous communities','원격지 원주민 공동체 초소형원자로의 제도적 구조, 소유 모델 및 경제적 영향','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Daniel Yupanqui; Oscar Zapata; Ken Belcher; Greg Poelzer','2026-09-09','','2027-01','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','According to North (1990), institutions are the formal and informal rulessuch as laws, norms, and customsthat shape human interaction and structure how organizations interact.2 Economies of size refer to the ability of a utility to lower the energy costs of production by increasing energy production.For more context, visit (Duffy, 2009).3 Organizations are groups of people or entities that operate within rules and pursue a specific purpose or goal (North, 1990;Williamson, 1985).','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003598','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106594',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112820','Numerical investigation of interfacial stability and crack-induced cohesive degradation in Cr-coated zircaloy-4 cladding under LOCA conditions','LOCA 조건에서 Cr 코팅 지르칼로이-4 피복관의 계면 안정성 및 균열 유발 응집 열화 수치해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jinkai Zhang; Zhaohao Wang; Zhenhong Ge; Di Yun; Wenbo Liu','2026-09-08','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926007085','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112820',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112803','Numerical investigation of thermal-hydraulic behavior in LBE-Cooled fast reactor assembly under ocean conditions via UDF-Enhanced CFD model','UDF 강화 CFD 모델을 이용한 해양 조건에서 LBE 냉각 고속로 집합체의 열수력 거동 수치해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Yu Zhu; Kefan Zhang; Wenshun Duan; Sifan Dong; Hongli Chen','2026-09-08','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006912','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112803',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112792','Prompt neutron spectrum from 237Np(n,f) reaction at 〈En〉=3 MeV','〈En〉=3 MeV에서 237Np(n,f) 반응의 즉발중성자 스펙트럼','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','G. Mishra; Sukanya De; G. Mohanto; Ajay Kumar; R. Tripathi; R.G. Thomas','2026-09-08','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006808','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112792',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IN','IN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112736','Small-scale deposition behavior of radioactive plutonium aerosols in hilly terrain','구릉 지형에서 방사성 플루토늄 에어로졸의 소규모 침적 거동','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Miao Yang; Xingfu Cai; Yurui Shao; Jiale Tian; Sufen Li; Yonggang Huo; Sheng Fang; Mingjun Wang','2026-09-08','','2027-02','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006249','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112736',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115209','The oxide evolution of 316 L in 180 °C high-temperature water and alternating 430 °C steam/180 °C water environments','180 °C 고온수 및 430 °C 증기/180 °C 물 교번 환경에서 316L의 산화막 변화','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Haodong Wu; Kun Ouyang; Lili Li; Yaqing Ren; Jiajun Liu; Jian Xu','2026-09-08','','2026-12','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004619','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115209',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104701','Global research trends in nuclear forensic: A bibliometric review','핵감식 분야의 전 세계 연구 동향: 계량서지학적 고찰','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Nurul Ilyani Zaharudin; Mohd Zamri Zainon; Anindya Drysca Kurniasari; Farah Hussan Sahib; Suriani Ibrahim; Mahazani Mohamad','2026-09-08','','2027-02','리뷰·관점','핵연료·재료','Nuclear forensic science is essential for global nuclear security, supporting the identification and attribution of nuclear materials outside regulatory control. Despite its strategic importance, a systematic understanding of the evolution, thematic structure, and key contributors shaping nuclear forensic research remains limited. This study presents a comprehensive bibliometric analysis of global nuclear forensic publication trends from 1973 to 2024 using peer-reviewed records from the Scopus database as of October 2025. Bibliometric indicators and network analyses were applied to examine temporal publication patterns, source journals, research themes, and authorship characteristics. Findings show that nuclear forensic research has transitioned from an emergent activity to a maturing and structured scientific discipline, mainly driven by international nuclear security priorities. The journal landscape is dominated by analytical chemistry, radiochemistry, and nuclear measurement science. Thematic analysis reveals a consolidated focus on uranium-based materials and attribution-oriented analytical techniques, whereas emerging approaches, such as microstructural analysis and computational methods, remain peripheral. Authorship and country-level analyses demonstrate a high concentration of research output within a limited number of nuclear-capable states and government-affiliated institutions. The results reveal methodological maturity yet highlight structural constraints, emphasizing the need for thematic diversification, interdisciplinary collaboration, and international capacity building to enhance nuclear forensic science globally.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005899','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104701',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','MY;ID','MY','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104700','Physical protection of nuclear facilities against unmanned aerial threats: Performance limits under identification timing constraints','무인 항공 위협에 대한 원자력시설 물리적 방호: 식별 시간 제약 하의 성능 한계','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Inhye Hahm; Seung-oh Seo; Sang-gon Park; Koo-yong Jeong; Ho Jin Ryu; Sungyeol Choi','2026-09-08','','2027-01','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Nuclear physical protection systems (PPS) have traditionally been designed against ground-based adversaries delayed by physical barriers. Unmanned aerial systems (UAS) bypass this design assumption through three-dimensional approach paths that no ground barrier can interrupt, compressing the defender response window to UAS flight time. Counter-UAS (C-UAS) response at nuclear sites is further constrained by site-specific conditions. Broadband RF jamming, widely deployed elsewhere, is disfavored due to electromagnetic compatibility requirements for instrumentation and control systems and the risk of uncontrolled UAS descent near radiological areas. Intelligent soft-kill neutralization (ISN), the preferred alternative, cannot be initiated until the UAS type is identified. This identification prerequisite introduces a timing constraint not yet quantitatively assessed in the nuclear physical protection literature. This paper presents a field-validated physical protection framework for evaluating C-UAS performance at nuclear facilities. Identification, neutralization, and detection performance are parameterized from field trials and environment-specific literature values. Analytical and Monte Carlo evaluations identify a critical UAS approach speed beyond which the baseline configuration structurally fails, falling within the operational range of payload-capable commercial platforms. Automated response emerges as the most impactful near-term improvement, and quantitative requirements for identification range and system response time are derived for open, suburban, and urban deployment environments.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005887','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104700',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2724783','Qualitative Cost-Benefit Assessment of Ownership Transfer versus Continued Storage of Legacy
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106597','How do evacuees'' choice behaviors regarding decontamination sites affect evacuation? — A case study of a nuclear power station in China','제염소 선택 행태가 대피에 미치는 영향 — 중국 원자력발전소 사례 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Shouhao Zhang; Yamin Ji','2026-09-08','','2027-01','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003628','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106597',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112789','An efficient method for fault tree analysis to support nuclear plant operation decision-making','원자력발전소 운전 의사결정 지원을 위한 효율적 고장수목 분석 방법','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Mohamed Y. Nassar; Joseph O’Leary; Yunfei Zhao','2026-09-07','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Fault tree analysis (FTA) is extensively used in the probabilistic risk assessment of nuclear power plants. One application of FTA is to support nuclear plant operation decision-making. In a nuclear plant, when the availability of components changes, that will affect the basic event probabilities in the fault tree of the plant. A fast and accurate evaluation of the fault tree to update the plant risk, represented by the top event probability in the fault tree, is essential to make adequate operation decisions. However, this task is challenging when the fault tree is large and complex. In this paper, a new method is introduced to efficiently update the top event probability without recalculating from scratch when basic event probabilities change. This method involves an offline phase where a set of scenarios is generated via importance sampling. Each scenario includes a sequence of basic event states and the associated weight, which accounts for importance sampling. In the online phase, only the stored weights need to be adjusted to reflect changes in basic event probabilities, allowing fast updating of the top event probability. A case study using synthetic fault trees demonstrates the proposed method’s effectiveness in achieving fast and accurate top event probability updating. Relative errors remain low and confidence intervals for given confidence levels remain narrow when the increase in the basic event probability is under one order of magnitude, though they increase or become wider when the increase in the basic event probability becomes larger, highlighting areas for future improvement. • An integrated offline–online approach to updating top event probability in fault tree analysis. • Reuse of sample scenarios from importance sampling to reduce computation time. • Capability of quantifying confidence in the updated top event probability. • Case study shows substantial computation time reduction.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006778','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112789',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112824','Identification of key determinants for operational stability in a 200 kW aqueous homogeneous reactor','200 kW 수용액 균질로의 운전 안정성 핵심 결정인자 규명','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Hongping Sun; Qingwen Xiong; Zhifang Qiu; Chunrui Deng; Ting Zhang; Gongle Song; Ziqiang Zou; Yong Zhang; Yu Liu','2026-09-07','','2027-02','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926007127','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112824',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115191','CFD-grade measurements of flow-debris interaction and PWR filter clogging behavior using MRI scanner','MRI 스캐너를 이용한 유동-이물질 상호작용 및 PWR 필터 막힘 거동의 CFD급 측정','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Vincent Klempau; Kristine John; Sven Grundmann; Martin Bruschewski; Markus Rehm; Elmar Rieder','2026-09-07','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','The reliability of the primary cooling circuit in a pressurized water reactor (PWR) is crucial for safe operation. Debris fretting, caused by solid particles in the coolant, can damage fuel rods and lead to the leakage of fission products into the primary circuit coolant. Optimized filters in the fuel assembly bottom nozzle (BNO) can capture debris while minimizing pressure loss and reducing clogging risk. To investigate the cooling flow through the bottom nozzle and filter, Magnetic Resonance Velocimetry (MRV) was employed using a 3 Tesla magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scanner. The study focused on a simplified bottom nozzle, filter, and the leading edge of a 5 × 5 fuel rod bundle. Without requiring optical access to the complex filter structure, MRV provided high-resolution flow measurements. It obtained 3D velocity fields and, for one unclogged case, 3D Reynolds stress tensors. The pressure drop across the filter was measured separately. Wire-like particles were introduced sequentially, enabling reconstruction of their positions and analysis of their impact on flow. At a Reynolds number (Re) of 50,250, and with up to 100 particles, the filter test resembled standard conditions. A clogging scenario was created by introducing 240 additional particles at Re = 20,000. Using MRI data, the clogged filter''s geometry was reconstructed for computational fluid dynamics (CFD) implementation. These CFD-grade measurements provide unique experimental data for validating particle motion and clogging models. Time-averaged velocity and Reynolds stress tensor data provide insights into how particles and agglomerations influence flow through the filter and around fuel rods, informing design improvements for enhanced reactor safety and efficiency.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004437','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115191',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','DE','DE','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115206','Deformation and fracture modeling of nuclear vessel penetration nozzles under severe accident: part I – Modeling for Alloy 600','중대사고 시 원자로용기 관통 노즐의 변형 및 파단 모델링: 제1부 – Alloy 600 모델링','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Jun-Won Park; Eui-Kyun Park; Yun-Jae Kim; Yukio Takahashi','2026-09-07','','2026-12','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004589','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115206',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','JP;KR','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115198','Deformation and fracture modeling of nuclear vessel penetration nozzles under severe accident: part II – modeling for alloy 82 and comparison with OLHF test data','중대사고 시 원자로용기 관통 노즐의 변형 및 파단 모델링: 제2부 – Alloy 82 모델링 및 OLHF 시험 데이터와의 비교','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Jun-Won Park; Hwang-Young Choi; Yun-Jae Kim; Yukio Takahashi','2026-09-07','','2026-12','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004504','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115198',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR;JP','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104670','Examining the significance of CRUD source-term at the coolant contact interface during decommissioning','해체 중 냉각재 접촉 계면에서 CRUD 선원항의 중요성 검토','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Do-Won Hyeun; Sang-Hyun Lim; Yu-Sun Yeom; Sang-Heon Lee; Jong-Soon Song','2026-09-07','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','In Korea, Nuclear Power Plants continually prepare and revise the final safety analysis report (FSAR), which is essential for predicting the source-term information of radioactive materials throughout their lifecycle. This report provides detailed information on the source-terms of Chalk River Unidentified Deposits (CRUD). The management of radioactive corrosion products, present on nuclear fuel surfaces and within the primary system, is crucial for ensuring equipment integrity and controlling worker exposure during operation. Unlike earlier studies that focused solely on the radioactive inventory of major components, this study established an integrated evaluation framework by coupling the CRUDTRAN, ORIGEN2, and PHITS codes to quantitatively assess the relative contribution of the CRUD source-term on the core support barrel (CSB) to worker doses, in comparison with the activation source-terms of the reactor pressure vessel (RPV). By calculating these specific source-terms and conducting subsequent radiation exposure assessments, this work underscores the critical significance of the CRUD source-term during the decommissioning phase. The comparative dose assessment revealed that in the absence of system decontamination, the radiation exposure contributed by the CRUD source-term exceeded that from the structural activation of the RPV across the range of deposition-fraction assumptions, from about 1.5 times under the minimum assumption to about 117 times under the maximum assumption. These quantitative findings indicate that CRUD is a major source of worker exposure during the decommissioning phase, which should not be neglected relative to the activation of internal components.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005589','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104670',1,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
