INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112779','Uncertainty-aware superpixel segmentation and bayesian optimization for sampling strategy development using activation analysis of OPR-1000','OPR-1000 방사화 분석을 이용한 시료채취 전략 수립을 위한 불확실성 고려 슈퍼픽셀 분할 및 베이지안 최적화','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jeongon Eom; Sewon Kim; Seokjun Hong; Changje Park','2026-09-06','','2027-02','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006675','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112779',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112811','ZnO-rich Borate-Titanate glasses engineered with Eu3+ and Ba2+ for improved optical features and gamma-ray shielding properties','광학 특성 및 감마선 차폐 성능 향상을 위해 Eu3+ 및 Ba2+를 첨가한 ZnO 고함량 붕산염-티탄산염 유리','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','M.I. Sayyed; Manjunatha; Sulochana P. Melinmath; Shams A.M. Issa; P.B.Ranjith Gowda; A.S. Bennal','2026-09-06','','2027-02','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006997','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112811',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','JO;IN;LB;SA','JO','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115200','Development of a multilayer vapor-liquid phase change model for the VOF method and simulation of vapor condensation process','VOF 방법을 위한 다층 증기-액체 상변화 모델 개발 및 증기 응축 과정 모의','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Xiaohong Yan; Hekai Ye; Ting Ma; Qi Xiao','2026-09-06','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004528','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115200',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112810','Characterizing self-attenuation in UO2 powder gamma spectrometry: development of a matrix-independent assay for mass and enrichment quantification in bulk nuclear material⋆','UO2 분말 감마 분광분석의 자기감쇠 특성 규명: 벌크 핵물질의 질량 및 농축도 정량을 위한 매질 독립 분석법 개발','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Mohamad Sukron F. Husein; Mohammad Subekti; Sihana Sihana; Didik Setiaji; Agus. Sunarto; Fajar M. Ramadhan; Mohammad Alfarisie; Etty Mutiara; Ahadi D. Prasetya; Erlina Noerpitasari','2026-09-05','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Accurate nondestructiv e assay (NDA) of bulk nuclear materials lacking a rigid physical form presents significant geometric challenges compared with standard item-form configurations such as sintered pellets, plates, or fuel rods. The quantification of unsealed uranium dioxide UO 2 powder is compromised by variable localized packing densities and severe internal self-attenuation of the primary 185.7 keV 235 U gamma-ray emission. This study investigates these limitations by characterizing UO 2 powder samples (0.4 to 4.0 wt% 235 U enrichment; 1–25 g uranium mass) using both a portable low-resolution NaI(Tl) and a high-resolution HPGe spectrometer. Empirical modeling of the specific count rate against areal density confirmed adherence to the integrated Beer-Lambert law, establishing a minimum physical thickness threshold of 1.0 cm to achieve infinite thickness saturation of 95%. Absolute 185.7 keV count rates below this geometric threshold are highly susceptible to density fluctuations, rendering them unreliable for direct mass or enrichment quantification in non-rigid matrices. To overcome this self-attenuation barrier, the highly penetrating 1001 keV emission from 234m Pa was validated as an internal bulk mass standard. Using the relative activity ratio (185.7 keV/1001 keV) successfully neutralized both structural matrix inconsistencies and discrepancies in intrinsic hardware efficiency. A comparative analysis between the two detection systems yielded a linear transfer function (R 2 > 0.97, slope = 0.68, intercept = 0.51). This methodology provides a detector-agnostic physical signature that significantly enhances bulk uranium verifications and lays the groundwork for accurately quantifying advanced non-item nuclear materials, such as molten salt fuels.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006985','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112810',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','ID','ID','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112817','Effect of thermal-hydraulic model simplifications on steady-state temperature distributions in the MSRE','MSRE 정상상태 온도분포에 대한 열수력 모델 단순화의 영향','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Long He; Shaoru Zhang; Jiajie Shen; Yu Huang','2026-09-05','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S030645492600705X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112817',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;US','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112804','Effects of applied load on microstructure and corrosion behavior of sensitized 304H stainless steel treated by ultrasonic nanocrystalline surface modification (UNSM)','초음파 나노결정 표면개질(UNSM) 처리된 예민화 304H 스테인리스강의 미세조직 및 부식 거동에 대한 인가 하중의 영향','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jinwook Choi; J.P. Lacy; Carson Lukas; Kasturi Sasidhar; Kumar Sridharan; Hwasung Yeom','2026-09-05','','2027-02','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006924','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112804',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR;US','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112807','A coupled three-dimensional porous-media and drift-flux model for full-domain thermal-hydraulic analysis of steam generators','증기발생기 전 영역 열수력 해석을 위한 3차원 다공성매질-표류유속 연계 모델','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Bo Wang; Yan Zhang; Zhiwei Huang; Yang Yang; Zhengrong Guo; Yukang Liu; Mingyang Li','2026-09-04','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S030645492600695X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112807',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115189','Synthesis and use of potassium copper hexacyanoferrates(II) for the separation of cesium and rubidium from boric acid solutions','붕산 용액으로부터 세슘 및 루비듐 분리를 위한 칼륨 구리 헥사시아노철산염(II)의 합성 및 활용','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Pavel Kůs; Martin Kovář; Šárka Lásková; Semen Gogulin; Thi Minh Do; Petr Večerník; Martin Člupek','2026-09-04','','2026-12','연구논문','핵연료주기·폐기물','Several potassium copper hexacyanoferrate(II) sorbents were prepared and characterized. The adsorption not only of cesium but also of less-explored rubidium was studied on the hexacyanoferrates in the presence of boric acid, simulating a real nuclear wastewater environment. The highest sorption capacity of cesium was 256 mg · g −1 , and that of rubidium was 184 mg · g −1 . The experimental data were fitted to the Langmuir isotherm, pseudo-first and pseudo-second-order kinetic models, and the intra-particle diffusion model. The prepared sorbents demonstrated effective adsorption performance for both Cs and Rb in the presence of boric acid, indicating promising potential for application in nuclear wastewater treatment.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004413','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115189',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CZ','CZ','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104698','A Comparative Molecular Dynamics Study of Pre-existing Point Defect-Induced Tensile Strength Loss in Single Crystal Ni and NiCr','단결정 Ni 및 NiCr에서 기존 점결함에 의한 인장강도 저하의 분자동역학 비교 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Wendong Cui; Junfeng Nie; Junyu Chen; Liyang Yu','2026-09-04','','2026-09','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This study investigates the effects of pre-existing point defects on the tensile behavior of single crystal Ni and Ni 0.8 Cr 0.2 alloy using molecular dynamics simulations. Vacancies, interstitials, and Frenkel pairs were introduced at different concentrations to compare their effects on the tensile response and deformation-induced microstructural evolution of both materials at 300 K, while the temperature effects were examined in representative Ni systems containing 0.5% point defects over 300–1200 K. All three defect types reduce the yield stress and yield strain of both materials, with the weakening effect increasing with defect concentration. At the same concentration, interstitials cause the most severe tensile degradation, followed by Frenkel pairs and vacancies. Atomistic analyses reveal that vacancies mainly promote degradation by acting as precursors for dislocation-loop nucleation and local void evolution, whereas interstitials and Frenkel pairs more readily facilitate the nucleation and growth of interstitial-type dislocation loops, accelerating defect-network formation and deformation twinning. Compared with pure Ni, the Ni 0.8 Cr 0.2 alloy shows smaller strength reduction and delayed defect-assisted microstructural evolution, indicating improved tolerance to point-defect-induced mechanical degradation. For the representative Ni systems containing 0.5% defects, increasing temperature further decreases the yield stress and yield strain, with vacancy-containing samples showing the highest temperature sensitivity.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005863?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104698',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2722501','A Toolkit for Cellular Level Radiation Dosimetry','세포 수준 방사선 선량 측정을 위한 툴킷','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Hiroshi Watabe; Tatsuhiko Sato; Peter K. N. Yu; Dragana Krstic; Dragoslav Nikezic; Kyeong Min Kim; Taiga Yamaya; Naoki Kawachi; Hiroki Tanaka; Zoran Jovanovic; A. K. F. Haque; M. Rafiqul Islam; Gary Tse; Mehrdad Shahmohammadi Beni','2026-09-04','2026-09-04','2026-09-04','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2722501','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2722501',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','JP;HK;RS;KR;BD','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2724782','NuScale SMR Core Verification via MCNPX2.7 and Assessment of Alternative Burnable Absorbers Beyond Natural Gadolinium','MCNPX2.7을 이용한 NuScale SMR 노심 검증 및 천연 가돌리늄 대체 가연성흡수체 평가','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','M. AboBakr Mohamed; Hanan Akhdar; Moamen G. El-Samrah; Mohy Sabry; Tamader Alhazani; Mohamed Y. M. Mohsen; Ahmed Omar','2026-09-04','2026-09-04','2026-09-04','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','The NuScale small modular reactor (SMR) employs burnable absorbers (BAs) to control initial excess reactivity, making the choice of optimal BA materials a key factor in ensuring both safety and fuel utilization efficiency. This study focuses on verifying the NuScale reactor core model and evaluating alternative BAs using MCNPX 2.7. Model verification was performed by benchmarking the results against previously published studies, with agreement demonstrated across critical neutronic parameters, including criticality, power distribution, and fuel burnup.Following this verification, a comparative neutronic evaluation was conducted to examine the performance of alternative BA materials relative to natural gadolinium recommended in the final safety analysis report. Erbium and enriched gadolinium were employed, using the same concentrations as those used for natural gadolinium. Also, enriched gadolinium was utilized at adjusted concentrations, which were half that of natural gadolinium, to attain the same initial excess reactivity as natural gadolinium.The simulation results revealed that enriched gadolinia, at the same concentration of natural gadolinium, effectively suppressed initial excess reactivity at the beginning of cycle and maintained better performance across other neutronic metrics. This makes it a strong candidate for improving reactivity control during the burnup cycle while preserving reactivity coefficients and flux distribution in NuScale SMR cores.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2724782','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2724782',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','EG;BD;US','EG','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106591','Numerical investigation of fretting wear behavior of fuel rod cladding in pressurized water reactors','가압경수로 핵연료 피복관의 프레팅 마모 거동 수치해석','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Haidong Liu; Yansen Liao; Mingxia Liu; Minxing Chen; Quanyao Ren; Deqi Chen','2026-09-04','','2026-11','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003562','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106591',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112771','Comparison of control rod worth and doubling time in the high flux reactor: Static and dynamic Serpent 2 simulations with ENDF/B-VIII.0 and JEFF-3.3','고중성자속 원자로의 제어봉 가치 및 배가시간 비교: ENDF/B-VIII.0 및 JEFF-3.3을 이용한 정적·동적 Serpent 2 모의','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Alan Wichink Kruit; Benjaminas Marcinkevicius; Kornilios Routsonis','2026-09-03','','2027-02','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006596','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112771',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','NL','NL','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112809','Environmental performance of clay-based barriers for radioactive waste disposal: a review with relevance to Portuguese geological materials','방사성폐기물 처분용 점토 기반 방벽의 환경 성능: 포르투갈 지질 재료와 관련한 고찰','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Paula Galego Fernandes; M. Isabel Dias; José Marques','2026-09-03','','2027-02','리뷰·관점','안전·사고·리스크','The environmental performance of clay-based materials is a key factor in the long-term safety of radioactive waste disposal systems. In Portugal, radioactive waste arises exclusively from medical, industrial and research activities and is limited to low- and intermediate-level waste (LLW and ILW), with no production of high-level waste or spent nuclear fuel. This context supports the implementation of near surface disposal facilities and enhanced containment strategies for long-lived low-level waste (L-LLW). This review critically evaluates the suitability of Portuguese clay materials as components of engineered barrier systems, with particular emphasis on radionuclide retention and transport processes. Available geological, mineralogical and physicochemical data are synthesised, including sorption behaviour, diffusion parameters and stability under chemically perturbed conditions. Portuguese clays are typically composed of illite, smectite and kaolinite, with smectite contents locally reaching 40–53%, and exhibit cation exchange capacities in the range of approximately 185–350 μmol·g −1 . Sorption parameters, including frayed edge site capacity and radiocaesium interception potential, indicate strong affinity for radionuclide retention, with distribution coefficients for Cs generally ranging between 10 2 and 10 4 L·kg −1 . Field observations further support these findings, with activity concentrations of 226 Ra (24.6–290 Bq·kg −1 ), 228 Ra (30.1–403 Bq·kg −1 ), 210 Pb (44–368 Bq·kg −1 ) and 137 Cs (1.25–31.2 Bq·kg −1 ), demonstrating the strong association of radionuclides with clay-rich fractions. Diffusion coefficients in compacted clay systems are typically within the range of 10 −11 –10 −13 m 2 ·s −1 , indicating effective retardation of radionuclide migration. Key uncertainties related to irradiation-induced alterations, clay–cement interactions and limitations in reactive transport modelling are critically discussed. Although Portuguese clay materials exhibit properties consistent with engineered barrier requirements, current evidence indicates that further site-specific characterisation is required before their implementation as primary barrier materials. This review provides a scientifically grounded framework to support the development of safe and sustainable radioactive waste disposal strategies based on local geological resources. The review also discusses the expected radiation fields in LLW and ILW near-surface disposal facilities, the physicochemical mechanisms induced by gamma irradiation, and their potential influence on radionuclide sorption and long-term barrier performance.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006973','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112809',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','PT','PT','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112808','Experimental and numerical study on the protective performance of special doors in nuclear power plants subjected to windborne missile impact and long-duration blast loading','비산물 충돌 및 장시간 폭발하중을 받는 원자력발전소 특수문의 방호 성능에 관한 실험 및 수치해석 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Peng Xu; Xunjia Zhuo; He Zhu; De Chen','2026-09-03','','2027-02','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006961','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112808',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112787','Studies of oxygen control in a lead–bismuth eutectic loop','납–비스무트 공정 루프에서의 산소 제어 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Hui Li; Xiaoyang Lun; Wei Mao; Xingyan Zhou; Haicai Lyu; Huiping Zhu; Fang Liu; Ruixian Liang; Xiaobo Li; Fenglei Niu','2026-09-03','','2027-02','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006754','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112787',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115188','Temperature-dependent fretting Wear of zirconium alloy cladding tubes in simulated PWR primary water','모의 PWR 1차계통수 환경에서 지르코늄 합금 피복관의 온도 의존 프레팅 마모','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Quanyao Ren; Kaidong Chen; Zhong Xiao; Zhengyang Li; Sai Li','2026-09-03','','2026-12','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004401','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115188',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104697','A Deep Generative Model and Bayesian Optimization Scheme for PWR First-cycle Loading-Pattern Optimization','PWR 초기노심 장전모형 최적화를 위한 심층생성모델 및 베이지안 최적화 기법','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Junwei Qin; Yuancheng Zhou; Yunzhao Li; Liangzhi Cao; Hongchun Wu','2026-09-03','','2026-09','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','ABSTRACT Pressurized water reactor (PWR) core loading-pattern optimization is a high-dimensional, nonlinear combinatorial problem that suffers from high computational costs due to reliance on a large number of nodal-diffusion and nuclide-depletion calculations. Conventional meta-heuristic algorithms exhibit low sample efficiency, while surrogate models suffer from unreliability caused by extrapolation from its training data. Thus, in this paper, a novel scheme integrating a deep generative model is proposed to address these limitations. Firstly, it utilizes a Variational Autoencoder (VAE) to map the discrete loading patterns into a continuous latent space, transforming the complex discrete optimization into a continuous search problem. Secondly, within this latent space, the Multi-Objective Regionalized Bayesian Optimization (MORBO) algorithm is employed for efficient multi-objective optimization. Thirdly, several enhancement strategies are introduced, including a Gaussian-process feedback loss to guide latent space structuring, a deep metric learning for online fine-tuning, and a Yeo–Johnson transform to correct heteroscedasticity. The scheme is integrated with the automated software Bamboo-Frame and tested on the first-cycle loading-pattern optimization of an M310-type PWR. The method demonstrates its effective convergence and diversity compared to the classical Non-dominated Sorting Genetic Algorithm II (NSGA-II) algorithm. The results validate that this approach effectively balances exploration and exploitation, yielding significantly better Pareto-dominant solutions.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005851?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104697',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104695','A Multi-Objective Approach to Fracture Parameter Estimation for Hydride-Containing SNF Cladding Considering Morphological Variability','형상 변동성을 고려한 수소화물 함유 사용후핵연료 피복관 파괴 변수 추정을 위한 다목적 접근법','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Seyeon Kim; Dahyeon Woo; Youho Lee; Sanghoon Lee','2026-09-03','','2026-09','연구논문','핵연료·재료','This study developed a numerical framework for estimating the parameters of fracture simulation model for SNF cladding under pinch load. A pixel-based finite element modeling was used to construct simulation datasets from metallographic images of hydrogen-charged cladding, enabling explicit consideration of hydride morphology in the evaluation of cladding fracture resistance. However, because the specimens used for the ring compression test (RCT) cannot be identical to those used for microstructural imaging, statistically representative fracture parameters are required. For this purpose, a dual kriging metamodel was constructed to predict the mean crack initiation load and its standard deviation as functions of fracture parameters. Multi-objective optimization (MOO) was then performed to minimize both the deviation of the mean crack initiation load from the experimental value and the prediction uncertainty arising from hydride morphology variability. The optimized fracture parameters were validated using reference and independent verification specimens. The predicted average crack initiation load for the verification specimen differed from the experimental value by only 0.12%. This result supports the capability of the developed model to reproduce the mean crack initiation response for the investigated hydrogen-charged cladding specimen. This approach improves the understanding and prediction of the degradation and fracture behavior of SNF cladding associated with hydride reorientation under pinch load.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005838?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104695',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104696','Residence time distribution of delayed neutron precursors in molten salt reactor shell-tube heat exchangers','용융염원자로 쉘-튜브 열교환기 내 지발중성자 선행핵 체류시간 분포','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Zehang Kang; Xiaoling Liang; Guifeng Zhu; Jintong Cao; Shanjie Lv; Yang Zou; Minghai Li; Rui Yan; Changqing Yu','2026-09-03','','2026-09','연구논문','열수력·유체','Variations in residence time distribution of delayed neutron precursors (DNPs) transported with liquid fuel salt through complex components such as heat exchangers in molten salt reactors cause dynamic changes in effective delayed neutron fraction and localized neutron flux perturbations, thereby compromising reactivity control precision. Focusing on the Molten Salt Reactor Experiment primary heat exchanger, this study constructs a 3D model incorporating U-tube bundles and segmental baffles. Employ a standard k - ε turbulence model coupled with six-group DNP decay equations and simulate DNP transport under pulsed injection conditions via transient solutions of species transport equations. Non-synchronized transit times of DNPs through intricate structures like heat exchangers create disparities in their return timing to the reactor core, directly impacting core reactivity regulation and operational safety. Results demonstrate that the dimensionless RTD curves of DNPs exhibit asymmetric distributions with peaks at > 1, indicating that more than 70% of DNPs have residence times longer than the mean. This study quantitatively characterizes 3D DNP transport mechanisms in heat exchangers, delivering critical datasets and theoretical foundations for formulating molten salt reactor reactivity control strategies and optimizing equivalent 1D heat exchanger models.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S173857332600584X?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104696',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112805','Validation and sensitivity analysis of subchannel modular analysis program','부수로 모듈형 해석 프로그램의 검증 및 민감도 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Weihua Cai; Di Li; Qian Li; Jianchuang Sun; Jincheng Wang','2026-09-02','','2027-02','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006936','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112805',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115174','An analysis of energy needs and seawater-extraction approaches for the integration of primary magnesium production with nuclear power','원자력과 1차 마그네슘 생산의 연계를 위한 에너지 수요 및 해수 추출 방식 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Aidan Rigby; Aaron Wilson','2026-09-02','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','The cost of primary magnesium production is highly dominated by the energy required to produce the metal. This, along with the current geographical concentration of its production, makes the magnesium price vulnerable as energy-production paradigms begin to rapidly change. In this work, four full-integration pathways for the efficient supply of heat and electricity to magnesium production from a nuclear power plant are considered. A production route using electrified metallothermic reduction is compared to a nuclear-heat-integrated electrolytic pathway. It is shown that while the former can achieve a lower primary energy consumption, 293 MJ/kg Mg compared with 301 MJ/kg Mg, the electrolytic pathway can both reduce emissions compared to current production and allow access to magnesium from seawater rather than a mined ore. The emissions from the process are reduced to 2 kgCO2/kg Mg, down from around 32 kgCO2/kg Mg in the Pidgeon process. Beyond energy and emissions, the four pathways considered are also compared to their ability to reduce locational dependence of the production plant and reduce process complexity. This work also highlights future advances in magnesium production with a potential scheme for the efficient extraction of magnesium from seawater with coproduction of desalinated water and the potential of demand-side response from magnesium electrolysis. This is the first work to consider the full integration of primary-metal production using nuclear cogeneration, and it is hoped the study paves the way for the analysis of economic nuclear integration within metal extraction and manufacturing.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004267','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115174',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115195','Laser beam welding properties and microstructural characterization of Kanthal APMT ferritic alloys in the application of accident tolerant fuel cladding','사고저항성핵연료 피복관 적용을 위한 Kanthal APMT 페라이트계 합금의 레이저빔 용접 특성 및 미세조직 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Lin Xiao; Robyn Sloan; Shane Audette; Kaiping Zhang; Peng Peng','2026-09-02','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','Ferritic FeCrAl steel is one of the most promising candidate materials for accident tolerant fuel cladding due to its excellent high temperature mechanical properties, low thermal expansion coefficient, and most importantly, very low void swelling rate under neutron irradiations. Different fuel bundle parts are usually joined together by a variety of joining techniques. These joining processes must allow the cladding to retain acceptable mechanical and accident-tolerant properties. The objective of this study is to assess the feasibility of laser beam welding (LBW) of advanced oxidation-resistant Kanthal APMT Fe-21Cr-5Al-3Mo alloy and to analyze the microstructure of welds. The ultimate tensile strength of FeCrAl weldments reached 78% of the as-received FeCrAl rod, although the ductility of the FeCrAl welds was significantly reduced. Welding-induced cracking and pores were observed in Kanthal APMT alloy welded using high-power laser beam single-side welding technique. Two groups of dispersoids were observed in APMT alloy: smaller particles of Y O, and larger particles of Y-Al-O. Relative abundance of smaller particles can be noted after LBW welding. The particles show slight coarsening, and the number of precipitates increases in comparison with the as-received condition. Based on the results, laser beam welding can be used for joining FeCrAl alloy, but further optimization on welding parameters and post-welding heat treatment are needed to enhance mechanical properties of weldments in the future.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004474','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115195',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115196','Microstructure and mechanical properties of SiC layers in TRISO particles heat-treated in the range of 2500–2800 °C','2500–2800 °C 범위에서 열처리된 TRISO 입자 SiC 층의 미세조직 및 기계적 특성','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Zebing Liu; Bowen Li; Rongzheng Liu; Xu Yang; Malin Liu; Bing Liu; Yaping Tang','2026-09-02','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004486','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115196',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115176','Subgrid-based analytical wall function for steam condensation in the presence of air','공기 존재 하 증기 응축을 위한 부격자 기반 해석적 벽함수','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Shu Soma; Masahiro Ishigaki; Satoshi Abe; Yasuteru Sibamoto','2026-09-02','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004280','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115176',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','JP','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104682','A halophilic bacteria-derived bioadsorbent for efficient uranium removal from alkaline wastewater: Preparation, performance, and mechanism','알칼리성 폐수로부터 효율적 우라늄 제거를 위한 호염성 세균 유래 생체흡착제: 제조, 성능 및 메커니즘','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Guangwen Feng; Huizhong Li; Zhi Chen; Li Li','2026-09-02','','2026-09','연구논문','열수력·유체',': Alkaline uranium-containing wastewater presents a significant remediation challenge due to the formation of stable, anionic uranyl-carbonate complexes that are recalcitrant to conventional treatment methods. Developing efficient, cost-effective, and sustainable biosorbents for uranium removal under alkaline conditions remains a critical need. Building upon previous findings that living Halomonas campaniensis JX-12 efficiently removes uranium from such effluents, this study systematically evaluated the performance and mechanisms of heat-treated, non-living JX-12 biomass for uranium removal under pH conditions of 7.0–9.0 (neutral to alkaline). Batch adsorption experiments demonstrate that the inactivated biomass achieves faster and more efficient uranium removal than its living counterpart at a low uranium concentration of 10 mg/L. Under selected conditions (60 min, 30°C, 180 rpm), removal rate reached 82.80 ± 0.41% (pH 7.0), 81.15 ± 0.34% (pH 8.0), and 77.99 ± 0.24% (pH 9.0). Kinetic modeling indicated that biosorption was dominated by rapid surface complexation, with FT-IR analysis confirming that hydroxyl, amide, carboxyl, amino, and phosphate groups served as the primary binding sites. The adsorption process was determined to be a spontaneous, exothermic, and entropy-driven monolayer chemisorption, wherein electrostatic attraction and ion exchange played secondary roles. Notably, the contributions of amide, amino, and phosphate groups to uranium binding intensified significantly with increasing pH. These findings demonstrate that heat-treated H. campaniensis JX-12 biomass is a robust, efficient, and promising biosorbent, offering a potential low-cost solution for the remediation, using biological processes, of alkaline wastewater that has been contaminated by uranium in nuclear and mining contexts.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S173857332600570X?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104682',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104690','Development and Validation of a System-Code-Oriented Two-Phase Frictional Pressure Drop Correlation Using Locally Updated Properties for Helically Coiled Tubes','국부 갱신 물성치를 이용한 계통코드용 나선형 코일관 2상 마찰압력강하 상관식 개발 및 검증','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Min Young Park; Jong-Hyuk Lee','2026-09-02','','2026-09','연구논문','열수력·유체','Accurate prediction of two-phase frictional pressure drops in HCSGs is important for the thermal-hydraulic analysis of SMRs. Existing correlations are generally developed using fluid properties evaluated at representative operating conditions and may exhibit reduced accuracy when implemented in system codes, where local pressure and fluid properties continuously vary along the flow path. In this study, the applicability of existing two-phase pressure-drop correlations to system-code calculations was first assessed using both standalone calculations and SPACE code simulations. Although the existing correlations showed good agreement with experimental data under standalone conditions, their prediction errors increased significantly after implementation in the SPACE code. Based on these observations, a new two-phase frictional pressure-drop correlation, designated the KAERI correlation, was developed using locally reconstructed pressure and quality distributions derived from experimental databases. Validation against 421 experimental data points showed a MAPE of 12.6%, comparable to those of representative existing correlations. After implementation in the SPACE code, the MAPE increased to 19.1%, corresponding to an increase of 6.5 percentage, which was substantially smaller than those observed for the existing correlations. These results demonstrate that incorporating local pressure-dependent thermophysical properties during correlation development improves consistency between standalone calculations and system-code applications.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005784?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104690',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104689','Development and benchmarking of a novel multitissue anthropomorphic pediatric head phantom against established reference phantoms for CT-based HU-RED calibration in pediatric radiotherapy','소아 방사선치료 CT 기반 HU-RED 교정을 위한 신규 다조직 인체형 소아 두부 팬텀 개발 및 기존 기준 팬텀 대비 벤치마킹','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','H. Sekkat; O. El Mouden; I. Brika; Y. Madkouri; A. Khallouqi; A. Halimi; O. El rhazouani','2026-09-02','','2026-09','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','A novel multitissue anthropomorphic pediatric head phantom was developed for CT-based Hounsfield unit-relative electron density (HU-RED) calibration and preliminarily assessed through controlled retrospective recalculation of pediatric craniospinal irradiation plans. The patient-derived phantom incorporated air cavities and CSF-, eye-, tumor-, brain-, bone-, and teeth-equivalent materials and was benchmarked against EasyCube, CIRS 062, and pediatric ATOM phantoms. Four calibration curves were applied to 20 retrospective CSI datasets while maintaining identical beam geometry, monitor units, dose grid, and calculation settings. Target and organ-at-risk dosimetry, gamma-index agreement, dose-difference maps, and eight line-dose profiles were evaluated. With the novel curve, mean PTV D95, D2, Dmean, and V95% were 30.92 ± 5.65 Gy, 32.88 ± 6.01 Gy, 31.54 ± 5.76 Gy, and 99.40 ± 0.41%, respectively. All PTV endpoints met predefined equivalence margins. Most organ-at-risk endpoints were also equivalent, with non-equivalence limited to the thoracic spinal cord versus EasyCube and kidneys versus EasyCube/CIRS 062. Global and local gamma passing rates were 99.55-99.75% and 98.75-99.05%, respectively, using 2%/3 mm. Profile MAE was 0.56-0.87%, with Pearson r values of 0.9985-0.9993. The phantom provided an anatomically realistic head-protocol HU-RED calibration platform, but the findings do not constitute physical dosimetric validation or delivered-dose verification.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005772?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104689',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','MA','MA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104694','Sparse Measurement-Based Three-Dimensional Radiation Field Reconstruction Using Physics-informed Neural Network','물리정보신경망을 이용한 희소 측정 기반 3차원 방사선장 재구성','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Biyang Mao; Xingyu Luo; Qingqing Wen; Yunlei Guo; Jianwen Huo','2026-09-02','','2026-09','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Accurate reconstruction of radiation dose fields is essential for nuclear facility monitoring and radiation protection. Conventional 3D gamma field reconstruction methods rely on dense, high-quality measurements and often suffer from severe distortions under sparse and non-uniform sampling due to insufficient physical constraints. To address this limitation, a physics-informed neural network (PINN) based sparse reconstruction method is proposed. The approach integrates physical laws of radiation transport into the learning process, where a Kriging-interpolated field provides prior knowledge, the proxy residuals of energy conservation are combined with other physical constraints to form a hybrid loss function. This framework enables a shift from purely data-driven reconstruction to physics-guided inference. The method is validated using Geant4-simulated datasets with approximately 1,000 randomly sampled measurement points (0.2% of the total 500,000 voxels). Results show that the proposed approach achieves mean relative errors of 14% (without shielding) and 19% (with shielding), reducing errors by approximately 50% compared with Kriging and backpropagation neural network(BPNN). Source localization errors are below 0.05 m and 0.12 m, respectively. The proposed method significantly enhances reconstruction accuracy, physical plausibility, and applicability in complex shielded environments.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005826?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104694',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/s0306-4549(26)00686-9','Editorial Board','편집위원회','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-09-01','','2026-12','편집물','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006869','https://doi.org/10.1016/s0306-4549(26)00686-9',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115167','Capabilities and limitations in the computational modelling of homogeneous flow regimes in a pilot-scale bubble column with focus on lateral lift force','파일럿 규모 기포탑 균질 유동영역 전산 모델링의 능력과 한계: 횡방향 양력을 중심으로','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Nicolò Varallo; Riccardo Manfrè; Riccardo Mereu; Giorgio Besagni; Benjamin Krull; Fabian Schlegel; Dirk Lucas','2026-09-01','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S002954932600419X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115167',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IT;DE','IT','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/s0029-5493(26)00436-x','Editorial Board','편집위원회','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-09-01','','2026-11','편집물','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S002954932600436X','https://doi.org/10.1016/s0029-5493(26)00436-x',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104678','Impact of correcting beam hardening and detector response function in photon-counting X-ray imaging when using anti-coincidence mode','반동시계수 모드 사용 시 광자계수 X선 영상에서 빔 경화 및 검출기 응답함수 보정의 영향','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Hiroaki Hayashi; Rina Nishigami; Daiki Kobayashi; Takuya Kasue; Natsumi Kimoto; Takashi Asahara','2026-09-01','','2027-01','연구논문','핵연료·재료','X-ray imaging using photon-counting detectors (PCDs) allows for the calculation of quantitative images such as the effective atomic number ( 𝑍 e f f ). However, physical phenomena such as characteristic X-ray emission and charge sharing can cause incomplete total absorption events during signal generation, which reduces the accuracy of X-ray penetration analysis. To solve the problem, an anti-coincidence mode (ACM) has been developed, but complete correction has not been established. We aimed to investigate the accuracy of 𝑍 e f f image when the proposed software-based corrections, namely beam hardening and response function corrections, are added to the hardware-based correction of the ACM. The response function was calculated using the Monte-Carlo simulation code. In a simulation study, we analyzed a phantom composed of virtual materials with 𝑍 e f f values of 4–16. While sufficient accuracy cannot be achieved by applying only the ACM, it was demonstrated that low-noise 𝑍 e f f images can be obtained by applying our correction. Furthermore, it was demonstrated that 𝑍 e f f images of food samples can be generated by using actual non-destructive testing equipment with a 10 m/min transportation speed. In conclusion, our correction procedure can maximize the performance of PCDs, and our findings are essential for promoting imaging techniques concerning quantitative images.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005668','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104678',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','JP','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104688','Local structure and early-stage aggregation behavior of Mo in LiF-BeF2-UF4-ZrF4 molten salts','LiF-BeF2-UF4-ZrF4 용융염에서 Mo의 국부 구조 및 초기 응집 거동','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Haiyang Gao; Linbing Jiang; Wenguan Liu; Rui Yan; Yang Zou; Guifeng Zhu','2026-09-01','','2026-09','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Redox-dependent speciation and transport of molybdenum (Mo) in actinide-bearing fluoride melts strongly influence fission-product behavior in molten-salt reactors, yet their atomistic origins remain unclear. Here, on-the-fly machine-learning molecular dynamics simulations were performed to investigate the local structure and early-stage aggregation behavior of Mo in LiF-BeF 2 -UF 4 -ZrF 4 molten salt at 923 K under systematically varied fluorine stoichiometries. For isolated Mo, increasing fluorination shortens the Mo-F distance, increases both the coordination number and the positive effective Bader charge of Mo, and significantly suppresses diffusivity. In contrast, U- and especially Zr-centered fluoride coordination environments remain relatively stable and mainly act as the multicomponent host matrix. In two-Mo systems, direct Mo-Mo bonding persists under fluorine-deficient and moderately fluorinated conditions, but disappears at high fluorination; the most compact dimer is observed under the neutral condition. In four-Mo systems, aggregation evolves from a compact U/Zr-associated cluster to a Mo-dominated compact cluster, partial pairing, and finally complete dispersion with increasing fluorination. Separate auxiliary simulations involving Nb and Te as representative noble-metal fission products were further performed to compare heteroatomic association. These results provide an atomistic basis for understanding redox-controlled fission-product speciation, early-stage aggregation, and mobility in reactor-relevant fluoride salts.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005760?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104688',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2684826','Cyberattack Scenario Development Targeting Nuclear Power Plants Using I&amp;C Focused System Dynamics','계측제어 중심 시스템 다이내믹스를 이용한 원자력발전소 대상 사이버공격 시나리오 개발','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Stephen Yoo; Fan Zhang','2026-09-01','2026-09-01','2026-09-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','The increasing digitalization of nuclear power plant instrumentation and control (I&C) systems has introduced new cyber-induced risk pathways that are not adequately captured by traditional, network-centric cybersecurity analyses. In particular, the malicious manipulation of digital control logic or sensor signals can propagate through plant feedback structures and manifest as delayed or indirect physical consequences.This work proposes a consequence-oriented framework for cyberattack scenario development using an I&C-focused system dynamics (SD) modeling approach. Rather than emphasizing intrusion mechanisms or network architectures, the framework concentrates on the physical and digital I&C layers, where cyber actions translate into measurable system behavior. The methodology systematically transforms legacy reactor documentation into an executable SD model, while the Molten Salt Reactor Experiment (MSRE) is used as a representative case study due to the availability of publicly accessible design and operational documentation.A set of representative scenarios is evaluated for validation and verification purposes by comparing them with an existing MSRE MELCOR input deck. These scenarios include steady-state operation, drain tank valve opening to represent both cyber-physical manipulations and coolant pump speed perturbations covering reduced, zero, and increased flow conditions to depict both cyber-physical manipulations and cyber-specific attacks.The results demonstrate that the SD model captures the dominant causal relationships, response timing, and trend behavior observed in MELCOR simulations, despite differences in the transient resolution, numerical smoothness, and value differences. The difference is caused by the confidential regions not publicly available for the MSRE documents, resulting in an incomplete MSRE I&C SD model. Nevertheless, the proposed framework provides a practical and extensible foundation for consequence-driven nuclear cybersecurity assessments and supports future integration with automated model generation techniques.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2684826','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2684826',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2721226','Simulation-Based Artificial Intelligence Framework for Assessing Environmental Impacts of Radioactive Releases from Nuclear Facilities: A Real-World Case Study','원자력시설 방사성물질 방출의 환경영향 평가를 위한 모의 기반 인공지능 프레임워크: 실제 사례 연구','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Navid Delgarm; Saeed Bordekhouni; Ali Haghighi Shad; Kiana Haghighi Shad; Kiarash Haghighi Shad; Saeed Delgarm','2026-09-01','2026-09-01','2026-09-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This research presents a novel framework leveraging artificial intelligence for the accurate estimation of radiation doses resulting from the release of radioactive materials at nuclear facilities. The methodology couples HOTSPOT with an Adaptive Neuro-Fuzzy Inference System (ANFIS) developed in MATLAB, enabling rapid and sophisticated predictions of population exposure doses arising from atmospheric radionuclide dispersion. The framework is validated through a case study of hypothetical failure scenarios of the radioactive waste (radwaste) system at the Bushehr Nuclear Power Plant (BNPP), Iran, including: (I) equipment leakage or malfunction in the gaseous radwaste system, (II) leakage or rupture of liquid radwaste storage tanks, and (III) simultaneous failure of both gaseous and liquid subsystems, analyzing the spatial distribution of radionuclide concentrations at various distances from the emission source. Dose estimations for critical human organs, including the whole-body, thyroid, and lungs, are derived using both HOTSPOT simulations and the trained ANFIS model. Comparative analysis demonstrates excellent agreement between ANFIS predictions and HOTSPOT results, with mean absolute percentage errors below 0.01 and coefficients of determination exceeding 0.98 across all scenarios, alongside a 97% reduction in computational time relative to full deterministic simulations. In addition, the final ANFIS–HOTSPOT model was evaluated and validated using real monitored data under normal operation conditions, confirming its predictive accuracy in routine facility operations. Results indicate that, under both hypothetical accident scenarios and normal operation, the maximum annual effective dose to the public remains well below regulatory limits (0.05 mSv/year), which is substantially lower than the regulatory thresholds established by the International Commission on Radiological Protection (ICRP) and the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA). Overall, the developed framework is highly scalable and adaptable, providing an efficient and reliable tool for modeling radionuclide transport and assessing radiological doses across all exposure pathways, supporting both operational safety and emergency preparedness.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2721226','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2721226',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IR','IR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2712103','The Effect of Baffle Position on the Distribution Characteristics of Aerosol Produced from Solution Ejection','용액 분출로 생성된 에어로졸의 분포 특성에 대한 배플 위치의 영향','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Zhi Zhang; Yi-Ren Lian; Shu-Tang Sun; Ye-Ming Zhu; Jiang-Yu Niu; Jin Yan; Shi-Qi Zhang; Hao-Ming Dou; Hong-Chao Sun; Guo-Qiang Li; Yan-Long Qi','2026-09-01','2026-09-01','2026-09-01','연구논문','핵연료·재료','A simulation experimental equipment with baffles was designed based on the phenomena of solution leakage in nuclear fuel cycle facilities. The distribution characteristics of aerosol produced from solution jetting at different baffle positions was studied with help of an electrical low-pressure impactor and a laser particle size analyzer. Analysis on experimental data that compared large particles (0.040–10.000 μm) with small particles (0.006–0.108 μm) revealed that the number concentration curves of large particles reached equilibrium relatively quickly. The number of aerosol particles gradually decreased with the increase in distance from baffle to jet pipe; this may be because the farther the baffle was from the jet pipe, the more energy the ejected solution lost. Fewer droplets of the solution were broken up after impacting the baffle, and more large droplets were formed. The increase in distance from baffle to jet pipe resulted in the decrease in volume concentration of large particles within the size range of 1.000 to 4.400 μm. The maximum particle size of aerosol reduced to 68.13 μm at 80 cm of the distance from baffle to jet pipe. Finally, the aerosol release fraction (ARF) of aerosol was analyzed. The ARF of aerosol at 40 cm and 60 cm distance from baffle to jet pipe was about 7.0 × 10−5, which was was approximately one order of magnitude larger than that at 20 cm and 80 cm. This result was consistent with a large mass concentration of aerosol at the same condition.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712103','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712103',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106579','Development of a high-Reynolds k–ω–kθ–ϵθ model and a hybrid-resolution simulation method for lead–bismuth-eutectic loops','납-비스무트 공정 루프를 위한 고레이놀즈수 k–ω–kθ–ϵθ 모델 및 혼합 해상도 모의 방법 개발','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Qingji Su; Wanai Li; Weifu Lin; Meilan Chen','2026-09-01','','2026-11','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003446','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106579',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112793','AI-powered spectral analysis for nuclear non-proliferation to enhance operational readiness of safeguards technologies','안전조치 기술의 운용 준비태세 강화를 위한 핵비확산용 AI 기반 스펙트럼 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Muhammad Zubair; Mariam Obaid; Jameel-Un Nabi; Abdul Kabir','2026-08-31','','2027-02','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S030645492600681X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112793',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','AE;PK','AE','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112749','Development of a neutronics–thermal–fluid–structure coupling methodology for performance analysis of U-50Zr helical cruciform fuel','U-50Zr 나선형 십자형 핵연료 성능해석을 위한 중성자–열–유체–구조 연계 방법론 개발','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jianfeng Xu; Qufei Song; Tenglong Cong; Hui Guo; Hanyang Gu','2026-08-31','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006377','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112749',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112788','Fuel-form effects on normal-operation and LOCA performance of U–ZrH and MOX fuel rods in the MARVEL microreactor','MARVEL 초소형원자로에서 U–ZrH 및 MOX 핵연료봉의 정상운전 및 LOCA 성능에 대한 핵연료 형태의 영향','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Yuze Tan; Rong Liu','2026-08-31','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006766','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112788',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112780','Performance mechanism and reliable operating regime of high-temperature sodium heat pipes with a large aspect ratio for MHPRs','MHPR용 대종횡비 고온 소듐 히트파이프의 성능 메커니즘 및 신뢰 운전 영역','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Kun Li; Yan Yan; Xujia Wang; Quan Zhou; Kai Zhang; Qiming Men; Shengyao Jiang; Nan Gui','2026-08-31','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006687','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112780',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112785','Research on system operation control method for SMRs based on main pump health assessment','주냉각재펌프 건전성 평가 기반 SMR 계통 운전제어 방법 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Kai Wang; Zhi Chen; Pengcheng Yang; Yaowu Li; Yifan Jian; Xuecen Zhao','2026-08-31','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006730','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112785',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115178','Experimental study on the influence of epoxy patterns of bi-conductive surfaces on Pool boiling','이중 전도성 표면의 에폭시 패턴이 풀비등에 미치는 영향에 관한 실험 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Longchang Tang; Wei Xu; Yan Liu; Xiaojing Liu','2026-08-31','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004309','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115178',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115172','Nodal Expansion Method in the Fuel associated with an Analytical Solution in the Reflector','반사체 해석해와 연계한 핵연료 영역 노달 전개법','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Flamarion da Silva Santos; Adilson Costa da Silva; Fernando Carvalho da Silva','2026-08-31','','2026-12','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004243','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115172',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','BR','BR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104687','An Agentic Multimodal RAG Framework for Enhancing Nuclear Regulatory Review: Preserving Structural Integrity of Safety Analysis Reports','원자력 규제심사 고도화를 위한 에이전트형 멀티모달 RAG 프레임워크: 안전성분석보고서의 구조적 무결성 보존','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Bokyeong Kim; Yonggyun Yu','2026-08-31','','2026-08','리뷰·관점','안전·사고·리스크','Final Safety Analysis Reports (FSARs) distribute the evidence for a single answer across narrative text, engineering tables, and system diagrams, and flattening this evidence into generic text chunks can obscure the structure needed to verify an answer. We propose an agentic multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) framework that decomposes FSAR pages into layout-aware segments, stores modality-labeled text, table, and image evidence for agent-specific retrieval, and routes each query to specialist agents before generating a cited answer. The framework is evaluated on a 200-question FSAR question-answering benchmark with questions labeled as text, table, image, or composite. Under a fixed generation backbone, we compare the framework with text-centric RAG, agentic RAG, and multimodal RAG baselines and with component ablations. The proposed framework achieves the highest overall accuracy of 69.0%, exceeding Unified Multimodal RAG by 6.5 percentage points and Self-RAG by 20.0 points, the highest segment-level retrieval hit rate of 77.5% among segment-indexed systems, and the lowest hallucination rate of 0.10. Removing the table or image agent degrades modality-specific and composite performance, and remaining errors concentrate in expression mismatch, synthesis error, and retrieval miss. These results suggest that modality-specific evidence processing can improve evidence grounding for FSAR question answering within the evaluated setting.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005759?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104687',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104686','Migration of pores and grain boundaries in uranium dioxide driven by temperature gradient: A phase-field simulation','온도구배에 의한 이산화우라늄 내 기공 및 결정립계 이동: 상장(phase-field) 모의','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Lipan Zhu; Haoxue Wang; Yongxiao La; Yuxuan Liao; Jinli Cao; Xuezhi Wu; Wenbo Liu','2026-08-31','','2026-08','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005747?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104686',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104683','PSA-Informed Design Implications of Fail-Safe Passive Safety Systems for Advanced Reactors','차세대 원자로의 고장 시 안전(fail-safe) 피동안전계통에 대한 PSA 정보 활용 설계 시사점','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Sung-Min Shin; Kibeom Son; Jin Hee Park; Jong Woo Park','2026-08-31','','2026-08','연구논문','열수력·유체','Advanced reactors increasingly employ passive safety systems (PSSs) with fail-safe actuation, in which key valves are held by continuous energization and move to predefined positions upon de-energization. Loss of the holding power, however, can also cause spurious actuation, so prevention features are often added. A review of large-plant and SMR designs shows such features appear only where unintended actuation discharges primary coolant, indicating that the suitability of a fail-safe concept depends on the function it serves. This study applies probabilistic safety assessment (PSA) to an example plant to examine how the resulting risk is redistributed. Component-level attributes, including the fail-safe designation itself, cannot be verified at the component level alone, since suppressing spurious operation adds actuation conditions, failure modes, and operator actions that raise failure on demand. A refinement example quantifies the trade-off: a prevention feature cut the spurious-operation contribution by about 73% but raised the demand-failure contribution, giving only an 8% net reduction in core damage frequency, whereas later simplification achieved 24%. A PSA-informed design decision framework is therefore proposed, in which both perspectives are evaluated iteratively and a design is finalized only when total plant-level risk is lowest among candidates. Six representative design cases are also generalized.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005711?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104683',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106551','Enhanced 3D modeling of single- and two-phase turbulent mixing in interconnected sub-channels through advanced diffusion and dispersion terms','고급 확산·분산항을 통한 상호연결 부수로 내 단상 및 2상 난류혼합의 향상된 3차원 모델링','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Filippo Arlotti; Xavier Manchon; Jorge Perez-Manes; Nathalie Seiler; Nicolas Rimbert; Jean-Marc Labit; Stéphane Mimouni','2026-08-31','','2026-11','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003161','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106551',1,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106590','Numerical investigation of CRUD deposit effects on subcooled boiling in a PWR fuel rod bundle','PWR 핵연료봉 다발에서 CRUD 침적물이 과냉비등에 미치는 영향 수치해석','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Yandong Hou; Hua Huang; Haoran Cheng; Chuntian Gao; Bowen Chen; Chao Zhang; Yan Xiang','2026-08-31','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003550','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106590',0,'2026-09-06','2026-09-07','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;SE','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112777','On the reported critical-heat-flux enhancement of helical fuel: comparison basis, correction-factor consistency, and look-up-table uncertainty','나선형 핵연료의 임계열유속 향상 보고에 대한 고찰: 비교 기준, 보정계수 일관성 및 룩업테이블 불확실성','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Hamza Zeghari','2026-08-29','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006651','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112777',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115177','Boiling flow simulation of a SIRIUS-3D full fuel assembly using an Eulerian two-fluid approach','오일러리안 2유체 접근법을 이용한 SIRIUS-3D 전체 핵연료집합체의 비등 유동 모의','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Yohei Sato; Annika Hämmer; Daniel Vlček; Bojan Ničeno','2026-08-29','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','A three-dimensional boiling-flow simulation method was developed within the Eulerian two-fluid computational fluid dynamics framework for boiling water reactor (BWR) fuel assemblies. The method extends the previously developed two-dimensional axisymmetric PSI-CTU boiling model, originally formulated for the DEBORA experiment, to fully three-dimensional geometries and water boiling conditions at 72 bar . A key feature of the model is the coupling of a void-fraction-dependent bubble lift-force model with a population balance model (PBM) employing twenty bubble-size bins and tuned coalescence and breakup models. Different combinations of nucleation site density and bubble departure diameter models were employed for the DEBORA and SIRIUS-3D simulations because of the different working fluids. The model was implemented in Ansys Fluent through user-defined functions. The three-dimensional model was first verified through simulations of selected DEBORA experiments using several mesh configurations, including structured and polyhedral meshes. Good agreement with the reference 2D axisymmetric simulations and experimental data was obtained for all meshes except for the excessively coarse meshes. The model was then applied to the SIRIUS-3D experiment, which represents a full-length BWR fuel assembly. Simulations reproduced the overall void-fraction distributions measured by X-ray tomography, including higher void fractions near heated rods and lower void fractions near non-heated rods. Sensitivity analysis showed that tuning the lift-force-model parameter improved agreement in the intermediate elevation range. Remaining discrepancies were attributed to limitations in the prediction of cross-sectional flow and omission of spacer grids. The computed wall heat-flux partitioning behavior and the bubble-size distributions predicted by the PBM were also investigated.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004292','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115177',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104668','SACCL: A reinforcement learning-based approach for radiation source localization','SACCL: 강화학습 기반 방사선원 위치 추정 기법','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Xiaolu Li; Jianwen Huo; Mingrun Ling; Yunlei Guo; Xulin Hu','2026-08-29','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005565','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104668',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106589','AI-driven modeling of complex condensation heat transfer in the presence of non-condensable gases for enhanced thermal system safety','열계통 안전성 향상을 위한 비응축성 기체 존재 하 복합 응축 열전달의 AI 기반 모델링','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Rehan Zubair Khalid; Farooq Ahmad; Usman Zubair; Ibrahim A. Altuwair; Atta Ullah','2026-08-29','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003549','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106589',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','PK;SA','PK','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106585','Composition stratification characteristics study of helium-xenon mixture gas in the horizontal circular heated pipe','수평 원형 가열관 내 헬륨-제논 혼합기체의 조성 성층 특성 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Lin Xie; Kewei Ning; Xiaojian Ge; Hui Bao; Junrui Liu; Sichao Tan; Fulong Zhao; Ping Song; Ruifeng Tian','2026-08-29','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003501','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106585',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112768','Flow–induced vibration response of the helical cruciform fuel rod coupled the TMM and MSM','TMM과 MSM을 연계한 나선형 십자형 핵연료봉의 유동유발진동 응답','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Hongyi Li; Hongyu Yang; Menghui Fang; Guangyun Min; Naibin Jiang','2026-08-28','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006560','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112768',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112770','Parametric assessment of submerged horizontal plates to mitigate tsunami-like wave overtopping at vertical coastal revetments','수직 호안에서 쓰나미성 파랑 월파 저감을 위한 수중 수평판의 매개변수 평가','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Hyeon-Jeong Kim; Seonyong Choi; Taegeon Hwang; Byung-Il Min; Woo-Dong Lee','2026-08-28','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006584','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112770',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112784','Physics-informed reduced-order modeling for rapid flow-field reconstruction in a lead-cooled fast-reactor pump','납냉각 고속로 펌프 내 신속 유동장 재구성을 위한 물리정보 축소차수 모델링','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Yiwen Guo; Liangxing Li; Jiabin Gui; Weimin Ma; Jingwen Jia; Junpeng Han','2026-08-28','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006729','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112784',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;SE','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104681','Development and Evaluation of an Integrated Drying and Multi-stage Incineration Process for Animal Carcass Waste Volume Reduction: Implications for Radioactive Waste Management','동물 사체 폐기물 감용을 위한 건조 및 다단 소각 통합 공정 개발 및 평가: 방사성폐기물 관리에 대한 시사점','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Sang-Jun Han; Bo-Gil Kim; Jun-Seok Kim; Seung-Gwan Han','2026-08-28','','2026-08','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Radioactive animal carcass waste combines high moisture, biological instability, and radiological hazard. As preliminary verification prior to radioactive application, an integrated drying–multi-stage incineration process was developed and evaluated using non-radioactive surrogate carcasses. Mouse and rat samples dried under a stepwise descending profile (130 → 120 → 110°C) reached moisture contents below the Korea Radioactive Waste Agency (KORAD) acceptance criterion of 40% within one day. Dried samples were incinerated in a nitrogen atmosphere. A single-ramp condition (≤800°C) gave incomplete combustion with tar and condensable organics, whereas a multi-stage ramp (200–1100°C) achieved complete combustion and a stable inorganic ash. Volume reduction reached 96.7–96.9% (mouse) and 95.5–95.7% (rat), exceeding the KORAD target of 90%. Ash analysis indicated near-complete organic decomposition (C: 1.04 mg kg -1 ; N, H, O: <0.05 mg kg -1 ), and regulated heavy metals were below detection limits in ash and off-gas capture solutions, suggesting limited environmental impact. Because hazardous-waste classification depends on leachable rather than total metals, TCLP testing and direct off-gas measurement remain future tasks. These results represent an important preliminary step toward, rather than direct validation of, treating actual radioactive carcass waste.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005693?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104681',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2691680','Introduction: Sociotechnical Research on Nuclear Energy: A Retrospective and an Agenda for Field-Building','서론: 원자력 에너지의 사회기술적 연구 – 회고와 분야 구축을 위한 의제','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Aditi Verma; Todd Allen; Sebastian Javier Lecha; Randall Fowler; Sungyeol Choi; Margot Hurlbert; Lisa Marshall; Teva Meyer; Katie Snyder; Siegfried Evens','2026-08-28','2026-08-28','2026-08-28','편집물','설계·운전·경제','I. Many of nuclear energy’s most significant challenges can be thought of as wicked problems [1,2]. Wicked problems, by their very nature, are difficult to define because they may be framed differe...','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2691680','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2691680',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US;KR;CA;FR;GB','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2716593','Irradiation Effects on Additively Manufactured Metallic Alloys: Recent Progress and Future Perspectives','적층제조 금속 합금의 조사 효과: 최근 연구 동향 및 향후 전망','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Eva Homberger; Indrajit Charit','2026-08-28','2026-08-28','2026-08-28','리뷰·관점','열수력·유체','Additive manufacturing (AM) processes fabricate components from a three-dimensional model through the sequential layering of material. AM is an emerging manufacturing method that shortens production time, reduces material waste, rapidly creates one-off parts, and improves overall efficiency in the design and fabrication process. These benefits make AM appealing for use in many industries, including the nuclear energy field. While the potential of AM materials is attractive, an understanding of the irradiation behavior of these materials must be established, especially in comparison to conventionally manufactured materials currently in service. In AM alloy materials, repeated thermal cycles and highly ordered depositions create microstructures that deviate from those expected for conventionally manufactured components. Such characteristic microstructures include the development of subgrain cell structures, pores, and anisotropic grains; these features in turn affect the material properties and behavior under irradiation. While the number of irradiation studies in this area is limited, this review attempts to summarize the findings of these studies in a succinct manner and identify areas for future meaningful research.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2716593','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2716593',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2716594','NeuG4: Developing a Geant4-Based Monte Carlo Framework for Nuclear Reactor Analysis','NeuG4: 원자로 해석을 위한 Geant4 기반 몬테카를로 프레임워크 개발','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Roshlan Rahman Dipto','2026-08-28','2026-08-28','2026-08-28','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','We developed a Geant4 (Geometry and Tracking 4)–based Monte Carlo framework, NeuG4 (Neutronics with Geant4), primarily to calculate the k-eigenvalue for fissile materials of spherical geometry. Geant4 is a C++–based Monte Carlo simulation toolkit. Using Geant4, NeuG4 was programmed to determine the effective multiplication factor, neutron flux spectrum and distribution, depletion analysis, and Shannon entropy convergence test using continuous-energy cross sections provided by the Geant4 nuclear data library. Hypothetical uranium spheres with varying radii, enrichment levels, and criticality conditions were used to demonstrate the proposed approach. The performance of NeuG4 for criticality evaluations was compared with the neutron transport code OpenMC.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2716594','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2716594',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','BD','BD','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112667','A digital-twin of the MSRE: Finite-difference modeling and host-mediated dual-FPGA real-time emulation','MSRE 디지털트윈: 유한차분 모델링 및 호스트 매개 이중 FPGA 실시간 에뮬레이션','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Yuyao Wang; Yulin Wang; Weiran Chen; Venkata Dinavahi','2026-08-27','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','The Molten-Salt Reactor Experiment (MSRE) remains a central reference for flowing-fuel reactor dynamics, in which delayed-neutron precursor circulation, neutronic feedback, salt–graphite heat transfer, and heat-removal dynamics are tightly coupled. These features are also important for digital-twin and hardware-in-the-loop studies of advanced reactor systems. A remaining gap is the lack of a reproducible MSRE-scale model that retains explicit axial precursor transport and temperature-feedback physics while remaining simple enough for deterministic host–FPGA real-time emulation. High-fidelity multiphysics models are difficult to schedule at real-time rates, whereas many reduced models suppress the transport-delay structure that makes flowing-fuel reactors distinctive. This work develops a one-dimensional two-group finite-difference MSRE model coupled to six-group precursor advection, external-loop decay, fuel-salt/graphite thermal feedback through temperature-dependent cross sections, heat exchangers, and a hypothetical ideal-gas Brayton balance-of-plant workload. The offline equations are advanced by a method-of-lines solver with upwind advection, centered diffusion, and RK4 time integration. For emulation, the spatial state is mapped to split core and BOP HLS kernels on two Xilinx® VCU118-class FPGA boards, while a host runtime broker manages physical-delay boundary channels and JTAG–AXI launches without direct board-to-board communication. The model is assessed using analytical plug-flow code verification, feedback-coefficient calibration, a delayed-source circulation-loss surrogate comparison, reduced-order reactivity-step demonstrations, CPU split-proxy checks, and board-level readback tests. The circulation-loss surrogate gives 200.38 pcm versus the MSRE benchmark value of 212 ± 6 pcm, and calibrated feedback coefficients match adopted targets within 0.025 pcm/K. For − 75 , − 600 , and − 2400 pcm insertions at Δ t = 0.25 s, the first resolved power ratios are 0.659, 0.174, and 0.049. In the N z = 200 R12 hardware case, the host-mediated dual-FPGA path achieves 3.043 ms per 1 s outer step, corresponding to 329 × faster-than-real-time execution. All simulation and emulation code and data are available at https://github.com/yuyao-wang/MSRE-RT .','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926005554','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112667',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112774','Impact of incorporating thorium in MTR fuel designs – An evaluation of SAFARI-1 using OSCAR-5','MTR 핵연료 설계에 토륨 도입의 영향 – OSCAR-5를 이용한 SAFARI-1 평가','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Willard S. Maraire; Rian H. Prinsloo; Frik Van Niekerk; Eric M. Chinaka; Marina H. Du Toit','2026-08-27','','2027-01','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006626','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112774',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','ZA','ZA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112772','Understanding low-frequency neutron noise: Evidence of flow shifting in KWU reactors and separation of global and local components','저주파 중성자 잡음의 이해: KWU 원자로의 유동 편향 증거 및 전역·국부 성분 분리','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','L.A. Torres; C. Montalvo; A. García-Berrocal','2026-08-27','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Low-frequency neutron noise below 1 Hz has been repeatedly observed in pressurised water reactors (PWRs) of KWU design, although its physical origin remains only partially understood. Early studies suggested that this frequency range arises from the superposition of a global component and a local component. In this work, neutron-noise measurements from a commercial KWU three-loop PWR are analysed combining conventional spectral techniques and Operational Modal Analysis (OMA) applied to neutron detectors and core-exit thermocouples. The results identify two dominant spatial contributions below 1 Hz. The first exhibits coherent axial behaviour with an approximately linear phase progression along the coolant flow direction, consistent with global thermohydraulic transport. The second displays radial out-of-phase regions and an axial dipole structure, indicating spatially non-uniform core dynamics. Two characteristic spectral contributions, centred near 0.1 Hz and 0.7 Hz, show different spatial distributions and fuel-cycle evolutions. Comparison with thermocouple signals reveals similar radial phase asymmetries, supporting the interpretation that the local component is associated with slow coolant-flow redistributions (flow shifting). Through moderator-temperature feedback, these hydraulic perturbations generate structured neutron-noise fluctuations. The findings indicate a dual interpretation of neutron noise below 1 Hz in KWU reactors as the coexistence of global thermal transport and local hydraulic redistribution processes, and demonstrate the usefulness of OMA for reactor diagnostics.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006602','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112772',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','ES','ES','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115116','Transient simulations of heat exchangers in a nuclear power plant by reduced order models','축소차수 모델을 이용한 원자력발전소 열교환기의 과도 모의','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','C. Allery; M.A. Balin; C. Beghein; J. Marie; V. Melot','2026-08-27','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326003687','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115116',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','FR','FR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104680','Development of a PCB-Based Bucking Rotating Coil System for Quadrupole Magnets in Korea-4GSR','Korea-4GSR 사중극 전자석용 PCB 기반 버킹 회전코일 시스템 개발','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Y.G. Choi; D.E. Kim; G. Hahn; Y.G. Jung; W.W. Lee; B.J. Kim; S.H. Ahn; M.J. Kim','2026-08-27','','2026-08','연구논문','방사선·계측','A PCB-based bucking rotating coil system was developed for high-precision measurements of small-aperture quadrupole magnets in the Korea Fourth-Generation Synchrotron Radiation Source (4GSR). The sensor consists of a 14-layer PCB with 84-turn main coils and 126-turn compensation coils, providing effective suppression of the main quadrupole component. The system was evaluated using a prototype Q31 quadrupole magnet. After applying a 40 μm geometric offset correction, the difference between the rotating-coil and Hall-probe measurements was reduced from 2.5% to 0.003%, with a repeatability better than 7.0 × 10 -5 . The normalized sextupole and allowed harmonic components were measured as B 3 /B 2 = 2.82 × 10 -3 and B 6 /B 2 = 4.55 × 10 -4 in non-bucking mode, and were reduced to 3.52 × 10 -4 and 7.46 × 10 -5 in bucking mode. The measured bucking ratio agreed well with the geometrical bucking ratio of 652. The results demonstrate that the developed system provides accurate and repeatable harmonic measurements for quality control of 4GSR quadrupole magnets.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005681?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104680',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2713829','Predictions of the Maneuvers of Spent Fuel Elements in a Nuclear Power Plant to a Dry Storage Unit Using Artificial Intelligence','인공지능을 이용한 원자력발전소 사용후핵연료 요소의 건식저장 설비 이송 작업 예측','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Rafaela da Silva Andrade Freitas; Pedro Luiz da Cruz Saldanha; Paulo Fernando Frutuoso e Melo; Andressa S. Nicolau','2026-08-27','2026-08-27','2026-08-27','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Transfer operations of irradiated fuel elements (IFEs) from storage pools to dry storage units (DSUs) involve heavy equipment and complex multibody dynamics, where failures may result in significant radiological and economic consequences. Incidents at nuclear power plants, such as those at San Onofre in 2018 and Vermont Yankee in 2008, involving prolonged canister suspensions and crane brake failures, highlight critical vulnerabilities in conventional reactive monitoring approaches and the need for advanced predictive monitoring systems.This study proposes a simulation-based methodology to evaluate the feasibility of the FastTree model for predictive anomaly detection during IFE transfer operations, from initial handling to final canister positioning in DSUs. The methodology integrates a physics-based simulation framework employing PyBullet with a FastTree-based prediction model, whose performance is benchmarked against random forest, eXtreme Gradient Boosting, Light Gradient Boosting Machine, and support vector machine models.The results show that FastTree achieved 97.2% accuracy, 95.8% precision, 97.1% recall, and a 95.6% F1 score on a data set comprised of four operational scenarios. The model provided 5 to 15 s of advance warning before critical events while exhibiting lower computational cost than the more complex models evaluated, thereby demonstrating that the proposed methodology is suitable for real-time implementation in predictive monitoring applications.Although the proposed framework was assessed using physics-based simulation data, these findings establish a foundation for future validation using operational data from nuclear facilities.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2713829','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2713829',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','BR;PE','PE','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
