INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106587','Transient thermal performance and safety assessment of a liquid lead heat pipe cooled microreactor','액체 납 히트파이프 냉각 초소형원자로의 과도 열성능 및 안전성 평가','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Taiwo Saheed Yinusa; Huaping Mei; Isaac Kwasi Baidoo; Chao Chen; Taosheng Li','2026-08-26','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003525','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106587',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;GH','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112778','Computational fluid dynamics simulation of coolant flow and heat transfer in a VVER-1000 reactor core','VVER-1000 원자로 노심 내 냉각재 유동 및 열전달의 전산유체역학(CFD) 모의','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Vahid Rafiei; Farshad Rahimi','2026-08-25','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006663','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112778',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IR','IR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104672','Generalizable machine learning framework for Bragg peak prediction in polymeric materials using Monte Carlo simulations','몬테카를로 모의를 이용한 고분자 재료 내 브래그 피크 예측용 일반화 가능한 기계학습 프레임워크','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Fatih Eki̇nci̇; Nur Kaya; Zeyneb Sude Alaca; Berfin Türkoğlu; Aynur Akbarlı; Mehmet Serdar Güzel; Mehmet Büyükyıldız','2026-08-25','','2027-01','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Accurate prediction of ion-induced energy deposition in polymeric materials is essential for space radiation shielding and advanced radiotherapy applications. This study proposes a generalizable machine learning framework for predicting Bragg peak characteristics using Monte Carlo simulation. Energy deposition profiles were generated via SRIM/TRIM and Geant4 for ions with atomic numbers Z = 1–10 at energies between 70 and 150 MeV. Two key targets were defined: Bragg peak position (MM 150 ) and maximum ionization intensity (IONIZ 150 ). For SRIM/TRIM data, the Poly-2 method achieved near-ideal accuracy for MM 150 (R 2 = 0.9999), while persistence performed best for IONIZ 150 (R 2 = 0.9991). However, performance degraded in Geant4 data, where MM 150 errors increased (for Poly-2) and IONIZ 150 showed higher variability (for sMAPE). The proposed machine learning framework, evaluated using LOPO validation, achieved consistently high generalization performance. In SRIM/TRIM, R 2 reached 0.9942 ± 0.0178 (MM 150 ) and 0.9951 ± 0.0144 (IONIZ 150 ), with sMAPE values of 5.11% and 3.76%, respectively. In Geant4, similar robustness was observed, with R 2 up to 0.9942 and sMAPE reduced to 4.41% for IONIZ 150 . These results demonstrate that simulation-informed machine learning enables accurate, robust, generalizable prediction of Bragg peak behavior in polymeric materials, offering a scalable framework for radiation interaction modeling and material design.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005607','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104672',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','TR','TR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104669','Photon shielding response of GNP-reinforced B4C-TiB2 composites: Experimental and MCNP6.2 insights','GNP 강화 B4C-TiB2 복합재의 광자 차폐 특성: 실험 및 MCNP6.2 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Berkay Uygun; Onur Erbay; Demet Aydogmus; Nuri Yorulmaz; Bulent Buyuk; M. Murat Yasar; Leyla Yanmaz; Iskender Atilla Reyhancan; Filiz Cinar Sahin; Ismail Kocak; Bircan Calisir; Erhan Ayas; Mirac Kamislioglu','2026-08-25','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','In this study, the gamma and X-ray radiation attenuation properties of B 4 C-TiB 2 reference ceramics and those reinforced with 1, 2, and 3 vol% graphene nanoplatelets (GNP) were systematically investigated. The composites were fabricated via Spark Plasma Sintering (SPS), enabling rapid densification and controlled microstructural evolution. B 4 C is known for its strong thermal neutron absorption due to its high 10 B content. In addition, it contributes to gamma radiation attenuation through photon absorption and scattering interactions. The incorporation of TiB 2 and GNPs into B 4 C enhances the composite density thereby increasing the photon interaction probability and improving the overall gamma shielding performance. Radiation attenuation measurements of the composites were conducted using 0.356 MeV ( 133 Ba), 0.662 MeV ( 137 Cs), and 1.173 MeV ( 60 Co) sources, and diagnostic X-ray sources (50-110 kVp). Gamma and X-ray attenuation coefficients were independently calculated through MCNP6.2 Monte Carlo simulations to validate the experimental results. The close agreement between simulated and measured values demonstrates the reliability of the computational methodology and its consistency with established theoretical models of photon interaction cross sections. This consistency further supports the applicability of the approach for accurate evaluation and comparative analysis of photon attenuation performance in composite materials. In this study, key photon interaction parameters including the half value layer (HVL), tenth value layer (TVL), mean free path (MFP), effective atomic number (Z eff ), and effective electron density (N eff ) were computed. The results indicate that these parameters are significantly dependent on both the photon energy and the chemical composition of the examined composites. Both MCNP and experimental results show that the B 4 C-TiB 2 -GNP composites have linear attenuation coefficients (μ) ranging from 0.1468 to 0.2498 cm −1 , with the sample with 1 vol% GNP (BT1G) exhibits the highest performance, reaching 0.2498 cm −1 for 133 Ba. The results reveal that among all investigated samples, the BT1G composite exhibits the highest shielding efficiency in radiation conditions. GNP-reinforced B 4 C-TiB 2 composites, may serve as a potential alternative to reduce the use of lead in gamma radiation protection.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005577','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104669',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','TR','TR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104679','Real Options Valuation of the Pyroprocessing-SFR Fuel Cycle: Assessing Decision Flexibility in Fuel Cycle Cost under Uranium Price Uncertainty','파이로프로세싱-SFR 핵연료주기의 실물옵션 가치평가: 우라늄 가격 불확실성 하 핵연료주기 비용의 의사결정 유연성 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Manki Lee; Min Baek','2026-08-25','','2026-08','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study evaluates the economic value of maintaining the Pyroprocessing–Sodium-cooled Fast Reactor (Pyro-SFR) fuel cycle as a strategic option for spent nuclear fuel management in Korea, using a real options framework. The analysis focuses exclusively on fuel cycle costs (FCC), assuming that construction and operation & maintenance (O&M) costs of PWRs and SFRs are identical, because no reliable commercial-scale SFR cost data are currently available. Conventional discounted cash flow (DCF) analysis shows that the Pyro-SFR fuel cycle costs approximately $3.4 billion (0.40 $/MWh) more than the once-through (OT) cycle over the planning horizon. However, when decision-making flexibility is incorporated through a binomial lattice model with uranium price as the underlying stochastic variable, the option to choose between the two fuel cycles during the 2045–2065 decision window reduces total expected fuel cycle costs by $4.8 billion (0.55 $/MWh) compared to a rigid commitment to the OT cycle alone. A key methodological feature is the conservative specification of zero drift for the uranium price process, ensuring that the option value is not inflated by an assumed upward price trend. Terminal fuel cycle costs beyond 2065 are modeled using the Gordon Growth Model to capture the perpetual cost stream. Monte Carlo simulation with 10,000 iterations, using triangular distributions to sample unit cost parameters, confirms the robustness of the result with a mean option value of $4.3 billion and a 95% probability of being positive. These findings demonstrate that the value of maintaining strategic flexibility in fuel cycle policy substantially exceeds the incremental fuel cycle cost of Pyro-SFR technology development, providing a quantitative rationale for continued R&D investment in pyroprocessing technology.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S173857332600567X?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104679',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
