INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112760','On-the-fly multiple energy regions cross-section processing in OpenMC for accelerator-driven subcritical systems','가속기구동 미임계계통을 위한 OpenMC의 실시간 다중 에너지 영역 단면적 처리','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Hualiang Bai; Ruoxiu Zhao; Tong Qiao; Shichang Liu; Peng Hui; Xunchao Zhang; Hanjie Cai','2026-08-24','','2027-01','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006481','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112760',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112776','UNet-Transformer-based prediction of radionuclide dispersion under spent fuel transportation accident conditions','UNet-Transformer 기반 사용후핵연료 운반 사고 조건에서의 방사성핵종 확산 예측','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Zirui Zhang; Huining Zhou; Liwei Chen; Chunhua Chen','2026-08-24','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S030645492600664X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112776',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115160','Multiphysics continuous shape optimization of LWR nuclear reactor components under uncertainty','불확실성 하 경수로 원자로 구성품의 다중물리 연속 형상 최적화','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Jonathan Geymer; Muhammad Ramzy Altahhan; Max Nezdyur; Lynn Munday; Sebastian Schunert; Yousry Azmy','2026-08-24','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','We present the capabilities of the continuous shape optimization module within the MOOSE Multiphysics simulation framework and showcase its relevance for nuclear engineering applications. We demonstrate the module''s capabilities through an optimization study of annular fuel pin-cell shape, incorporating coupled neutronics and thermal-hydraulics simulations. The optimization process reveals significant improvements in both neutron multiplication and thermal performance. Our analysis explores the impact of various objective functions and physics feedback mechanisms, highlighting the importance of Multiphysics modeling in reactor design optimization. When including both spatial and thermal feedbacks in the pin-cell two-dimensional model, we achieve improvements of 1500 pcm in keff and around 50K reduction in maximum temperature. Furthermore, we introduce a novel DAKOTA-MOOSE interface for uncertainty quantification that provides a robust shape optimization capability under uncertainty. Both thermal conductivities and linear power uncertainties were propagated through the shape optimization process. This approach not only enhances design resilience but also quantifies the uncertainty in the expected economic benefits. By applying uncertainty quantification to the economic value derived from fuel area reduction, we can provide a more robust assessment of potential savings. Our optimized designs consistently achieve a 16-22% reduction in fuel area while maintaining or improving performance, with quantifiable confidence in the associated economic outcomes. The optimization module that we demonstrated in MOOSE, coupled with uncertainty quantification, provides a robust framework for exploring innovative fuel designs that facilitate the next generation of more efficient and safer nuclear reactors.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004127','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115160',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104675','An information flow model for quantifying emergency operating procedure execution complexity in nuclear power plants: Integrating primary and secondary tasks','원자력발전소 비상운전절차서 수행 복잡도 정량화를 위한 정보흐름 모델: 주업무 및 부업무 통합','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Wenming Chen; Licao Dai; Meihui Zhang; Yujie Quan; Chenxi Li','2026-08-24','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Design adequacy of Emergency Operating Procedures (EOPs) is critical for nuclear power plant (NPP) safety. Traditional complexity evaluations rely on qualitative analysis, failing to objectively quantify information load during the coordinated execution of primary (e.g., manipulation) and secondary (e.g., navigation) tasks in digital control rooms. This study proposes a novel information flow model to quantify the information-processing complexity of EOP execution in digital main control rooms. The approach models operator execution across six transformation stages (from scheduled action to planning), integrating primary and secondary tasks, and employs the Conant model (1976) to compute information entropy and mutual information. Validation involved 17 procedure segments from SGTR and SLOCA scenarios and an experimental study with 18 participants on an M310 simulator. Results show calculated information flow (65.54–349.05 bits) correlates strongly with task time (R 2 = 0.902), NASA-TLX workload (R 2 =0.851), mean pupil diameter (R 2 =0.654), and saccade count (R 2 =0.760). The average information processing rate converged to 2.41 bit/s under the present experimental conditions. The primary-to-secondary task information-flow ratio showed a slightly higher descriptive association with mean fixation duration (R 2 = 0.770) than the traditional primary-to-secondary task quantity ratio (R 2 = 0.738). The main contribution of this study is the explicit integration of primary and secondary task information flows within an EOP execution-complexity framework, providing an objective framework for procedure optimization, human factors risk assessment, and human-machine interface enhancement in NPPs.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005632','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104675',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;PL','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104677','Numerical investigation of reinforced concrete shear walls under bi-axial loading conditions','2축 하중 조건에서 철근콘크리트 전단벽의 수치해석 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Hyeon-Keun Yang; Jun-Hee Park','2026-08-24','','2027-01','연구논문','기타 원자력','ABSTRACT This study investigates the effects of bi-axial loading on the seismic performance of reinforced concrete (RC) shear walls through nonlinear finite element analysis (FEA). The analytical models were developed and validated against previously published experimental results, and direct comparisons were conducted between uni-axial and bi-axial loading conditions. Parametric analyses were performed by varying wall aspect ratio and reinforcement configuration, with emphasis on low-aspect-ratio walls representative of nuclear power plant auxiliary buildings. For walls with an aspect ratio of 0.8, strength reduction due to bi-axial loading was limited, with Bi/Uni strength ratios ranging from 0.90 to 0.94 and showing minor sensitivity to reinforcement ratio. However, as the aspect ratio decreased to 0.65 and 0.5, the influence of bi-axial loading became more pronounced, with average Bi/Uni ratios of approximately 0.85 and 0.80, respectively. The results indicate that strength degradation under bi-axial loading is governed primarily by wall aspect ratio rather than reinforcement ratio. Furthermore, shear-dominated failure was observed under bi-axial loading even when the corresponding uni-axial response was governed by flexural yielding. These findings suggest that uni-axial-based evaluations may overestimate the seismic capacity of low-aspect-ratio RC shear walls.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005656','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104677',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104676','Verification and validation of CFD modeling for steam line break thermal–hydraulics in PWR containment (ATLAS-CUBE benchmark)','PWR 격납건물 내 증기배관 파단 열수력에 대한 CFD 모델링 검증 및 확인(ATLAS-CUBE 벤치마크)','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Mubashir Hassan; Pankaj Jagad; Ahmad Alkaabi; Yacine Addad','2026-08-24','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','ABSTRACT This study presents a verification and validation (V&V)-based computational fluid dynamics (CFD) framework for predicting steam line break (SLB) thermal–hydraulic behavior in pressurized water reactor (PWR) containment using the ATLAS-CUBE experimental facility. Unsteady Reynolds-averaged Navier–Stokes (URANS) simulations are performed to investigate steam–air mixing and thermal stratification. Numerical uncertainty is quantified through mesh sensitivity analysis using three grids (1.6–8.2 million cells) and the Grid Convergence Index (GCI) methodology, confirming grid-independent solutions with increased uncertainty near injection region. Three turbulence models, realizable k–ε (RKE), Reynolds stress model (RSM), and k–ω SST, are evaluated against experimental measurements. All models capture dominant buoyancy-driven plume and stratification behavior, with root mean square (RMS) errors in the range of 0.033–0.056 across measurement locations. However, the RSM model provides improved agreement in anisotropic regions, while sensitivity analyses indicate that inlet steam temperature can introduce deviations of up to ±15% in predicted temperatures. Furthermore, break orientation strongly influences plume evolution and upper containment heating, with horizontal injection producing higher temperatures. The results establish a validated CFD framework for predicting steam–air mixing and thermal stratification during the early stages of SLB transients, highlighting the importance of turbulence modeling, boundary condition specification, and break configuration for reliable containment thermal–hydraulic assessments.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005644','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104676',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','AE','AE','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2686548','Developing and Sustaining World-Class Simulation Software: A Case Study with RELAP5','세계 수준 모의 소프트웨어의 개발과 유지: RELAP5 사례 연구','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','George Mesina','2026-08-24','2026-08-24','2026-08-24','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','New fields of technology emerge every year, creating a significant demand for computer programs that aid researchers in exploring and advancing theories, that assist developers in conducting experiments and building practical prototypes, and that enable builders to deploy developments as functional inventions for clients. While many of these programs are only effective for a few years before becoming obsolete, there are those that stand the test of time by addressing the evolving needs of their field and offering reliability, user friendliness, and flexible designs that allow users to analyze new concepts without requiring frequent upgrades.This document explores the essential attributes required to design a world-class program that builds and sustains enduring value over decades. Such a program must demonstrate resilience and adaptability across evolving application domains, technological shifts, organizational dynamics, and funding landscapes. RELAP5 (Reactor Excursion and Leak Analysis Program) exemplifies these abilities, having maintained its status as the premier nuclear power plant safety analysis program over its nearly 50-year lifespan. This article outlines the foundational principles and strategic decisions that have enabled RELAP5 to become a generational program and a benchmark in its field.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2686548','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2686548',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2694010','Performance of Heavyweight EAFS-Geopolymer Concrete Under Thermal and Radiation Exposure: Experimental and Machine Learning Study','열 및 방사선 노출 하 중량 EAFS-지오폴리머 콘크리트의 성능: 실험 및 기계학습 연구','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Arian DarvishaliNezhad; Seyed Hosein Ghasemzadeh Mousavinejad; Amin Gholizad; Seyyedeh Mohaddeseh Moosavifard; Sheyda Malehmir','2026-08-24','2026-08-24','2026-08-24','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study investigates the mechanical and radiation shielding performance of heavyweight geopolymer concrete incorporating electric arc furnace slag (EAFS) as both coarse and fine aggregates after exposure to elevated temperatures (200°C to 600°C) for durations of 30 to 120 min. Ground granulated blast furnace slag served as the aluminosilicate precursor, activated by sodium hydroxide and sodium silicate.The results showed that the compressive strength decreased by up to 52% at 600°C after 120 min, primarily due to dehydration, microcracking, and geopolymer matrix degradation. Despite this, the concrete retained ~48% of its original strength, outperforming many conventional heavyweight concretes.Gamma radiation shielding, evaluated using a 60Co source, revealed a 35% reduction in the linear attenuation coefficient (from 0.083 to 0.054 cm−1), while neutron shielding (via an Am-Be source) showed a 21% drop in the effective removal cross section (from 0.228 to 0.179 cm−1). These declines correlated strongly with density loss (up to 14%) and increased porosity, as confirmed by X-ray diffraction/X-ray fluorescence analyses showing phase transformations (e.g. wollastonite formation) and reduced crystallinity. A life cycle assessment indicated a 40% to 50% reduction in embodied CO2 (0.35 t CO2/t) compared to ordinary Portland cement concrete, highlighting significant environmental benefits.Machine learning models (artificial neural networks and support vector machines) accurately predicted the compressive strength (R2 ≈ 0.997), enabling performance extrapolation. This research bridges a critical gap by evaluating the effect of prior high-temperature exposure on subsequent radiation shielding performance, conditions typical in nuclear and medical facilities, demonstrating that EAFS-based geopolymer concrete is a sustainable, dual-functional material with robust performance under multihazard exposure.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2694010','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2694010',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IR;IN','IR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106573','Experimental study on flow distribution characteristics in annular fuel channel under rolling motion conditions','요동 운동 조건에서 환형 핵연료 유로 내 유량분배 특성에 관한 실험 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Yu Zou; Shouxu Qiao; Gongyao Liu; Xiangyang Cao; Sijia Hao; Ruifeng Tian; Sichao Tan','2026-08-24','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003380','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106573',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106583','PecTAF: A three-dimensional thermal hydraulic analysis code for coupled containment and PCS heat exchanger in PWR','PecTAF: PWR 격납건물 및 PCS 열교환기 연계 3차원 열수력 해석 코드','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Ziang Cao; Kai Liu; Chunjie Zeng; Hanrui Qiu; Huang Zhang; Mingjun Wang; Wenxi Tian','2026-08-24','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003483','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106583',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106584','Scaling method for lead-bismuth natural circulation under marine rolling conditions','해양 요동 조건에서 납-비스무트 자연순환의 척도 방법','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Jianing Xu; Zhen Wang; Shichao Zhang; Chao Chen; Jie Yu; Gang Pei','2026-08-24','','2026-11','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003495','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106584',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106581','Study on the reflooding behavior of debris bed based on the thermal non-equilibrium porous media model','열적 비평형 다공성매질 모델 기반 잔해층 재관수 거동 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Shihao Wu; Haotian Lu; Yapei Zhang; Jian Yu; Wenxi Tian; Suizheng Qiu; G.H. Su','2026-08-24','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S014919702600346X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106581',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112722','Statistical analyses of granular flows in pebble bed reactors','페블베드 원자로 내 입자 유동의 통계적 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ethan Nicolls; Timothy Grunloh; Seth Pemberton; Ming Fang; Sohaib Malik; William Dick; Caleb Brooks; Angela Di Fulvio','2026-08-23','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Fuel costs are a major component of pebble bed reactor (PBR) operating expenses, and uncertainty in pebble trajectories can lead to under- or over-irradiation, reducing fuel utilization and potentially degrading performance. More accurate pebble-path prediction can therefore improve fuel-management economics, particularly during load-following operation. Simulating granular flow in PBRs is a challenging task because it is affected by material properties and contact mechanics, which exhibit a large degree of time variability because of operation and fuel position. These uncertainties propagate directly into predictions of pebble trajectories and residence times, which are central quantities for fuel management. This paper reports the development and validation of Pebble TRACK : a discrete element method (DEM)-informed statistical framework for rapid pebble trajectory assessment. The Pebble TRACK approach uses mesh-free DEM simulations to generate high-resolution trajectory and contact-interaction data, including dynamic surface interactions. Pebble TRACK -predicted trajectories and residence times agree well with experimental data, requiring approximately 5.52% of the computational time as compared to a full DEM simulation. While developed for PBR applications, Pebble TRACK can be extended to produce granular flow predictions for an arbitrary geometry. These components and performances provide a computationally efficient path to predicting real-time pebble trajectories suitable for advanced fuel management strategies that will be combined with the neutron flux history to help determine a pebble’s burnup in the future.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006109','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112722',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112761','Development and verification of the SCENES code for nuclear power plants safety design and analysis','원자력발전소 안전 설계 및 해석을 위한 SCENES 코드 개발 및 검증','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Peng Zhou; Hao Zhang; Meng Zhao; Yanhua Yang','2026-08-22','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006493','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112761',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112746','Experimental and numerical study on the flow and heat transfer degradation of supercritical carbon dioxide in zigzag channels','지그재그 유로 내 초임계 이산화탄소의 유동 및 열전달 열화에 관한 실험 및 수치해석 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jinye Luo; Zichao Wu; Maolong Liu; Xianglong Guo','2026-08-22','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006341','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112746',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112766','Modeling and control strategy of nuclear power plant based on heat pipe reactor and Brayton cycle system','히트파이프 원자로 및 브레이튼 사이클 계통 기반 원자력발전소 모델링 및 제어 전략','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jian Wu; Wenxiang Gao; Mingjun Wang; Kailun Guo; Guanghui Su','2026-08-22','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006547','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112766',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112759','Neutronic assessment of reactivity control strategies in fast-spectrum Dual Fluid Reactor','고속 스펙트럼 이중유체원자로(DFR)의 반응도 제어 전략에 대한 중성자 해석 평가','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jakub Sierchuła','2026-08-22','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S030645492600647X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112759',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','PL','PL','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112764','Numerical investigation on thermal–hydraulic characteristics of a heating unit considering non-condensable gas in a heat pipe cooled reactor','히트파이프 냉각 원자로에서 비응축성 기체를 고려한 가열 단위의 열수력 특성 수치해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Chao Deng; Haochun Zhang; Hengsen Jing','2026-08-22','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006523','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112764',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112673','PRA, regulation, and protection system risk quantification: A DES/MPP refinement for risk-informed, performance-based oversight','PRA, 규제 및 보호계통 리스크 정량화: 리스크 정보 활용·성능 기반 규제감독을 위한 DES/MPP 개선','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ernie Kee; Wen-Chi Cheng; Hojun Choi','2026-08-22','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','We propose and demonstrate an alternative quantification backbone based on Marked Point Process (MPP) implemented via Discrete Event Simulation (DES) (MPP/DES). The platform renders the probability law explicit at the level of state-/time-dependent intensities and marks, represents maintenance/test resets and environment coupling, and yields pathwise metrics aligned with inspection and enforcement (e.g., time-to-accident distributions, Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) exceedances, downtime). The framework preserves traditional Probabilistic Risk Assessment (PRA) logic while avoiding fragile calibrations and clarifying the separation of aleatory vs. epistemic uncertainty. A proof-of-concept illustrates how MPP/DES outputs map to regulatory safety margins and performance thresholds, supporting risk-informed, performance-based oversight (e.g., under the Accelerating Deployment of Versatile Advanced Nuclear for Clean Energy Act of 2024 (ADVANCE)). Dynamic Probabilistic Risk Assessment (DPRA) artifacts (e.g., Dynamic Event Tree (DET) branches, solver coupling) can be layered where nonlinear plant physics dominate.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S030645492600561X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112673',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112751','Quantifying uncertainty in void swelling prediction: A conformal prediction framework for reactor safety margins','공극 팽윤 예측의 불확실성 정량화: 원자로 안전여유도를 위한 등각 예측 프레임워크','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Minhee Kim; Yong Yang','2026-08-22','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006390','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112751',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112714','Stochastic adjoint-weighted surface integration for geometric sensitivity analysis in Monte Carlo neutron transport','몬테카를로 중성자 수송의 기하학적 민감도 해석을 위한 확률론적 수반가중 표면적분','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Diplav Dongre; Ujwal Warbhe; Nileshchandra Kalbarao Pikle','2026-08-22','','2027-01','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S030645492600602X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112714',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IN','IN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115164','Design of a neutron irradiation campaign for electron beam welded reactor pressure vessel steel','전자빔 용접 원자로압력용기강의 중성자 조사시험 계획 설계','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Janelle P. Wharry; Rongjie Song; Maria A. Okuniewski; Elliot H. Marrero-Jackson; Jasmyne N. Emerson; Travis Howell; Benjamin Sutton; David W. Gandy','2026-08-22','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','The objective of this study is to document a neutron irradiation experiment campaign intended to enable evaluation of embrittlement in electron beam (EB) welded SA508, Grade 3 reactor pressure vessel (RPV) steel for small modular reactors. Arc welds in RPVs have historically experienced severe irradiation embrittlement, but advanced techniques such as EB welding, offer promise for minimizing embrittlement. Here, EB welds are made on a forged SA508 ingot and a SA508 compact manufactured by powder metallurgy with hot isostatic pressing (PM-HIP). Two different post-welding heat treatments are applied. Miniature compact tension (CT) specimens are machined from each weld region (weld centerline, heat affected zone, base metal) then fatigue pre-cracked. The average number of cycles to achieve the pre-crack length is negatively correlated with grain size, but positively correlated with hardness and ferrite phase fraction. These results imply that ductile ferrite phases absorb more energy than harder martensite and/or bainite phases. Specimens are then neutron irradiated in the Advanced Test Reactor to an average dose of 0.17 ± 0.02 displacements per atom at 322.4 ± 7.8 °C, representative of high-fluence end-of-life conditions. Specimens will undergo slow-strain-rate fracture testing over multiple temperatures to determine irradiation-induced ductile-to-brittle transition temperature shifts. Microstructural underpinnings of this irradiation embrittlement across different weld regions and materials, will also be ascertained. Specimens will be made available to researchers worldwide for future studies; this manuscript will serve as a permanent reference for material provenance.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004164','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115164',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115169','NRBO-XGBoost-based prediction of sealing leakage and preload in an RPV bottom-penetrating lance head under high-temperature and high-pressure conditions','고온·고압 조건에서 RPV 하부 관통 랜스 헤드의 밀봉 누설 및 예하중에 대한 NRBO-XGBoost 기반 예측','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Jiewei Li; Hanzhou Liu; Tiezhu Feng; Bing Zhou; Yubao Wang; Xijie Liang; Xiao Zhang; Deqi Chen','2026-08-22','','2026-11','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004218','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115169',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104674','Transient aerosol concentration inversion method based on a novel weighted spatiotemporal kriging model','새로운 가중 시공간 크리깅 모델 기반 과도 에어로졸 농도 역추정 방법','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Zebang Tan; Yuwei Yang; Xiyu Yang; Hui Yang; Jian Shan','2026-08-22','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Nuclear facility explosion accidents can instantly release large amounts of radioactive aerosols, the dispersion of which adversely affects environmental safety and health risks. This study established a novel concentration calculation and inversion model called the weighted spatiotemporal Kriging (WSTK) model to characterize the spatiotemporal distribution of radioactive aerosols under transient conditions more accurately. The proposed WSTK model significantly improves the transient concentration inversion accuracy, reducing the relative errors to as low as 1.14%. The mean relative error is -0.048%, demonstrating the effective suppression of systematic bias. These results confirm the capability of the WSTK model to accurately reconstruct radioactive aerosol concentration fields under transient conditions. This study provides a method for high-accuracy spatiotemporal inversion of radioactive aerosol concentrations under transient conditions and offers valuable technical support for safety assessments and the development of nuclear facilities.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005620','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104674',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112754','Radiological characteristics of Hong Ngu sediment samples: A statistical analysis approach','Hong Ngu 퇴적물 시료의 방사선학적 특성: 통계적 분석 접근','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Vu Ngoc Ba; Huynh Truc Van; Nguyen Van Thang; Truong Thi Hong Loan','2026-08-21','','2027-01','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006420','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112754',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','VN','VN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115170','Composite fuel-bundle design for Mo-99 production in CANDU reactors using natural molybdenum','천연 몰리브덴을 이용한 CANDU 원자로 Mo-99 생산용 복합 핵연료다발 설계','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Guo Lv; Qingquan Pan; Xiaojing Liu','2026-08-21','','2026-11','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S002954932600422X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115170',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104673','Development of a low-concentration direct calibration system for portable tritium-in-air monitors using tritium standard gas','삼중수소 표준가스를 이용한 휴대용 공기 중 삼중수소 감시기의 저농도 직접 교정 시스템 개발','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','YoungJu Lee; Kyoung su Lim; Kyeong-Min Kuk; Jae-Sung Kim','2026-08-21','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Portable Tritium-In-Air Monitors are widely used in PHWR nuclear power plants for real-time monitoring of airborne tritium concentrations and rapid detection of tritium leakage. Reliable calibration of these monitors requires direct calibration using traceable tritium standard gas. However, conventional calibration methods generally rely on indirect gamma-ray substitution techniques or relatively high-concentration tritium environments. In this study, a practical low-concentration direct calibration system was developed by combining a commercial tritium gas distribution manifold with a serial dilution-based concentration control system. Multiple calibration concentrations ranging from 3.5 to 130 μCi/m 3 were generated from a single tritium gas injection, significantly reducing tritium standard gas consumption. The developed system was validated using portable Tritium-In-Air Monitors previously calibrated by a specialized calibration laboratory in Canada. For tritium concentrations above 10 μCi/m 3 , the measured values agreed with the reference concentrations within approximately ±10% , demonstrating the reliability of the developed calibration system. An uncertainty analysis showed that the expanded uncertainty of the system was approximately 10.7% (coverage factor k =2, corresponding to a confidence level of approximately 95%). However, because of the limited display resolution and measurement accuracy of the portable Tritium-In-Air Monitor used in this study, the performance of the concentration control system could not be adequately evaluated at tritium concentrations below approximately 10 μCi/m 3 . The proposed calibration system provides a practical and cost-effective approach for the direct calibration of portable Tritium-in-Air Monitors and is expected to enhance the reliability of airborne tritium monitoring in radiation protection programs at PHWR nuclear power plants.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005619','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104673',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104665','On unprotected loss-of-flow accident in a generic molten-salt reactor','일반 용융염원자로의 비보호 유량상실사고에 관하여','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Barbara Kędzierska; Philip Pfahl; Andrei Rineiski','2026-08-21','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Unprotected loss-of-flow (ULOF) transients in molten salt reactors (MSRs) are governed by a unique interplay between thermal-hydraulics and neutronics due to the circulation of the fuel salt, which carries the delayed neutron precursors (DNPs). This study analyzes a generic fast-spectrum molten chloride reactor, similar to the LOTUS design, during a ULOF accident using the SIMMER-III multi-physics code. The work investigates the previously observed double-peak in the power evolution and examines the conditions under which this behaviour occurs. The first power peak arises primarily from the retention of DNPs in the core as flow decreases, while the second peak is driven by the return of colder fuel salt from the heat exchanger, inserting positive reactivity. Between these peaks, a power valley occurs when negative temperature feedback temporarily dominates. A comprehensive parametric study examines the influence of key operational parameters on the magnitude, timing, and presence of these characteristic features. Results demonstrate that higher mass flow rates and longer coast-down times generally increase the amplitude of the first power peak, while lower heat exchanger temperatures and lower initial powers enhance both peaks and prolong oscillations. For high-power operation​, and certain flow conditions, the double-peak behavior can be significantly damped or even eliminated. For MSRs operating at low power, the risk of significant power oscillations increases. For example, for the reference conditions, an initial power of 0.8 MW results in a first peak of approximately 104%, a subsequent valley of 55%, and a second peak of 108% of the initial power. Increasing the initial power to 3.2 MW under the same conditions eliminates the first peak, while the power decreases directly to 24% before recovering to 40% of the initial value. The analysis highlights the strong sensitivity of MSR transient behavior to steady-state design parameters and underscores the importance of accurately modelling DNP advection and heat exchanger performance in liquid-fuel reactor safety assessments.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S173857332600553X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104665',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2707610','TRISO Fuel Depletion Characterization in a Pebble Bed Modular Reactor','페블베드 모듈형 원자로에서 TRISO 핵연료의 연소 특성 평가','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Roberto Lopez-Solis; Gustavo Alonso; Eduardo Martinez; Luis Carlos Juarez-Martinez','2026-08-21','2026-08-21','2026-08-21','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2707610','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2707610',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','MX','MX','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106558','Carbon-14 design source term in pressurized water reactors considering chemical forms and release pathways','화학형태 및 방출경로를 고려한 가압경수로 탄소-14 설계 선원항','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Junnan Zhang; Defeng Yang','2026-08-21','','2026-11','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003239','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106558',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106572','Improving risk governance in nuclear facilities through integration of safety and security evaluation: An expert perspective','안전 및 보안 평가 통합을 통한 원자력시설 리스크 거버넌스 개선: 전문가 관점','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Dwi Rahayu; Julwan Hendry Purba; Boris Pavlovich Stepanov','2026-08-21','','2026-11','리뷰·관점','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003379','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106572',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','ID;RU','ID','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104660','The multi-unit human and organizational reliability analysis method with case study on emergency organization structures assuming staffing availability','인력 가용성을 가정한 비상조직 구조 사례연구를 포함한 다수기 인간 및 조직 신뢰도 분석 방법','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Jaewhan Kim; Seong Woo Kang; Yochan Kim; Jinkyun Park; Ho-Gon Lim','2026-08-20','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This study proposes a multi-unit human reliability analysis (MU-HRA) methodology to evaluate not only the human reliability of individual organizations involved in deployment of portable equipment but also that of inter-organizational cooperation activities (such as communication and coordination between these organizations). In addition, for typical responses in a multi-unit site, three types of emergency response organizational structures are presented: unit-level, station-level, and site-level. Next, using the proposed MU-HRA methodology, the human reliability value for each organizational structure is estimated. Then, the reliability levels and characteristics among these different organizational structures are compared. Through a case study applying the MU-HRA method for a case scenario where sufficient number of staffing are available on site, it was found as expected that an organization structure based on unit-level staffing allocation is most effective due to minimization of the inter-organizational dependencies and multi-unit influences. It should be noted, however, that this conclusion holds under the specific assumption of sufficient staffing availability for unit-based accident management, and that organizational reliability outcomes may differ under resource-constrained conditions. In addition, from the perspective of site-level accident management under extreme external hazards, situations may arise that require coordination and management of multiple units at a site level, beyond the management of individual unit accidents. Therefore, it is necessary to design the roles and structure of emergency organizations to ensure both efficiency and flexibility, enabling adaptive responses for various accident conditions.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005486','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104660',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2715924','Comparative Assessment of Cobalt Bioaccessibility and Bioavailability from Contaminated Media Using Unified BARGE Method and Rat Model','통합 BARGE 방법 및 쥐 모델을 이용한 오염 매체로부터 코발트의 생체접근성 및 생체이용률 비교 평가','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Nurul Syiffa Mahzan; Nur Shahidah Abdul Rashid; Kyungwon Kim; Khoo Kok Siong; Wooyong Um','2026-08-20','2026-08-20','2026-08-20','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Contaminated concrete (CC) was generated during the decommissioning of nuclear power plants, with the potential presence of radioactive cobalt (60Co). Inadvertent ingestion of these materials poses health risks to both humans and animals, underscoring the need to evaluate Co toxicity and exposure. This study investigated Co exposure from CC samples spiked at 10, 100, and 1000 mg/kg−1 through a tiered approach, incorporating the in vitro assay based on the Unified BARGE Method (UBM), in vivo testing in rats, and biokinetic modeling utilizing Simulation Analysis and Modeling (SAAM II). Co exhibited pH-dependent solubility, demonstrating greater bioaccessibility during the gastric phase (64.9%–77.4%) than in the gastrointestinal phase (47.0%–69.7%), due to the enhanced release of soluble Co2+ ions under acidic conditions. The in vivo relative bioavailability (RBA) of Co varied from 46% to 87% in blood and from 4% to 35% in urine, indicating significant systemic absorption, particularly at higher doses. The predictions made by SAAM II are closely aligned with the measured in vitro data, supporting the reliability of model-based extrapolation. Furthermore, significant dose-dependent interactions with Fe and Zn were observed, highlighting competitive uptake and regulatory mechanisms. This integration of in vitro, in vivo, and modeling approaches allows for more accurate assessments of human health risks associated with Co exposure to nuclear waste materials than methods based on the total concentration or single assay alone.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2715924','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2715924',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR;FR;MY','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2712745','Public Acceptability of Nuclear Power in Jordan: Extending the Theory of Planned Behavior with Institutional Trust and Risk-Benefit Perceptions','요르단의 원자력 대중 수용성: 제도적 신뢰 및 위험-편익 인식을 통한 계획행동이론 확장','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Ahmad Sattam Alhawamdeh; Ierenne Novendah; Yogi Tri Prasetyo','2026-08-20','2026-08-20','2026-08-20','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Jordan’s heavy dependence on imported fossil fuels has increased the policy relevance of nuclear energy as a potential pathway toward energy security, supply diversification, and long-term economic resilience. However, the success of nuclear energy development depends not only on technical and economic feasibility but also on public acceptability. This study examined the psychological, social, and institutional determinants of public acceptability of nuclear power plants in Jordan using an extended theory of planned behavior framework incorporating self-assessed knowledge, perceived benefits, perceived risks, social factors, subjective norms, and trust in regulations.Data were collected from 300 Jordanian respondents through a bilingual online survey and analyzed using partial least-squares structural equation modeling. The findings showed that perceived benefits were the strongest predictor of nuclear energy acceptability (β = 0.736, p < .001), while perceived risk had a weaker negative effect (β = −0.080, p = .028). Trust in regulations significantly increased perceived benefits (β = 0.462, p < .001), indicating that institutional trust strengthened the perceived value of nuclear energy.Contrary to the hypothesized direction, self-assessed knowledge was positively associated with perceived risk, suggesting that greater familiarity with nuclear energy may increase the awareness of potential hazards. Subjective norms and demographic variables did not show significant direct effects on acceptability. In addition, perceived benefits significantly mediated the relationships between social factors, institutional trust, and acceptability.These findings suggest that, among the surveyed respondents, public communication strategies in Jordan may benefit from prioritizing tangible national benefits, transparent governance, and regulatory credibility rather than relying solely on general information dissemination. This study contributes to the nuclear energy and risk communication literature by providing a context-specific framework for understanding public acceptability in a Middle Eastern developing country context.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712745','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712745',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','TW','TW','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2712091','Validation of Subchannel Code CTF for Sodium Fast Reactor Modeling','소듐냉각고속로 모델링을 위한 부수로 코드 CTF 검증','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Jonas Vanderwaeren; Heloise Velardo; Christophe Schneidesch; Matthias Vanderhaegen; Elias-Yammir Garcia-Cervantes; Lucia Rueda Villegas','2026-08-20','2026-08-20','2026-08-20','연구논문','열수력·유체','Liquid Metal Cooled Fast Reactors (LMFRs) use liquid metal as the primary coolant of the reactor core. First demonstrated in the 1950s, they were never fully deployed compared with light water reactor technologies. However, the early 2000s saw a resurgence of interest, particularly in Sodium Fast Reactors (SFRs) and Lead Fast Reactors (LFRs) as Generation IV designs, because of their potential to significantly reduce the amount and toxicity of nuclear waste in a closed fuel cycle. This investigation is part of Tractebel Engineering’s effort to evaluate new tools for SFR modeling. It evaluates the extended CTF subchannel code for thermal-hydraulic modeling of SFRs using new capabilities for low-Prandtl-number fluids, sodium heat transfer, hexagonal fuel assemblies, and wire-wrapped geometries. Verification and validation are performed against two complementary datasets within the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development Nuclear Energy Agency Liquid Metal Cooled Fast Reactor Thermal/Hydraulic (LMFR T/H) and Sodium Fast Reactor–Uncertainty Analysis in Modeling (SFR-UAM) benchmarks: isothermal pressure drop measurements from the Texas A&M University (TAMU) 61-pin wire-wrapped bundle, and various tests from the SEFOR facility (SFR full core). CTF-SFR reproduces the TAMU frictional pressure losses across the full Reynolds number range, confirming the suitability of the implemented wire-wrap correlations. In SEFOR single-assembly cases, the code matches 61 heat balance points and shows good agreement with reference results for average and peak sodium temperatures. Additional code-to-code comparisons with the TrioMC code highlight discrepancies in axial temperature profiles, revealing the impact of axial conduction, currently not modeled in CTF. Sensitivity studies highlight that simplified mixing and radial conduction models can overpredict corner channel peak temperatures in bare rod bundles. Overall, the results demonstrate that CTF-SFR provides reliable predictions for wire-wrapped SFR assemblies while identifying modeling assumptions requiring refinement for nonstandard geometries.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712091','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712091',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US;FR','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106575','Power generation via the development of multistage supercritical carbon dioxide Brayton and organic Rankine combined cycles: Layout design, thermal performance, and global optimization','다단 초임계 이산화탄소 브레이튼 및 유기랭킨 복합 사이클 개발을 통한 발전: 배치 설계, 열성능 및 전역 최적화','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Silong Yao; Bingtao Zhao; Jiaxin Ma; Yaxin Su','2026-08-20','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003409','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106575',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106553','Utilizing physics-informed synthetic data to predict reactor operations','물리정보 합성 데이터를 활용한 원자로 운전 예측','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Jaden Palmer; Ryan Stewart; Ashley Shields; Chad Pope; Christopher Ritter','2026-08-20','','2026-11','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','The ability to predict how a reactor will operate, understand when anomalous conditions arise, and ensure a reactor is being operated as expected is crucial for deploying new nuclear facilities. Digital twins serve as a unique solution for recognizing reactor behavior; however, they require data to be effectively utilized. For next-generation reactors, these data may not currently be available. The following work aims to validate the efficacy of using synthetic data for modeling reactor operations and enabling digital twin development of nuclear reactors prior to physical data acquisition. Physics-informed synthetic data is generated using surrogate models of reactor physics simulations of the Idaho State University AGN-201 research reactor for efficient data generation. This synthetic data generation process is validated on AGN-201 operational data to understand biases in the synthetic data generation process. Finally, the physics-informed synthetic data is used to train a long short-term memory (LSTM) recurrent neural network to dynamically predict reactor operations and allow for consistent model updating as more data becomes available. The LSTM was validated using both synthetic and real operational data. By training an LSTM model on synthetic data and validating the model on operational data, this approach can help bridge the gap between the virtual and physical sides of a digital twin.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003185','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106553',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US;MX','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115171','Reduced-order modeling of burnup calculation based on augmented invariant manifolds','증강 불변다양체 기반 연소 계산의 축소차수 모델링','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Yanzhao Bi; Fulin Zeng; Yahui Wang; Yu Ma','2026-08-19','','2026-11','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004231','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115171',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;RU','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104667','A denoising autoencoder for dual-target radionuclide quantification robust to unseen contamination and high background','미지 오염 및 고배경에 강건한 이중 표적 방사성핵종 정량용 잡음제거 오토인코더','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Chanho Kim','2026-08-19','','2027-01','연구논문','방사선·계측','In gamma-ray spectroscopy, target-isotope quantification becomes unreliable when unknown isotopes—absent from the training data—contaminate the measured spectrum. We propose a denoising autoencoder (DAE) with a direct ratio-prediction head: it reconstructs the clean target spectrum from a contaminated measurement and, from that reconstruction, predicts the fractions of 137 Cs and 133 Ba directly. Using measured Ce:GPS scintillator pulse data, a leave-one-out unknown noise (LOO-UN) protocol withholds one or two of three contaminant isotopes ( 60 Co, 54 Mn, 22 Na) from training and reintroduces them at up to 50% of the spectrum (only the contaminant identity is unseen; its fraction and the background stay within the trained ranges). The DAE is compared with a direct regression model (MLP) trained on the same data and an NNLS baseline given isotope templates and a sufficient background prior. The MLP was most accurate when clean (mean absolute error 0.015) but degraded to 0.037–0.053 at 50% contamination, whereas the DAE stayed nearly flat (0.027 clean, 0.023–0.031 thereafter), overtaking the MLP once any contamination appeared. Even with a sufficient prior, NNLS remained about 1.6 times the DAE error under high background. The contribution is robustness: without any contaminant or background library at inference, the target-fraction error barely rises as unknown contaminants increase.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005553','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104667',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104666','Codes and standards and digital technology use - recommendations for innovative nuclear plants','코드·표준 및 디지털 기술 활용 - 혁신 원자력발전소를 위한 권고사항','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Lucien Allais; Bruno Autrusson; Joachim Herb; Andreas Wielenberg; Mirela Nitoi; Andreas Ikonomopoulos; Remigijus Janulionis; Egidijus Urbonavičius; Karl-Fredrik Nilsson; Mitja Uršič; Cécile Petesch; Thierry Lebarbé; Jorge Munoz Garcia; Francesco Lodi','2026-08-19','','2026-08','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Numerous innovative reactor projects have emerged in response to the decarbonisation challenges. These projects require codes and standards as well as the use of emerging digital technologies. Most of the results presented in this publication stem from the HARMONISE project ( https://harmonise-project.eu/ ) where the requirements for codes and standards, as well as the use of emerging digital technologies, were identified for innovative reactor projects. A questionnaire was distributed to Standards Development Organisations and other industrial sectors to identify requirements already covered and those that were not. Analysis of the responses received enabled us to map out the needs that were being met and, for those that were not, recommendations were made on how to address them. As far as it concerns codes and standards, the methodologies are well known since they involve introducing new materials, extending the operating conditions of existing materials, or using new manufacturing processes, while recommendations in terms of methodology have been made. For emerging digital technologies the recommendations are less precise since, for most of them, regulatory requirements have yet to be defined. A recommendation of interest is that of reaching out to other industrial sectors facing the same challenges in order to identify potential solutions.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005541?v=s5','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104666',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','FR;DE;RO;GR;LT;BE;SI;GB','FR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
