INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112763','Application of harmonics synthesis method based on ex-core detector in pin-resolved power reconstruction','노외 검출기 기반 조화함수 합성법의 봉단위 출력 재구성 적용','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Chen Hao; Zhinan Xie; Wen Yin','2026-08-18','','2027-01','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006511','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112763',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112758','CiADS-Based 237Np transmutation experimental scheme design and gamma spectrometry simulation for burnup measurement','CiADS 기반 237Np 핵변환 실험 방안 설계 및 연소도 측정을 위한 감마 분광 모의','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Deliang Fan; Yongwei Yang; Feng zhou; Xunchao Zhang; Neng Pu; Haiyan Meng','2026-08-18','','2027-01','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006468','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112758',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112757','Development and validation of a high-fidelity 3D adjoint neutron transport calculation module for liquid fueled molten salt reactors','액체핵연료 용융염원자로를 위한 고충실도 3차원 수반 중성자 수송 계산 모듈 개발 및 검증','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Peijun Li; Ming Dai; Maosong Cheng','2026-08-18','','2027-01','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006456','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112757',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112762','Dose implications of radioiodine speciation, with a case study using CANDU severe accidents','방사성 요오드 화학종의 선량 영향: CANDU 중대사고 사례 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Luke Lebel; Javier Gonzalez-Mantecon; Sreeyuth Lal','2026-08-18','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S030645492600650X','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112762',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/s0306-4549(26)00530-x','Editorial Board','편집위원회','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-18','','2026-12','편집물','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S030645492600530X','https://doi.org/10.1016/s0306-4549(26)00530-x',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112756','High-fidelity velocimetry experiments and spatial-temporal flow analyses in a randomly packed pebble bed arrangement','무작위 충전 페블베드 배열에서의 고충실도 속도 측정 실험 및 시공간 유동 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Abdulaziz Almathami; Salman Alzahrani; Victor Ugaz; Yassin A. Hassan; Salman Alshehri','2026-08-18','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006444','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112756',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','SA;US','SA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112733','Model predictive control with state estimation and reduced-order physics for nuclear reactor operation during unanticipated communication transients','예기치 않은 통신 과도상태 시 원자로 운전을 위한 상태추정 및 축소차수 물리모델 기반 모델예측제어','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Zachery Dahm; Konstantinos Vasili; Vasileios Theos; Linyu Lin; Joe Oncken; Robert England; Vivek Agarwal; Stylianos Chatzidakis','2026-08-18','','2027-01','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Advanced nuclear reactors are increasingly being designed for remote operation and higher levels of autonomy, particularly for small and microreactor applications where on-site staffing and frequent fuel handling may be impractical. These new operational paradigms would require networked digital instrumentation and control systems, which could introduce communication uncertainties such as noise, latency, packet loss, and potential denial-of-service (DoS) events. Ensuring stable and efficient reactor operation under such conditions is therefore a critical challenge. Here, we present a quantitative evaluation of a proposed model predictive control integrated with a moving horizon state estimator (MPC-MHE) and reduced-order physics-based models for reactor power regulation under degraded communication conditions. Controller performance is benchmarked against a tuned PID controller under nominal conditions, high-intensity stochastic packet loss (95% probability of data loss), and extended sensor blackouts representative of DoS events. Across all scenarios, the MPC-MHE with reduced-order physics-based models consistently maintains tighter power regulation with substantially reduced control rod motion with the most significant improvements are observed during communication blackouts, where MPC-MHE reduces tracking error by 49–59% and control effort by 54–62% relative to PID control during both steady-state and transient power operations. These results demonstrate that model predictive control with state estimation could provide significant robustness and efficiency advantages over conventional PID control in network-degraded environments.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006213','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112733',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115168','Electrostatic precipitation-based radionuclide air sampler with vapour iodine discrimination','기체 요오드 판별 기능을 갖춘 정전 집진 기반 방사성핵종 공기 시료채취기','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Curtis Graham; Christine McGregor; David Grand-Maitre; Andrew Prudil; Luke Lebel','2026-08-18','','2026-11','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Current radionuclide monitoring stations used in accident scenarios lack capabilities in radionuclide speciation and real time readings. A device is proposed that uses a dual-stage electrostatic precipitator and an iodine-ozone conversion chamber to provide real time dose measurements, radionuclide content, and iodine phase speciation. A protype of both the electrostatic precipitator and iodine-ozone reactor stages were developed. The integrated device is expected to capture 99.0 ±0.1% of radionuclide bearing aerosols, and 59 ± 11% of vapour-phase iodine. The largest losses were vapour-phase iodine deposition on the circuit before the reactor chamber (40% to 90% of iodine vapour by mass). Of the iodine-ozone reactor produce aerosols, 98 ± 11% of these aerosols are expected to be captured by the electrostatic precipitator. The reaction chamber produced IOx aerosols with a mass median diameter of 0.19 ± 0.010 µm and a geometric standard deviation of 2.9 ± 0.5 µm.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004206','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115168',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104662','Critical di-butyl phosphate concentration and its degradation via ozonolysis governing phase stability during acidification of actinide carbonate system','악티늄 탄산염계 산성화 시 상 안정성을 지배하는 임계 인산디부틸 농도 및 오존분해에 의한 분해','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Satyabrata Mishra; Rudrashish Bhattacharya; Chayan Patra; Vishnu Anand P; N. Desigan; J. Kodandaraman; K.A. Venkatesan','2026-08-18','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Aqueous streams generated during the carbonate washing of lean solvent in the PUREX process contain di-butyl phosphate (DBP) along with residual uranium and plutonium. Prior to disposal, near-quantitative recovery of actinides is required; however, the presence of DBP interferes with downstream processing by forming a floating mass during acidification. In the present study, the threshold DBP concentration required for stable acidification of carbonate wash solutions was systematically evaluated in 0.5 M and 1 M sodium carbonate and 1.5 M hydrazine carbonate media containing uranium as a representative actinide. For a uranium concentration of 500 mg L⁻¹, the DBP concentration required prior to acidification was found to be below 1400 mg L⁻¹ and 1150 mg L⁻¹ in 0.5 M and 1 M sodium carbonate media, respectively, whereas a significantly lower threshold of 250 mg L⁻¹ was necessary in hydrazine carbonate medium. Ozonolysis was investigated as a pre-treatment strategy for DBP destruction in carbonate solutions. In 0.5 M sodium carbonate containing ~3 g L⁻¹ DBP, an ozone flow rate of 0.62 g h⁻¹ reduced DBP below 150 mg L⁻¹ within 8 h, while 1.10 g h⁻¹ achieved near-complete destruction within 7 h. DBP degradation in hydrazine carbonate medium was comparatively slower due to concurrent oxidation of hydrazine by ozone.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005504','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104662',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IN','IN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104632','Integrating diversity and defense-in-depth analysis into STPA for digital I&amp;C systems of small modular reactors','소형모듈원자로 디지털 계측제어계통을 위한 STPA에 다양성 및 심층방어 분석 통합','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Yoona Heo; Junbeom Yoo','2026-08-18','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Small modular reactors (SMRs) rely heavily on digital instrumentation and control (I&C) systems, making compliance with fundamental design principles essential for ensuring safety. Among these principles, diversity and defense-in-depth (D3) plays a key role in preventing common-cause failures (CCFs), which can simultaneously affect multiple system components and compromise safety functions. Traditional hazard analysis techniques primarily focus on chain-of-event failure propagation and may not adequately capture hazards arising from complex interactions within digital systems. Systems-theoretic process analysis (STPA) addresses this limitation by considering unsafe interactions and control flaws during early system design. However, D3 considerations are often analyzed separately from hazard analysis, potentially overlooking safety-relevant interactions related to CCFs. This paper proposes an approach for integrating D3 analysis into STPA. The approach incorporates D3-oriented control structure modeling guidelines and UCA identification guidelines, a taxonomy of causal factors, exclusion rules for structural credibility, and a prioritization process for CCF-related causal factors. A case study on both the module-level and plant-level protection system of the NuScale SMR demonstrates that the proposed approach can identify interaction-induced causal factors, shared dependencies, and fault propagation paths that are difficult to reveal without explicit consideration of D3.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005206','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104632',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104652','Probabilistic model chain methodology for defining emergency planning zones for iPWR-type reactors','iPWR형 원자로의 비상계획구역 설정을 위한 확률론적 모델 체인 방법론','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Piotr Kopka; Tomasz Kwiatkowski; Anna Wawrzynczak; Michał Jędrzejczyk; Afaque Shams','2026-08-18','','2026-08','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005401','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104652',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104664','Radiological shielding performance of selected titanate compounds: An experimental and theoretical investigation','선정된 티탄산염 화합물의 방사선 차폐 성능: 실험 및 이론 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Abdu Hamoud Al-khawlany; Shamsan S. Obaid; Fawziah Mohammad Al-Saar','2026-08-18','','2027-01','연구논문','원자로물리·해석',': The radiation shielding characteristics of selected titanate compounds, aluminum titanate (Al 2 TiO 5 ), strontium titanate (SrTiO 3 ), calcium titanate (CaTiO 3 ), manganese titanate (MnTiO 3 ), lithium titanate (Li 2 TiO 3 ), and lead titanate (PbTiO 3 ),were systematically investigated through theoretical and experimental approaches. The main radiation shielding parameters, including linear and mass attenuation coefficients (μ and μ/ρ), atomic cross-section (σ a ), electronic cross-section (σ e ), effective atomic number (Z eff ), effective electron density (N eff ), half-value layer (HVL), and mean free path (MFP), were calculated using the XCOM database and Geant4 simulations. Experimental measurements were performed using a γ-ray spectrometer equipped with a NaI (Tl) scintillation detector at photon energies of 122, 356, 511, 662, 840, 1170, 1275, and 1330 keV. The experimental results showed excellent agreement with the theoretical calculations, confirming the reliability of the obtained shielding parameters. Among the studied titanate compounds, Al 2 TiO 5 exhibited the highest HVL and MFP values, ranging from 1.2810 to 4.2489 cm and from 1.8484 to 6.1312 cm, respectively, indicating lower gamma-ray attenuation efficiency. Conversely, PbTiO 3 showed the lowest HVL and MFP values (0.0378–1.7692 cm and 0.0545–2.5530 cm, respectively), demonstrating superior gamma-ray shielding performance. These results provide valuable insights into the radiation attenuation behavior of titanate-based materials and highlight their potential for advanced radiation protection applications','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005528','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104664',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','YE','YE','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106571','Development of a MC/MOC two-step method for plate-type reactor with optimized self-scatter correction transport-corrected method','최적화된 자기산란 보정 수송보정 방법을 적용한 판형 원자로용 MC/MOC 2단계 방법 개발','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Jiannan Li; Ling Chen; Song Li; Yongfa Zhang; Yuyang Shen; Xiangyi Deng','2026-08-18','','2026-11','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003367','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106571',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106574','Flow and heat transfer of LBE in narrow rectangular channels: Correlation development and subchannel code implementation','좁은 직사각형 유로 내 LBE 유동 및 열전달: 상관식 개발 및 부수로 코드 구현','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Haibo Jia; Minyang Gui; Ruifeng Tian; Hangyuan Zhang; Yulin Mu; Sichao Tan','2026-08-18','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149197026003392','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106574',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112720','Code to code comparison of a dba sequence in a generic iPWR between MELCOR and ASTEC codes','일반 iPWR의 설계기준사고 시퀀스에 대한 MELCOR와 ASTEC 코드 간 비교','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Gianmarco Grippo; Giuseppe Agnello; Pietro Maccari; Fulvio Mascari','2026-08-17','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Nowadays, several integral Pressurised Water Reactor (iPWR) designs are close to the licencing stage since they are based on the well-established technology of large Light Water Reactors (LWRs), incorporating evolutionary design features aimed at enhancing the inherent safety of the plant through integral configurations and adoption of passive safety systems. However, a sound demonstration of iPWRs’ capability to address Severe Accident (SA) should be carried out for a comprehensive safety review process. In this context, the international scientific community is increasingly focusing on assessing SA integral codes in simulating typical iPWRs’ phenomenology during postulated accidental scenarios. The Horizon Euratom project “Safety Analysis of SMR with Passive Mitigation strategies – Severe Accident” (SASPAM – SA), coordinated by ENEA, investigates the applicability, the transfer of the large LWR knowledge and know-how to iPWRs, in view of SA and Emergency Planning Zone (EPZ) licensing analyses needs. In this regard, the present work carried out within the SASPAM-SA project presents a comparative analysis between the SA codes MELCOR and ASTEC. The goal of the study is to evaluate the capability of the codes in simulating the dominant thermal–hydraulic phenomena during a postulated Design Basis Accident (DBA) scenario in a generic 300 MWe iPWR, considering the full availability of the reactor passive safety systems. The code-to-code benchmark highlights the main consistencies and possible discrepancies between the codes.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006080','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112720',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IT','IT','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112737','Comparative thermal and hydrothermal decomposition of mixed thorium–uranium oxalates: phase evolution and microstructural characteristics','혼합 토륨–우라늄 옥살산염의 열분해 및 수열분해 비교: 상 변화 및 미세조직 특성','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Narges Bagheri; Ferial Nosratinia; Fazel Zahakifar; Taher Yousefi','2026-08-17','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926006250','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112737',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112681','Multi-scale modeling of Zircaloy cladding: From mechanistic crystal plasticity to finite element surrogates with scenario-based validation','지르칼로이 피복관의 다중스케일 모델링: 메커니즘 기반 결정소성에서 유한요소 대리모델까지 및 시나리오 기반 검증','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Andre Ruybalid; Andrea Rovinelli; Ryan Sweet; Kyle Gamble; Laurent Capolungo','2026-08-17','','2027-01','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306454926005694','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112681',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115152','CATHARE3 model description of the High Temperature Test Facility and HTGR T/H benchmark participation','고온시험시설(HTTF)의 CATHARE3 모델 기술 및 HTGR 열수력 벤치마크 참여','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Zsombor Bali; Gusztáv Mayer','2026-08-17','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','Accurate modeling of radial heat transfer in a gas-cooled nuclear reactor is important, especially when simulated with a one-dimensional thermal hydraulics code. To gain our knowledge in this field, HUN-REN EK decided to participate in the HTGR T/H benchmark, which is based on measurements conducted on the helium-cooled High Temperature Test Facility (HTTF) built at Oregon State University (OSU). Although the HTTF is a demonstrator of the Modular High Temperature Gas-cooled Reactor (MHTGR) with a relatively low power density in which the heat is mostly transferred via conduction, we believe that the knowledge gained here can be used in GFR development, such as the helium-cooled fast reactor demonstrator ALLEGRO, where the core power density is one order of magnitude higher. This paper describes the benchmark activity of HUN-REN EK in the OECD HTGR T/H benchmark using the CATHARE3 thermal hydraulics code. In this work, a new input deck was developed from scratch to model the dominant heat transfer phenomena in the HTTF core. As part of the OECD benchmark, the simulation results are compared with measurements. The results showed that if the model is sufficiently detailed, the corresponding temperature profiles are adequately described by the CATHARE code.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004048','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115152',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','HU','HU','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115157','Coupled thermal-mechanical monitoring of an HTGR reactor vessel','HTGR 원자로용기의 열-기계 연계 감시','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Pramatha Bhat; Lesley M. Wright; Luiz C. Aldeia Machado; Roberto Ponciroli; Lander Ibarra; Elia Merzari; Yassin A. Hassan','2026-08-17','','2026-11','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004097','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115157',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115159','Effects of Xe addition on the performance of a supercritical CO2 centrifugal compressor','Xe 첨가가 초임계 CO2 원심압축기 성능에 미치는 영향','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Zhiqiang Bao; Shilong Wang; Yongqing Xiao; Mingchao Li; Yilin Wang; Kuihua Han; Jianhui Qi; Shigang Fu; Jianli Zhao','2026-08-17','','2026-11','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004115','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115159',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115156','MAEO: Scalable Multiobjective Animorphic Ensemble Optimization for large-scale optimization applications','MAEO: 대규모 최적화 응용을 위한 확장 가능한 다목적 Animorphic 앙상블 최적화','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Omer F. Erdem; Dean Price; Paul Seurin; Majdi I. Radaideh','2026-08-17','','2026-11','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Multiobjective optimization remains challenging for many scientific and engineering problems due to the need to balance convergence, diversity, and computational efficiency across high-dimensional objective landscapes. This work presents the Multiobjective Animorphic Ensemble Optimization (MAEO) framework, a parallelizable ensemble strategy that unifies state-of-the-art evolutionary algorithms within an island-based architecture, overcoming the limitations of relying on a single optimizer, as implied by the No Free Lunch theorem. MAEO uses a parameter-free hypervolume indicator for island performance assessment and a strict Pareto-rank-based individual scoring formulation that incorporates crowding distance and nadir-point proximity to ensure consistent selection pressure within each front. The framework is initiated using four algorithms (NSGA-III, CTAEA, AGEMOEA2, SPEA2) and evaluated through extensive benchmarking on 12 DTLZ/ZDT functions under 36 dimensionality settings using Wilcoxon signed-rank tests with both hypervolume and inverse generational distance metrics. Results show that MAEO achieves balanced convergence–diversity performance, outperforming or matching some of the leading multiobjective optimization algorithms across different benchmark problems. To demonstrate practical applicability, MAEO is applied to the equilibrium-cycle optimization of a small modular nuclear reactor. Eight discrete design variables (seven assembly enrichments and burnable absorber configuration) and three objectives (levelized fuel cost, peak soluble boron concentration, fuel cycle length) are optimized under two safety constraints. The algorithm carried out 80,000 evaluations using computer simulations. MAEO identifies core designs that lower both the levelized fuel cost and the peak boron concentration, while preserving fuel cycle length and meeting all safety constraints. These findings highlight MAEO’s effectiveness for high-dimensional and large-scale engineering optimization.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0029549326004085','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115156',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104635','Assessment of gas capture via tunnel ventilation following an underground chemical explosion','지하 화학 폭발 후 터널 환기를 통한 기체 포집 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Bradley G. Fritz; Christine Johnson; Aliya H. Whitehill; Jacob A. Peterson; Jeffery Burghardt','2026-08-17','','2027-01','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','In October 2023 an underground chemical explosive test, Physics Experiment 1-A, was executed in a tunnel at the Nevada National Security Site. This test was part of a series of multi-physics experiments focused on enhancing nuclear explosion monitoring techniques. Part of the experiment included monitoring ga movement. As part of the facility operations, there were two events during the first five days of the experiment where the ventilation system was operated to purge gases from the facility. These events afforded an opportunity to evaluate the mass of gases emitted to the atmosphere during these ventilation events and compare to the total mass produced during the experiment. This provides a basis for estimating the fraction of gas produced in an underground test that might be expected to be released through natural and engineered pathways. Using several approaches, an estimate of between 1 and 9% of the total gas produced by the experiment was captured and discharged to the atmosphere during these events. The percentage of gas captured was nominally equal to the percentage of the plume volume that was bisected by the facility tunnels and represents a similar fraction to that assumed as potential releases for underground nuclear tests.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005231','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104635',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104645','CFD simulation of hydrodynamics in a pulsed sieve plate column using ANSYS fluent: An integrated multiphase modeling approach','ANSYS Fluent를 이용한 맥동 체판탑 내 유체역학의 CFD 모의: 통합 다상유동 모델링 접근','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Vahid Rafiei; Sadegh Moradi','2026-08-17','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study presents a Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD) investigation of a Pulsed Sieve Plate Column (PSPC) using ANSYS Fluent, combining a Eulerian-Eulerian two-fluid model with an empirically modified drag correlation, a Population Balance Model (PBM), and a Random-Forest-based surrogate model coupled with a Genetic Algorithm (GA) for pulsation parameter optimization. The modified drag correlation accounts for droplet swarm and Strouhal-number effects under pulsation and is presented as a calibrated closure rather than a first-principles result. Simulations were compared against experimental data from a laboratory-scale column (internal diameter 50 mm, height 1.5 m) operating with a kerosene-water system. The CFD-PBM framework reproduced dispersed-phase holdup within 5% of experimental values for the tested Dc = 50 mm kerosene-water system and the Sauter mean droplet diameter (d32) within 6-9% of the measured values, outperforming the standard Schiller-Naumann drag model, which exhibited holdup deviations of 12-21%. A dimensionless Pulsation Efficiency Number (PEN) is introduced, and a generalized form (PEN*) incorporating plate spacing and column diameter is derived using Buckingham π analysis to eliminate the geometric inconsistency of the original composite metric. The GA-Random-Forest optimization framework predicts operating conditions capable of improving the overall mass transfer coefficient by 23.5% (95% prediction interval: 18.1-28.9%) relative to the baseline operating conditions.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005334','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104645',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IR','IR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104640','Combined effects of Joule heating and nonlinear thermal radiation on stagnation-point flow of a second-order nanofluid over an exponentially stretching surface','지수적으로 늘어나는 표면 위 2차 나노유체 정체점 유동에 대한 줄 가열 및 비선형 열복사의 복합 영향','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Awatif Alhowaity; Muhammad Naveed Khan; Aamir Abbas Khan; Haneen Hamam; Salah Knani; Nurul Amira Zainal','2026-08-17','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','This article examines the stagnation-point flow and thermal transmission of a second-order nanofluid over an exponentially stretching surface, incorporating Joule heating and a magnetically induced field. The mathematical model includes nonlinear thermal radiation, activation energy, zero mass flux, and thermal slip boundary conditions to capture realistic transport phenomena. Using similarity transformations, the governing PDEs are reduced into coupled system of nonlinear ODEs, which is subsequently solved numerically using the MATLAB BVP4C solver. The findings demonstrate that the induced magnetic field is enhanced by raising the magnetic field parameter and magnetic Prandtl number. Higher estimations of the second-order fluid parameter lead to increases in both the skin friction and the heat transfer rate, highlighting the role of fluid elasticity in thermal transport. Further, the fluid temperature rises with increasing thermophoresis, Brownian motion, and thermal radiation parameters, whereas the concentration field declines with higher Lewis number and concentration slip parameter. The proposed model is applicable to magnetohydrodynamic cooling systems, liquid-metal nuclear reactor cooling, electromagnetic casting, polymer extrusion, and thin-film coating processes, providing valuable insights for improving heat transfer and thermal management in advanced engineering systems.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005280','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104640',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','SA;PK;MY','PK','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104658','Field- and filter-dependent tissue-maximum ratios for 6 MV photon','6 MV 광자선의 조사야 및 필터 의존 조직최대선량비','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','O. El mouden; H. Sekkat; A. Bannan; R. El Baydaoui; M. Tahiri; M. Bougteb; O. El Rhazouani; M. Mkimel; A. Seriani','2026-08-17','','2027-01','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Accurate characterization of the tissue–maximum ratio (TMR) is important for beam modelling and dosimetric verification, particularly for flattening-filter-free (FFF) beams and non-reference fields. This study characterized TMR for 6 MV flattened (FF) and FFF photon beams from an Elekta Versa HD across square fields from to . Central-axis water-phantom measurements using PTW microDiamond and Semiflex detectors were compared with GATE/Geant4 Monte Carlo simulations. For the reference field, simulated percentage depth-dose values agreed with measurements within 1 percentage point between 10 and 30 cm depth. TMR increased systematically with field size beyond the buildup region. At 10 cm depth, measured TMR increased from 0.6887 to 0.8215 for FF and from 0.6829 to 0.8130 for FFF. At 20 cm, the corresponding ranges were 0.4432-0.6016 and 0.4366-0.5830. Monte Carlo-measurement differences remained within 0.011 TMR units. The ratio also increased with field size, confirming that it is not field-size invariant outside reference geometry.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005462','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104658',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','MA','MA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104661','Practical validation of zeolite-modified cementation for real intermediate-level liquid waste under Waste Acceptance Criteria (WAC)','폐기물 인수기준(WAC)에 따른 실제 중준위 액체폐기물의 제올라이트 개질 시멘트 고화 실증 검증','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Gi Yong Kim; Su Jin Kim; Hyeonjune Noh; Dae Seok Hong; Junhyuck Im','2026-08-17','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Intermediate-level radioactive liquid waste (ILLW) generated at the Korea Atomic Energy Research Institute (KAERI) requires robust solidification for safe long-term disposal. Although bituminization has been widely applied, its limitations in mechanical stability and long-term durability necessitate alternative approaches, while conventional cement waste forms remain constrained by high porosity and limited capacity for immobilizing mobile radionuclides such as cesium. This study evaluates the performance of zeolite-modified cement waste forms using real ILLW obtained from the KAERI Radioactive Waste Treatment Facility (RWTF). Zeolite was incorporated at 3, 5, and 10 wt.% and the specimens were assessed in accordance with domestic Waste Acceptance Criteria, including compressive strength, thermal stability, and radionuclide leaching behavior. All specimens satisfied regulatory requirements, maintaining compressive strengths above 3.44 MPa after thermal and immersion aging. Zeolite addition significantly reduced Cs-134 and Cs-137 release and increased leachability indices beyond the regulatory threshold. The 10 wt.% specimen exhibited the lowest effective diffusivity, while 5 wt.% provided comparable performance with improved material efficiency. These results demonstrate that zeolite-modified cementation is an effective and practically applicable approach for enhancing cesium immobilization in real ILLW, supporting its use in long-term radioactive waste disposal.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005498','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104661',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104663','Thermal creep behavior of precipitation-strengthened wrought FeCrAl cladding tube at different temperatures','석출강화 가공 FeCrAl 피복관의 온도별 열 크리프 거동','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Jingze Zhou; Yuntao Zhong; Ruiqian Zhang; Huan Sheng Lai; Peinan Du','2026-08-17','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','FeCrAl alloys are recognized as an excellent candidate material for accident-tolerant fuel cladding tubes. However, thermal creep behaviors of FeCrAl alloy cladding tubes and the associated microstructural evolution have not been comprehensively investigated. This work addressed this gap by evaluating the axial thermal creep behavior of precipitation-strengthened wrought FeCrAl alloy cladding tubes at the temperatures of 360°C and 475°C, respectively. Creep test results indicated that there was a threshold stress for the FeCrAl alloy cladding tubes, because the thermal creep strain rate increased rapidly when the thermal creep stress was larger than a specific stress level. Consequently, a power-law thermal creep constitutive model with a threshold stress was established according to the thermal creep test results. Creep failure was primarily caused by shear stress. In addition, microstructural analysis indicated that the grain size of the FeCrAl alloy cladding tubes initially increased and subsequently decreased with increasing applied stress. Both the dislocation density and the proportion of low-angle grain boundaries demonstrated a decreasing trend with increasing stress levels.','OpenAlex','https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1738573326005516','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104663',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2707617','Effect of Crack Location on the Mechanical State at the Tip of Stress Corrosion Cracks in Dissimilar Metal Welded Joints','이종금속 용접부 응력부식균열 선단의 역학적 상태에 대한 균열 위치의 영향','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Shuai Wang; Yicheng Wang; Bin Wang; Wanzhong Li; Lu Cui; Shaohu Liu; Lijing Dong; He Xue','2026-08-17','2026-08-17','2026-08-17','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Dissimilar metal weld joints (DMWJs) between low-alloy steel SA508 and austenitic stainless steel 316L, fabricated using nickel-based alloy 52M as filler metal, are critically important in the primary circuit of pressurized water reactors (PWRs). The structural integrity of such DMWJs is strongly influenced by the mechanical heterogeneity, especially near the fusion line (FL). In this study, the local mechanical properties of an SA508-52M-316L DMWJ were determined via an indentation test, while metallographic analysis was employed to characterize the heterogeneous microstructure adjacent to the FL. A finite element (FE) model incorporating continuously graded mechanical properties was developed using a predefined temperature field approach to represent the material heterogeneity more accurately than conventional sandwich models. Based on this continuous transition model, elastoplastic FE analyses were conducted to evaluate the Mises stress and plastic strain distributions at the tip of cracks located at different positions relative to the FL. The results reveal that the inhomogeneous mechanical property distribution significantly alters the crack-driving force, particularly when the crack approaches the FL region, underscoring the necessity of accounting for local heterogeneity in the structural integrity assessment of DMWJs.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2707617','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2707617',1,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;GB;MX','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2712737','Quantitative Benchmarking and Uncertainty-Based Performance Evaluation of a Digital PET/CT System Using NEMA NU 2–2007','NEMA NU 2–2007을 이용한 디지털 PET/CT 시스템의 정량적 벤치마킹 및 불확실성 기반 성능 평가','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Morad El Kafhali; Marziyeh Tahmasbi; Abdelaali Rahmouni; Mohammed Khalis; Abdenbi El Moutaoukkil; Younes Ouled Sidi Ali; Amina El Kessioui','2026-08-17','2026-08-17','2026-08-17','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712737','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712737',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','PT;SE;IR;MA;US','PT','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2671624','TRISO-ATOPS: A Mechanistic Source Term Model for Gas-Cooled Reactors','TRISO-ATOPS: 가스냉각로를 위한 메커니즘 기반 선원항 모델','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Benjamin Stoyer; Alexandra Raichart; David Petti','2026-08-17','2026-08-17','2026-08-17','연구논문','열수력·유체','Source term modeling for TRistructural ISOtropic (TRISO) fuel has been performed for previous reactor designs, but few are available in the open literature. Thus, there is a need to develop a simple, versatile, and mechanistic model of fission product release and transport in gas reactor cores that can be applied to a variety of reactors through user inputs and reactor-specific radionuclide inventories. To meet this need, the TRISO Analysis Tool for Predictive Source terms was developed. This model calculates the release of the key safety-important fission products by diffusion through the kernel, silicon carbide, and graphite based on fuel and graphite temperatures in the reactor under normal operation. These releases from the fuel enter the coolant where some can plate out on cooler surfaces. A cleanup model is included for designs with a coolant purification system for removing fission gases. This initial distribution of fission products in the reactor serves as an initial condition for potential releases under postulated accident conditions. From this initial condition, the model calculates the fission product release for any transient temperature profile, and the fission product releases can then be used to assess radiological dose to the workers and the public using conventional radiological dose tools. Data on the diffusion of fission products is based on historic German TRISO experiments and the more current Department of Energy advanced gas reactor TRISO fuel development program. The example cases in this work demonstrate the flexibility of the model.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2671624','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2671624',0,'2026-08-30','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
