INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104657','Evaluation of aerial monitoring data by extended stripping window method','확장 스트리핑 윈도우 방법에 의한 항공 모니터링 데이터 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-14','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104657','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104657',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104659','Optimization of chemical etching conditions and evaluation of detection performance for the DX-22 solid-state nuclear track detector','DX-22 고체 비적 검출기의 화학 식각 조건 최적화 및 검출 성능 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-14','','','연구논문','방사선·계측','This study optimized the chemical etching conditions of the newly developed UV-polymerized poly(allyl diglycol carbonate) detector DX-22 and evaluated its detection performance. An orthogonal design followed by single-factor experiments was used to investigate the effects of NaOH concentration, etching temperature, and etching time on track morphology, track density, and background counts. The optimal conditions were 6.5 mol/L NaOH, 65 °C, and 8 h. Under these conditions, etched alpha-particle tracks showed clear contours, relatively uniform morphology, predominantly elliptical shapes, low background, and a track density of 201.8 tracks/mm 2 . CR-39 was used as a reference detector for indoor radon measurements. DX-22 and CR-39 showed consistent spatial track-density trends, with relative area errors of 6.46%-12.93% between fitted response curves. The field comparison was not intended as an absolute radon calibration, and standardized radon-chamber calibration and uncertainty evaluation remain necessary for quantitative dosimetric application. Overall, DX-22 demonstrated promising potential for radon monitoring and radiation protection.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104659','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104659',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115165','Corrosion and electrochemical response of 316L stainless steel in boron-free small modular reactor environments with KOH and NH3','KOH 및 NH3를 사용하는 무붕산 소형모듈원자로 환경에서 316L 스테인리스강의 부식 및 전기화학적 반응','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-13','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115165','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115165',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115151','Neutronics analysis and design of mechanical shim control strategy for a pressurized water reactors under base load operation','기저부하 운전 가압경수로를 위한 기계적 심 제어 전략의 중성자 해석 및 설계','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-13','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115151','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115151',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104655','Fast thermal-hydraulic-neutronic model to simulate transient behavior of an aqueous homogeneous reactor','수용액 균질로 과도 거동 모의를 위한 고속 열수력-중성자 연계 모델','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-13','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','Mo 99 is a widely used radioisotope in nuclear medicine, particularly for producing Tc 99m . The Aqueous Homogeneous Reactor (AHR) is a promising method for producing Mo 99 . This paper presents a coupled neutron point kinetics and thermal-hydraulics model for ARGUS, a kind of AHR, which utilizes uranyl sulfate liquid fuel in the reactor core. This research aims to develop an accurate and computationally efficient model to predict the transient behavior of ARGUS. The effects of transient reactivity insertion on the overall reactor performance have been studied. Analysis of the reactor''s performance demonstrates the effectiveness of its safety features, which are attributed to negative feedback mechanisms such as temperature feedback and void feedback. When power output rises, there''s a rapid increase in void formation, which generates strong negative feedback. In 1$ step reactivity insertion, the power initially increases to 366.5 kW but after 10 seconds returns to 78 kW due to void feedback. This model can contribute to developing an optimized control system for AHRs.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104655','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104655',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IR','IR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104595','Global seismic site characterization of nuclear power plant sites using USGS Vs30 data','USGS Vs30 데이터를 이용한 원자력발전소 부지의 전 지구적 지진 부지 특성 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-13','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104595','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104595',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2713831','Atmospheric Dispersion of Radioactive Materials Modeled by Stochastic Differential Equations','확률미분방정식으로 모델링한 방사성물질의 대기확산','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','','2026-08-13','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This research utilized stochastic differential equations to investigate the dispersion of radiological agents in the atmosphere. The modeling involved a stochastic component in the advective term of the advection-diffusion equation. The solution was obtained using the Euler-Maruyama and finite difference methods to ensure numerical stability and accuracy. The results aligned well with the hypothetical scenario of an environmental release of radioactive material from a nuclear reactor accident. The simulations illustrated how random atmospheric fluctuations and varying wind speeds impact the spread of radionuclides. The study emphasizes the importance of incorporating stochastic elements into predictive models to accurately capture the complex dynamics of radiological dispersion.In this context, the current study aimed to develop better methodological tools to enhance our understanding of the physical processes behind the atmospheric dispersion of radiological contaminants. Although the proposed model relies on simplifying assumptions, the approach based on stochastic differential equations offers a theoretical framework that can serve as a foundation for creating more comprehensive models in the future. These future models will focus on analyzing disruptive events related to the uncontrolled release of radioactive material into the atmosphere or the environment.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2713831','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2713831',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','BR','BR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
