INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112703','Research on the efficient and lightweight surrogate model for Probabilistic Safety Margin analysis of SBLOCA in nuclear power plants integrating DL-TL','DL-TL을 통합한 원자력발전소 SBLOCA 확률론적 안전여유도 해석용 고효율 경량 대리모델 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112703','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112703',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112742','Validation and reliability analysis of CFD-based atmospheric dispersion modeling against wind tunnel experiments at a nuclear power plant site with irregular buildings and complex terrain','불규칙 건물 및 복잡 지형을 갖는 원자력발전소 부지에서 풍동실험 대비 CFD 기반 대기확산 모델링의 검증 및 신뢰성 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112742','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112742',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115158','Multiobjective optimization methodology for the design of a 10-kW-class space nuclear fission power system','10 kW급 우주 원자력 핵분열 전력계통 설계를 위한 다목적 최적화 방법론','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115158','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115158',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','FR','FR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115154','Seismic analysis of TMSR graphite core with viscous damping','점성감쇠를 고려한 TMSR 흑연 노심의 지진 해석','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115154','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115154',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104656','Is grid-based intraoperative electron radiotherapy (IOERT) a potential solution for surface dose enhancement in breast cancer treatment?','격자 기반 수술 중 전자선 방사선치료(IOERT)는 유방암 치료에서 표면선량 증가를 위한 잠재적 해법인가?','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','Surface under-dosage is a challenge during breast intraoperative electron radiotherapy, especially at low energies (below 10 MeV). Current study tries to overcome this limitation by adding a grid to distal end of the employed electron applicator and producing a mixed electron-photon field. LIAC12 head, a dedicated IOERT Linac, along with attached applicator were simulated by MCNPX code. Then, a dedicated grid with fill factor of 0.1 was attached to distal end of applicator. Finally, PDD curves, TDPs and isodose curves were calculated in presence and absence of the grid. Inserting the grid improves surface dose at low electron energies (6 and 8 MeV), while it is not efficient at higher energies (10 and 12 MeV). Field symmetry and flatness were within recommended criteria at 6 and 8 MeV electron energies, while were not satisfied at higher energies. Isodose curves were affected within target superficial parts in grid presence. Adding the grid to distal end of IOERT applicator is efficient in surface dose enhancement and dose uniformity improvement at low electron energies (less than 10 MeV). In return, it doesn’t considerably increase surface dose at higher electron energies. Hence, the introduced method is only suitable, viable and effective for low energies.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104656','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104656',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104650','Optimization of a BWR bundle performance for reactor-grade plutonium and minor actinides recycling','원자로급 플루토늄 및 부악티늄 재활용을 위한 BWR 핵연료다발 성능 최적화','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study investigates the feasibility of recycling reactor-grade plutonium and minor actinides (MAs) in a boiling water reactor (BWR) using modified mixed-oxide (MOX) fuel compositions as an alternative to conventional burnable absorber rods. Six fuel compositions are proposed, requiring minimal modifications to the standard BWR fuel bundle design. Neutronic analyses were performed using the Serpent Monte Carlo code in conjunction with the ENDF/B-VII.0 nuclear data library. The analyses demonstrated that all proposed MOX configurations are capable of sustaining criticality over extended irradiation periods while delivering an energy output comparable to that of reference UOX fuel. The required 235 U enrichment per assembly is reduced from 3.67 wt.% in the UOX case to approximately 3.16 wt.% for most MOX configurations. Effective transmutation performance is achieved, with up to 86% of the initial MAs inventory and 32.2% of the initial plutonium inventory consumed over the fuel cycle. Key safety-related reactivity coefficients, including the fuel temperature coefficient, moderator temperature coefficient, void reactivity worth at 40% and 70% void fractions, and control rod worth, remain negative on average, indicating acceptable reactivity feedback and stable reactor behavior. These results confirm that the proposed MOX fuel concepts provide a viable and safe option for plutonium and minor actinide recycling in BWRs.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104650','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104650',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','EG;RU','EG','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2712744','Financing Nuclear Decommissioning in Ghana: An Evaluation of Public-Private Partnership Models','가나의 원자력시설 해체 재원 조달: 민관협력 모델 평가','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This review looks at how Ghana can use public-private partnership (PPP) models to obtain long-term funding for the decommissioning of its current research reactor and upcoming nuclear installations. Ghana’s current legal framework would benefit from strengthened institutional capacity, clearer financial assurance procedures, and the establishment of dedicated decommissioning funds.This review uses a comparative legal institutional analysis alongside international best practices from other countries and lessons learned from Ghanaian industries. The paper outlines a phased set of policy recommendations by identifying the technical, financial, regulatory, and sociopolitical risks associated with nuclear decommissioning. These recommendations include the creation of a national coordinating institution, long-term capacity building initiatives, and legal reforms to integrate decommissioning finance within nuclear safety regulations.The results demonstrate that well thought out PPP mechanisms can improve safety performance, lower uncertainty, and bring Ghana’s nuclear program into line with global best practices. These mechanisms are bolstered by transparent fund governance, robust regulatory oversight, and innovation-driven contracting.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712744','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712744',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','GH;PK','GH','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106546','Divergent and moderating determinants of social and local acceptance of high-level radioactive waste facilities: The role of nuclear power risk perceptions','고준위방사성폐기물 시설의 사회적·지역적 수용성의 상이한 결정요인 및 조절요인: 원자력 위험인식의 역할','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106546','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106546',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
