INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106536','Sensitivity analysis of fast neutron flux calculations for the RPV extended beltline region','원자로압력용기 확장 벨트라인 영역 고속중성자속 계산의 민감도 분석','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106536','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106536',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106555','Site selection procedure in Germany: Considerations on a depth limit for a high-level radioactive waste repository in claystone','독일의 부지선정 절차: 점토암 내 고준위방사성폐기물 처분장의 심도 한계에 대한 고찰','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','The depth of a repository for high-level radioactive waste is an important aspect with respect to both long-term and operational safety. In contrast to the minimum depth, no relevant constraints are given in the German legal regulations for a maximum value. To define such a limit, various safety-related aspects of claystone host rock are considered. This evaluation takes place within an early stage of the German site selection process. The available data are evaluated, and the respective assessments are discussed, ranging from aspects of construction and operation of the repository to its post-closure period. Furthermore, tunneling experience in relevant claystones is evaluated. It is concluded that a favorable depth is neither the maximum depth of existing underground excavations nor the maximum achievable with available techniques. Instead, it is the depth for which experience indicates that under the current assumptions, the extended operation of a nuclear waste repository can be well conducted without jeopardizing operational and long-term safety. The major argument for limiting the repository depth is robustness, which means that the repository as a whole can be operated safely, requires no extraordinary measures like resources, techniques, or time, and can be built with well-established techniques. It can be summarized that those requirements are unlikely to be met for a repository in claystone at depths greater than 1000 m.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106555','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106555',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','DE','DE','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112735','Analysis of the proliferation resistance of re-enriched reprocessed uranium on multiple recycling in nuclear reactors','원자로 내 다중 재활용 시 재농축 재처리우라늄의 핵확산저항성 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112735','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112735',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112727','Central-Difference method based on consistent Half-Node linear approximation for the neutron diffusion equation','중성자 확산방정식을 위한 일관된 반노드 선형근사 기반 중심차분법','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112727','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112727',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112688','Design and analysis of secondary-side passive residual heat removal system to enhance inherent safety of lead-bismuth fast reactor STELLAR-EX','납-비스무트 고속로 STELLAR-EX의 고유안전성 향상을 위한 2차측 피동잔열제거계통 설계 및 해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112688','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112688',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112734','Development of a benchmark experimental method for large angle scattering cross section of 14 MeV neutrons using compound targets – Application to fluorine benchmarking using PTFE','복합 표적을 이용한 14 MeV 중성자 대각도 산란 단면적 벤치마크 실험법 개발 – PTFE를 이용한 불소 벤치마킹 적용','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','In fusion reactors, large angle neutron scattering reactions significantly affect neutronics calculations, especially for the reactor blanket. Previous studies highlighted discrepancies in evaluated nuclear data, emphasizing the necessity for benchmarking large angle scattering cross sections. While the authors’ group previously developed a benchmark experimental system using the foil activation method, gaseous elements like fluorine could not be validated. This study introduces a new method that uses solid compounds containing the gaseous element to indirectly evaluate its large angle scattering cross section. Applying this method, benchmark experiments for fluorine were performed using graphite and polytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE) as the targets, and the fluorine contribution was extracted. The results were then compared with MCNP5 simulations using different nuclear data libraries and an excellent agreement was observed for ENDF/B-VIII.0 and JEFF-3.3. Future work will aim to reduce experimental uncertainties.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112734','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112734',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112698','Effect of burnup-dependent gap conductance on fuel–clad mechanical interaction and PCI risk during transient power excursions','과도 출력 급상승 시 연소도 의존 간극 열전도도가 핵연료-피복관 기계적 상호작용 및 PCI 위험에 미치는 영향','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112698','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112698',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112739','Multiresolution Photon Dose Reconstruction using FLUKA and Resolution-Adaptive Physics-Informed Neural Networks','FLUKA와 해상도 적응형 물리정보신경망을 이용한 다중해상도 광자 선량 재구성','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','AI·디지털','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112739','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112739',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112678','Numerical investigation on flow instability in casing once-through steam generators based on subchannel method','부수로 방법 기반 케이싱형 관류식 증기발생기의 유동 불안정성 수치해석 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112678','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112678',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112732','Seismic fragility analysis of multi-line transmission structure based on gas-insulated switchgear (GIS) equipment for nuclear power applications','원자력 적용을 위한 가스절연개폐장치(GIS) 기반 다회선 송전구조물의 지진 취약도 해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','The stable transmission of nuclear-generated electricity is vital for grid reliability and reactor external power supply. This study addresses this critical need by developing Finite Element Models (FEMs) of Gas-Insulated Switchgear (GIS) and a representative multi-line transmission structure to rigorously assess their seismic vulnerability through dynamic analysis and response evaluation. Based on the practical configurations of key substations system-level seismic fragility curves are constructed by integrating the failure probabilities of individual lines. The results indicate that, under identical structural dimensions, tapered bushings demonstrate superior seismic performance compared to uniform-section bushings. Furthermore, the maximum stress at spherical pipe joints is approximately three times that at right-angle joints, highlighting a critical structural vulnerability. Crucially, while a single transmission line is prone to failure under a given seismic excitation, increasing the number of parallel lines significantly enhances the seismic resilience and operational stability of the overall transmission system.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112732','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112732',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115161','CFD analysis of thermal mixing and stratification phenomena in a tee with a blind-end branch using URANS approach','URANS 접근법을 이용한 막힌 분기관 T자관의 열혼합 및 성층화 현상 CFD 해석','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115161','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115161',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
