                    <sub>2</sub>
                    Glasses for Optical and Radiation Shielding Applications','광학 및 방사선 차폐용 B2O3-TiO2-BaO-ZnO-CeO2 유리의 제조 및 특성 분석','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Aljawhara H. Almuqrin; M. I. Sayyed; Ashok Kumar','2026-09-11','2026-09-11','2026-09-11','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2722502','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2722502',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','SA;AZ;TR;IN','SA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
                    <sub>2</sub>
                    O
                    <sub>3</sub>
                    -Na
                    <sub>2</sub>
                    O-ZnO-CaO-Eu
                    <sub>2</sub>
                    O
                    <sub>3</sub>
                    Glass System Against Ionization Radiation','B2O3-Na2O-ZnO-CaO-Eu2O3 유리계의 전리방사선 차폐 성능','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Albandari W. Alrowaily; Aljawhara H. Almuqrin; M. I. Sayyed; B. Albarzan','2026-09-09','2026-09-09','2026-09-09','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Of utmost importance is the development of transparent, chemically stable, and effective radiation shields against ionizing radiation in terms of safeguarding personnel and machinery. Here we produced various B2O3-Na2O-ZnO-CaO-Eu2O3 glasses via the traditional melt quenching technique. Using Phy-X software, gamma ray attenuation properties were studied between 0.284 and 1.333 MeV energy levels to evaluate the impact of ZnO concentration. In terms of the linear attenuation coefficient value, the glass composed of 55B2O3-5Na2O-19ZnO-20CaO-1Eu2O3 was higher than the other glasses prepared with 0.273 cm−1 at 0.511 MeV and 0.174 cm−1 at 1.275 MeV. The tenth value layer (TVL) was calculated, with the results showing the value decrease by adding ZnO to the glasses, and was in the range of 6.232–7.134 cm at 0.284 MeV and 13.563–15.315 cm at 1.333 MeV. The effective atomic number follows the order Zn10Eu1 < Zn13Eu1 < Zn16Eu1 < Zn19Eu1, suggesting that the glass with 19 and 20 mol% ZnO and CaO respectively have better attenuation performance than the other glasses. Moreover, the results demonstrated that a higher ZnO amount led to increased density, meaning that the thickness needed to attenuate half of the photons is decreased across all energies. The radiation protection efficiency results showed that increased glass thickness has a great improvement on the shielding ability of the material.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2724784','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2724784',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','SA','SA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
                    <sup>226</sup>
                    Ra Sources Owned by the Philippine Nuclear Research Institute','필리핀원자력연구소 보유 노후 226Ra 선원의 소유권 이전 대 계속 저장에 대한 정성적 비용편익 평가','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Ray Matthew A. Bunquin; John Wilkin F. Lim; Angelo A. Panlaqui; Ronald E. Piquero','2026-09-08','2026-09-08','2026-09-08','연구논문','열수력·유체','Legacy 226Ra sealed sources require sustained management because of their high radiotoxicity and very long half-life with decay to 222Rn. This study presents a nonmonetized qualitative cost-benefit analysis comparing two management options for the legacy 226Ra inventory at the Philippine Nuclear Research Institute–Radioactive Waste Management Facility (PNRI-RWMF): (1) transfer of ownership to an organization with recycling capabilities, identified through the International Atomic Energy Agency Global Radium-226 Management Initiative and (2) continued interim storage at PNRI-RWMF.The assessed inventory consists of 22 containers, including 21 cemented drums and 1 container holding encapsulated 226Ra sources. Under the ownership transfer option, PNRI-RWMF personnel would demolish the cemented drums and recover the sources, while the recipient would undertake reconditioning, encapsulation, transport packaging, and shipment.Four PNRI-RWMF personnel directly involved in managing the inventory independently assessed the short- and long-term benefits, costs, and risks using five-point magnitude, consequence, and likelihood scales. Composite indices were presented through heat maps and synthesized using median ratings, ranges, confidence levels, and expert agreement. The ownership transfer option received very high ratings for post-transfer inventory removal, reduction of storage and stewardship burdens, beneficial reuse of 226Ra, and avoidance of intergenerational obligations. However, it also introduced high implementation burdens associated with demolition, source recovery, and secondary radioactive waste management.Continued storage avoided the immediate handling and transport activities but retained high long-term risks related to package deterioration, radon and helium management, surveillance, institutional costs, storage capacity use, and intergenerational responsibility. Overall, ownership transfer provided the more favorable long-term outcome, subject to safe source recovery, regulatory compliance, secondary waste management, and formal acceptance by the recipient.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2724783','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2724783',0,'2026-09-13','2026-09-14','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
CREATE TABLE topics (
  topic_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  topic_ko TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  keywords TEXT NOT NULL,
  active INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1
);
CREATE INDEX idx_papers_journal ON papers(journal);
CREATE INDEX idx_papers_registered ON papers(doi_registered_date);
CREATE INDEX idx_papers_topic ON papers(primary_topic);
COMMIT;
